{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi1v6vRutL7Uy8LyA5g5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018BRYMLW8W2QqRwT7gNG3uG","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-070556__xb697dc/work/PLAN.md","offset":899,"limit":420},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20451,"cache_read_input_tokens":38995,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20451},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49428dbe-779b-4248-8ac3-c582018d3c3d","uuid":"1d35f09e-4f65-48ac-8b47-2c692d2a64ea","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:06:22.436Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi1v6fYkpPZK2F6cZfom","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018BRYMLW8W2QqRwT7gNG3uG":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-070556__xb697dc/work/PLAN.md","offset":899,"limit":420}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018BRYMLW8W2QqRwT7gNG3uG","type":"tool_result","content":"899\t### 10.1 Hot Streak (\"BLAZING!\")\n900\t- **Big plays** are: a TD, a catch of 20+ yd, a run of 15+ yd, a sack, an INT, a forced fumble, and a Big Hit that\n901\t  tackles. Each athlete keeps a heat count. +1 per big play by him. It resets when the opponents make a big play\n902\t  against him (a sack of that QB, a tackle for a loss on that carrier, a pick of that QB) or when they score.\n903\t- At heat 3 he goes **BLAZING** for `T.hotPlays` (6 plays), or until a reset event happens:\n904\t  - unlimited turbo, +12% speed;\n905\t  - offense: tackle p −0.15 against him;\n906\t  - defense: tackle p +0.15, Big Hit fumble ×2;\n907\t  - a QB: aim error ×0.6 and fire-trail passes;\n908\t  - visuals: fire particles at his feet and shoulders (`particles.fire` every 0.05 s, emissive), a flaming ball while\n909\t    he has it, an orange light on him at night;\n910\t  - audio: the music's `hot` layer comes in (`audio.layer('hot', 1, .5)`), the crowd chants, the announcer's\n911\t    `hotStreakOn` lines.\n912\t- A team can have 2 blazing athletes. The HUD shows a flame icon by his name and a heat pip count (1–3) on held\n913\t  athletes' tags.\n914\t\n915\t### 10.2 The Fiasco Meter and the Fiasco Cards (the items)\n916\t**The Fiasco Meter** is the title's mechanic: every disaster is an opportunity. Each team's meter (0–100) fills when\n917\tthings go wrong for it:\n918\t\n919\t| Event | Fill |\n920\t|---|---|\n921\t| fumble lost | 35 |\n922\t| INT thrown | 35 |\n923\t| safety allowed | 40 |\n924\t| sacked | 20 |\n925\t| turnover on downs | 25 |\n926\t| opponent's TD | 20 |\n927\t| dropped pass | 10 |\n928\t| Big Hit received | 10 |\n929\t| late hit received | 5 |\n930\t\n931\tWhen it fills, the team **draws a Fiasco Card** at random from its pool (story: the cards you've unlocked;\n932\texhibition: all 8), up to 3 held. Then the meter resets. A HUD flourish plays: a card flips in, \"FIASCO BREAK!\".\n933\tEach team also starts a game with cards: story, a loadout of up to 3 picked on the chapter screen; exhibition, 1\n934\trandom card each; hub rounds, 1 each, dealt from `AIHub.rng('cards')`.\n935\t\n936\t**Using a card:** on the play-call screen press b4 (△) to open the card row and pick one (or click a slot). One card\n937\tper play. A card on offense needs an offensive card and so on; a card that doesn't fit the side is greyed out. Its\n938\teffect lasts as its text says. Cards are data: `{ id, name, side: 'off' | 'def' | 'any' | 'kick', text, art,\n939\tapply(ctx) }`. `apply` registers bus modifiers for the play or for N plays. The CPU trigger is in §8.5.\n940\t\n941\t| Card | Side | Effect | CPU uses it when |\n942\t|---|---|---|---|\n943\t| ROCKET CLEATS | off | your carrier and receivers +20% speed this play | 3rd & 10+, or trailing in the last 2:00 |\n944\t| GLUE GLOVES | off | your receivers can't drop the ball; contested catches +30% this play | a pass play on 3rd or 4th down |\n945\t| BRICK WALL | off | your blockers can't be shed for 3.5 s | a pass play on 3rd & long |\n946\t| HOT SAUCE | any | the held athlete (CPU: its best player) goes BLAZING for 3 plays | first chance in the 2nd half |\n947\t| MEGA HIT | def | this play's first tackle is a Mega Hit: launch × 1.6, fumble chance 60%, the slow-mo cam | 3rd down defense, or the opponent in the red zone |\n948\t| BUTTERFINGERS | def | opposing receivers' catch chance −35% this play | 3rd & long defense |\n949\t| MASCOT MAYHEM | any | your mascot runs on as a 12th player for the play: he blocks the nearest defender on offense, rushes the passer on defense, with `noClip` through blockers. The announcers lose their minds. | trailing by 7+ |\n950\t| SUPER FOOT | kick | the next kick: +15 yd, an accuracy band ×2.5, the power needle ×0.7 speed | a FG of 45+ yd, or a PAT in the last minute |\n951\t\n952\t### 10.3 Big Hits, Mega Hits, Dinged and the flying helmet\n953\t- **Big Hit:** turbo + b1 (§7.4–7.5). Hit-stop 0.08 s, `game.shake(4)`, `game.hitFx` with an impact star, grass, mud\n954\t  or snow bits, a camera punch-in to 1.25× for 0.35 s, slow motion (`timeScale` 0.4 for 0.3 s, honoring reduce\n955\t  motion), a comic \"BOOM!\" / \"WHAM!\" / \"KER-RUNCH!\" burst over the hit, and the crowd \"OOOOH\".\n956\t- **Mega Hit** (the card, or a 1-in-6 roll of a Blazing Big Hit): launch × 1.6, the victim spins in the air (PoseFX\n957\t  spin), hit-stop 0.12, the slow-mo cam (`timeScale` 0.25 for 0.6 s), a white flash (`game.flash`, honoring the\n958\t  flashes setting).\n959\t- **Dinged:** the victim of a Mega Hit, or of 2 Big Hits in one drive, is Dinged for 2 plays: −10% speed and little\n960\t  cartoon stars orbiting his helmet (3 tiny glints circling, emissive).\n961\t- **The flying helmet:** on a Mega Hit (and 25% of Big Hits) the victim's helmet pops off as a separate bouncing\n962\t  prop: a shape `helmet` in team colors, an `E.Body` with bounce 0.5. His hair shows until the next PRESNAP, when he\n963\t  picks it up (cosmetic). The announcer says \"HIS HELMET IS IN A DIFFERENT AREA CODE!\"\n964\t\n965\t### 10.4 Late hits\n966\tAfter the whistle, for 1.2 s, b1 near an opponent does a late hit (cosmetic knockdown). The refs throw their caps\n967\t(Fiasco rules: no flags). A crowd reaction, the announcer's outrage lines, a stat. AI athletes late-hit too, by team\n968\tpersonality (the Mudhogs often, the Dynasty sneakily).\n969\t\n970\t### 10.5 Boss specials (story bosses; also in exhibition)\n971\tEach special is used by the AI, or by a human holding that star (in exhibition or a hub round), who presses **lb and\n972\trb together** (L1 + R1, LB + RB, Q + E) within 0.1 s while its conditions hold. A single shoulder press waits those\n973\t0.1 s before it becomes a lateral, so the chord never laterals by accident. For the Golden Spiral, press the chord,\n974\tthen a receiver button within 1 s. A badge shows \"SPECIAL READY\" on the star's tag. NIGHT VISION is passive.\n975\t\n976\t| Star | Special | Rules |\n977\t|---|---|---|\n978\t| BIG BERTHA BOUDREAUX (Mudhogs RB #44) | **MUDSLIDE** | once per drive: for 1.2 s she lowers her shoulder; the first tackler in front is bowled over (down 1.2 s) unless it's a Big Hit from the front; mud spray FX |\n979\t| LUMEN LOPEZ (Owls QB #1) | **NIGHT VISION** | always on: his reads see 1 extra yard of openness, and his aim error ×0.8 |\n980\t| ZAP ZAPATA (Owls WR #11) | **AFTERBURNER** | once per play: a 1.0 s burst at ×1.35 speed that leaves neon light trails (`ghost` afterimages in cyan) |\n981\t| AVALANCHE (Yetis DE #99) | **SNOWPLOW** | once per drive: his engagement drives the blocker straight back at 3× push for 1.5 s; a snow spray |\n982\t| BROCK STERLING III (Dynasty QB #12) | **GOLDEN SPIRAL** | once per drive: a perfect pass, no aim error, it can't be intercepted (defenders may still deflect it with 0.15), gold sparkle trail |\n983\t| THE MOUNTAIN, MALU FALEOLO (Dynasty LB #55) | **SEISMIC SACK** | once per half, when within 3 yd of the carrier: he leaps (0.6 s) and slams down; everyone within 2.5 yd is knocked down; a shockwave ring (`particles.ring`), shake 7, \"SEISMIC!\" |\n984\tThe commentary has lines for each, and the HUD shows a banner with the star's portrait for 1.2 s when one fires.\n985\t\n986\t### 10.6 Celebrations\n987\tAfter a TD the scorer celebrates. Locally the scorer's human picks one: b2 the Charleston, b3 the Body Roll, b4 the\n988\tHelicopter (breakdance). Otherwise it's random by personality, from the list below. In hub sessions it's always\n989\trandom (no player-triggered emotes, §16.6).\n990\t\n991\t| Celebration | How it's animated |\n992\t|---|---|\n993\t| Spike | a throw-down attack spec, the ball bounces high |\n994\t| Charleston, Body Roll | mocap `Dance Charleston` / `Dance Body Roll` |\n995\t| Helicopter | mocap `Breakdance_Helicopter` |\n996\t| Backflip | mocap `Backflip` |\n997\t| Fist pump | mocap `Victory Fist Pump` |\n998\t| Stands Dive | he leaps into the end zone stands: `body.jump`, the crowd lifts him, bodies bob |\n999\t| Group Huddle Dance | 3 nearest teammates do `Dance_Loop` in a ring |\n1000\t\n1001\tTeammates near him do `Cheering_Two_Hands`. Defenders kneel (`pose: 'kneel'`) or put their hands on their helmets\n1002\t(PoseFX). Pyro cannons fire, confetti falls (`particles.bits` in team colors from z 160), the crowd goes wild.\n1003\t\n1004\t### 10.7 Mascots\n1005\tEach team has a mascot on the near sideline: a Humanoid in team colors with a big costume head drawn by the gear\n1006\thook (§12.2). They react: dance on scores, slump on turnovers, and do a backflip on a Big Hit. They flip the coin, and\n1007\trun on with Mascot Mayhem (`noClip`, a cartoon dust cloud, a squeaky sfx). Fumbles the Flaming Tumbleweed sets\n1008\thimself on fire when the Fiascos score (fire particles), and trips over the power cable in chapter 3 (§15.1).\n1009\t\n1010\t### 10.8 Refs\n1011\tTwo refs on the field (an umpire 6 yd behind the defense, a back judge 20 yd deep) and a line judge on the near\n1012\tsideline. They're cosmetic Humanoids in striped shirts (the gear hook draws the stripes), with poses for signals:\n1013\tTOUCHDOWN (both arms up), FIRST DOWN (an arm pointing at the offense's goal), INCOMPLETE (arms crossing, a wave),\n1014\tFUMBLE / POSSESSION (pointing), and \"Sure, why not\" (a shrug) after a late hit. A play running through a ref knocks\n1015\thim over comically (the announcer: \"AND THE REF GOES DOWN! HE'S FINE! HE'S... MOSTLY FINE!\").\n1016\t\n1017\t### 10.9 LIGHTS OUT (chapter 3's event; also a Dev toggle)\n1018\tFor 3 plays: `lights.ambient` 0.12, `darkness` 0.9, the light towers off. Every uniform's trim, the Owls' neon, the\n1019\tball, the yard lines and the Fiascos' glow paint (their trim turns `#7aff6a` with glow) stay bright as emissive (the\n1020\tgear hook draws trims with `px.glow` and queues them `emissive: true`). Camera flashes in the crowd sparkle.\n1021\tCommentary and the crowd play along, then the lights come back with a thunk and a flicker.\n1022\t\n1023\t---\n1024\t\n1025\t## 11. Presentation\n1026\t\n1027\t### 11.1 The camera director (`37-camera.js`)\n1028\tOur own smoothing (`E.smoothDamp` on x, y and zoom), `game.focus(x, y, z)` every update, `game.setZoom(z)`, and\n1029\t`cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v)`. The player's own zoom (wheel, `-` `=`) multiplies ours.\n1030\t\n1031\t| Shot | When | Focus and zoom |\n1032\t|---|---|---|\n1033\t| PRESNAP | the formation | x = LOS + dir × 5 yd; y = the ball's y × 0.6 + MID_Y × 0.4; zoom 1.0 |\n1034\t| RUN | a carrier | the carrier + v × `T.camLead` (0.35 s); zoom 1.05 |\n1035\t| PASS_PRE | QB with the ball on a pass play | `cam.frame([qb, ...receivers within 30 yd], { margin: 40, zoom: [.62, 1] })` |\n1036\t| BALL_AIR | a pass in the air | between the ball's ground point and its landing point, zoomed to fit both (min .62) |\n1037\t| KICK | kickoffs and punts | follow the ball, zoom .75; on the catch, RUN on the returner |\n1038\t| KICKCAM | FG and PAT | cut (`{ fade: 0 }` style, 0.15 s dissolve) to the `kickcam` view behind the kicker; follow the ball to the posts; hold 1.2 s on the result; cut back |\n1039\t| PUNCH | a Big Hit or Mega Hit | zoom × 1.25 over 0.12 s, hold 0.25 s, ease back over 0.4 s |\n1040\t| CELEBRATE | after a TD | the scorer, zoom 1.35 |\n1041\t| CUTAWAY | after the celebration (50% of TDs) | pan up to the stands at the end zone for 1.2 s, zoom 1.2: \"the crowd goes wild\" |\n1042\t| REPLAY | §11.2 | `field`, `iso`, `reverse` views at 0.5× and 0.35× |\n1043\t| CUTSCENE | §15.1 | scripted tweens (`game.tween` on a camera target object) |\n1044\tViews are fixed per shot. Never animate the yaw continuously: each new yaw rebakes the floor.\n1045\t\n1046\t### 11.2 Instant replay and the highlight reel (`38-replay.js`)\n1047\t- **Recording:** from the snap to 1 s after the whistle, at 60 Hz (every 2nd step), record a frame per entity:\n1048\t  athletes `[x, y, z, facing, poseCode, poseU, flags]` (flags: carrying, hot, dinged, helmet off), the ball\n1049\t  `[x, y, z, state, spin]`, refs and the mascot. Record presentation events with their time: hit FX, particles\n1050\t  bursts, comic pops, sfx names, card banners. A 12 s ring buffer in `Float32Array`s.\n1051\t- **Playback** is a REPLAY sub-state of the match scene. The sim is frozen and untouched. Rigs are driven from the\n1052\t  frames (positions interpolated, velocity derived for the gait), the recorded events re-fire at their times, and\n1053\t  the audio plays the sfx (the commentary doesn't repeat; the crowd bed stays). Shots: 1) the `field` view following\n1054\t  the ball at 0.5× over the 3 s around the key moment; 2) the `iso` or `reverse` view at 0.35× for the impact. Then\n1055\t  back to the live view.\n1056\t- **The overlay:** a REPLAY badge with a blinking red dot, a VCR timecode, letterbox bars, \"✕ SKIP\" (b1 or a click\n1057\t  skips). The music ducks.\n1058\t- **Triggers:** a TD (when Replays is All big plays or Touchdowns only), a turnover, a Mega Hit, a Big Hit fumble, a\n1059\t  play of 40+ yd, a FG of 50+ yd, a Seismic Sack, a Mascot Mayhem play. Setting: Replays: All big plays (default) /\n1060\t  Touchdowns only / Off. In hub sessions: off.\n1061\t- **Highlight reel:** the 5 most exciting clips of the game, by an excitement score (event priority × yards), are\n1062\t  kept (8 s each). The results screen offers WATCH HIGHLIGHTS, which plays them back to back with captions\n1063\t  (\"Q2 3:12 — DOC DOBSON 48-YD TD RUN\").\n1064\t- **Invariant (tested):** the sim's state hash is the same before and after a replay.\n1065\t\n1066\t### 11.3 Commentary and on-field text (`39-commentary.js`)\n1067\t- **Two announcers:** CHET THUNDERBUNS (play-by-play: loud, excitable) and LOU \"THE TOE\" DIGGS (color: an ex-kicker,\n1068\t  folksy, deadpan).\n1069\t- **Events** have priorities (Appendix D): TD 10, turnover 9, Mega Hit 9, special 8, Big Hit 8, sack 8, long play 7,\n1070\t  Hot Streak 7, mascot 7, FG result 7, late hit 6, card 6, drop 5, first down 4, incomplete 3, weather 2, idle\n1071\t  chatter 1.\n1072\t- **Rules:** at most one line per 2.5 s. A higher priority interrupts a lower one. On events of priority ≥ 7, CHET\n1073\t  speaks and LOU answers 1.2 s later with chance 0.4. No line repeats within the last 8 for that event. Lines take\n1074\t  variables (`{player}`, `{team}`, `{opp}`, `{yards}`, `{score}`).\n1075\t- **The caption:** a non-modal box at the bottom left (keep clear of the prompt strip and the score bug). The\n1076\t  speaker's portrait (`rig.drawPortrait` of the announcer rig: a headset and a blazer) and name, the text typed at\n1077\t  45 chars/s with the babble voice (§13.4). It hides after its length / 15 + 1.5 s. The Commentary setting: On /\n1078\t  Subtitles only (no voice) / Off.\n1079\t- **On-field pops:** comic bursts in world space over the event: BOOM!, WHAM!, KER-RUNCH!, SACKED!, PICKED OFF!,\n1080\t  FUMBLE!, PANCAKE!, BROKEN TACKLE!, DOINK!, BLAZING!, FIASCO BREAK!, SEISMIC!, DROPPED!. `E.font.title` with an\n1081\t  outline over a jagged polygon burst (`px.poly`, 12 points with radii alternating 1 and 0.6). It scales from 0.4 to\n1082\t  1.1 to 1.0 (`outBack`) and lasts 0.9 s. Anchor it with `r.w(x, y, z + 40)`.\n1083\t- **Center text** for game events: TOUCHDOWN! (title scale 4 in the scoring team's colors with a shine sweep), FIRST\n1084\t  DOWN!, TURNOVER!, SAFETY!, IT'S GOOD! / NO GOOD!, TOUCHBACK, 4TH DOWN, RED ZONE, TWO-MINUTE WARNING (if quarters\n1085\t  are 2:00 or longer), LIGHTS OUT!\n1086\t\n1087\t### 11.4 The crowd (`26-crowd.js`)\n1088\t- **Fans** sit on the stand tiers: 2–3 per tile per tier (about 2,400 at the Mega Dome). Each is drawn like the SPORTS\n1089\t  kit's fans (`r.queue` with 2–3 `px.rect`s: shirt, head, an optional hat), with the team colors by section (home\n1090\t  sections, plus an away section by one end zone), and skin and hat variety from a seeded hash. 8% hold signs: a\n1091\t  6×4 rectangle with a tiny-font word (\"FIASCO!\", \"D!\", \"HOGS!\", \"HOOT!\", \"BRRR!\", \"$$$\"). 5% have foam fingers.\n1092\t- **Excitement E** (0–1): big events set it up, `T.crowdDecay` (0.15/s) brings it down. Above 0.6 the fans stand and\n1093\t  bob. On a TD the scoring side's fans jump (+5 z). Below 0.2 they sway.\n1094\t- **The Wave** rolls around the stands every 40–70 s when E is moderate and the home team leads: a sine wave of\n1095\t  stand-ups moving 10 tiles/s.\n1096\t- **Density** by stadium. Tumbleweed Field is 35% full until the story's ending, when it's 100%.\n1097\t- **Camera flashes** at night: random 1-px white dots with tiny lights, more on big plays.\n1098\t- **Audio:** the crowd bed and reactions (§13.3).\n1099\t\n1100\t### 11.5 FX (`40-fx.js`)\n1101\t- **Hits:** `game.hitFx(x, y, z, { power, angle })` with no damage number (leave `damage` out and check that none\n1102\t  shows), `particles.impact`, surface bits (grass `#4a8a3a`/`#2e5a22`, mud `#5a3a1a`, snow `#f0f4ff`), dust, and white\n1103\t  `particles.sparks` on helmet-to-helmet hits.\n1104\t- **Divots:** on Big Hits and dives, a persistent decal of torn turf at the spot, up to 40 per game (the oldest fade).\n1105\t- **Footprints** in snow and mud: small decals behind runners every 0.15 s, fading over 6 s, up to 200.\n1106\t- **Breath puffs** at Frostbite: `particles.smoke` at each head every 1.2 s, on the cosmetic RNG stream.\n1107\t- **Weather:** `game.weather = { kind: 'rain', amount: .6, wind: .2, lightning: .1 }` at the Hog Wallow;\n1108\t  `{ kind: 'snow', amount: .7, wind: .3 }` at Frostbite; set in the match's `enter` (weather ends with the scene).\n1109\t- **Celebrations:** confetti (`particles.bits` in team colors from z 160), fireworks in the sky\n1110\t  (`particles.explosion(..., { debris: false, shake: 0 })` and colored rings at z 300+ over the end zone), pyro columns\n1111\t  from the cannons (`particles.fire` + a light), streamers.\n1112\t- **Trails:** a Hot Streak's fire on the ball and athlete, Afterburner's neon ghosts (`r.actor(..., { ghost })`), the\n1113\t  Golden Spiral's gold glints.\n1114\t- **Lights** (`game.lights.enabled = true` in every stadium):\n1115\t  - Tumbleweed: dusk, `ambient` 0.62 warm, a low sun light from the west, string lights over the bleachers.\n1116\t  - Hog Wallow: overcast, 0.55, lightning flashes from the weather.\n1117\t  - Afterglow: night, 0.35, 4 light towers (radius 420, intensity 0.9) and colored neon lights.\n1118\t  - Frostbite: 0.5, the northern lights tint the sky, towers.\n1119\t  - Mega Dome: indoor 0.55, 6 spotlights sweeping on tweens, pyro lights.\n1120\t  - Try GPU lighting (`game.enableGPU({ map })`, ground views) for soft shadows from the stands. The canvas fallback\n1121\t    must look right too: set both ambients.\n1122\t- **Shadows:** `r.shadow` under every athlete, and under the ball with a radius and alpha that shrink with its\n1123\t  height. The ball's shadow is how players read a lob.\n1124\t\n1125\t---\n1126\t\n1127\t## 12. Art and animation\n1128\t\n1129\t### 12.1 The look target (from API.md: use every step)\n1130\t`res: 'ps1'` with `expand: true` (480×270 at 1080p, 427×240 at 1440p and 4K). Dressed HD characters 40–60 px tall\n1131\t(sizes 1.2–1.45; bosses 1.6–1.8). A backdrop behind the stands. A textured field and stands. 3–8 props on screen.\n1132\tEffects on every hit. Colors shaded with `E.tones`. Titles with `E.font.title`. Lights in every scene. Portraits in\n1133\tevery dialog. Compare screenshots with Metal Slug and Symphony of the Night, not NES games. `node tools/check.mjs`\n1134\tgives look notes: act on every one.\n1135\t\n1136\t### 12.2 Characters (`27-rigs.js`)\n1137\t**Rig recipes by position** (`new E.Humanoid({...})`, `weapon: null`, `sleeves: 'short'`, `outfit: 'shirt'`,\n1138\t`hat: { style: 'football', color, stripe, logo }` (E4)):\n1139\t\n1140\t| Position | build | size | Notes |\n1141\t|---|---|---|---|\n1142\t| OL, DL | bulky | 1.38–1.48 | `shoulderHalf` +0.6, `torsoW` +0.6, a lean of 0.1 |\n1143\t| LB | bulky or heroic | 1.3 | |\n1144\t| RB | heroic | 1.22 | stocky: `limbW` +0.3 |\n1145\t| WR, CB, S | heroic | 1.2 | lean: `limbW` −0.2 |\n1146\t| QB | heroic | 1.25 | |\n1147\t| K | heroic | 1.02 | the tiny kicker (a joke the announcer makes) |\n1148\t| Bosses: Bertha 1.6, The Mountain 1.7, Avalanche 1.8 | bulky | | Avalanche has a beard (gear hook) and `eyeGlow` off |\n1149\t| Refs | heroic | 1.15 | a cap (`hat: 'cap'`, white); stripes from the gear hook |\n1150\t| Coaches | bulky or heroic | 1.2 | a cap and a headset (gear hook), a polo |\n1151\t| Cheerleaders | heroic | 1.1 | `hair: 'ponytail'`, pom-poms (gear hook) |\n1152\t| Mascots | bulky | 1.3 | a costume head (gear hook), team colors |\n1153\t| Announcers (portraits only) | heroic | 1.2 | a headset, a blazer (`outfit: 'coat'`) |\n1154\t| Story cast (Mama Pearl, Sterling, ...) | per character | 1.2 | §18.1 |\n1155\t\n1156\t**The uniform from team colors:** `colors.cloth` is the jersey, `trim` the jersey trim (sleeve bands), `pants`,\n1157\t`belt`, `boot` the cleats, `glove` the gloves, the hat color the helmet. Away teams wear white jerseys with\n1158\tteam-color trim, and home teams wear their color. Skin tones (`#f0c8a8 #e0b090 #c89070 #a87050 #6a4028 #4a2c18`) and\n1159\thair styles vary per player (data). Faces show: `face: { eyes: 'big' }` on story cast, default on athletes, and eye\n1160\tblack on athletes (gear hook).\n1161\t\n1162\t**The gear hook (E3)** draws, depth-sorted inside the rig:\n1163\t- **Shoulder pads:** a wide disc over each shoulder joint in the jersey color, with a darker rim. They sit over the\n1164\t  torso, so the silhouette reads as football at a glance.\n1165\t- **The jersey number:** 3×5 digits (`font: 'tiny'`, scale by `u`) in the trim color, on the chest when the torso\n1166\t  faces the camera (`dot(facing, view.fx/fy) > .3`), on the back when it faces away (< −.3), hidden edge-on. Placed at\n1167\t  `Sp(J.shC, ±torsoDepth, 0, -3)`.\n1168\t- **The carried ball:** at the carrying hand, a brown ellipse with white laces (below), at the hand's depth + 0.02.\n1169\t  The sim sets `rig.carry = 'R' | 'L' | null`.\n1170\t- **Eye black,** a headset on coaches, pom-poms on cheerleaders (discs at the hands, team colors), ref stripes (black\n1171\t  vertical lines over the torso).\n1172\t- **Mascot heads:** a big disc 2.2× the head with features. Fumbles is a twig ball (brown line scribbles) with googly\n1173\t  eyes. Hambone is a pink hog with a snout and ears. Hooty is an owl with neon eyes (glow). Abominable Al is a white\n1174\t  fur ball with horns. Goldie is a gold lion with a mane.\n1175\t- **Big Heads cheat:** `rig.o.headR × 1.9` live. Check it re-solves; if not, rebuild the rigs.\n1176\t- **The Fiascos' glow paint** in LIGHTS OUT: the trims drawn with `px.glow(g, 1)` and an emissive queue.\n1177\t\n1178\t### 12.3 Pose codes to animation (`FF.Rigs.drive(rig, athlete, dt)`)\n1179\tThe sim sets `pose` and `poseU` (Appendix C). The presentation maps each to rig inputs, from four sources: the\n1180\tengine's procedural rig (velocity gait, `pose`, `expr`, `air`, `down`, `stance`, `run`, `flip`, `land`), `E.MOVES`\n1181\tand attack specs, mocap clips (§12.4), and PoseFX (§12.5).\n1182\t\n1183\t| Pose | Drive |\n1184\t|---|---|\n1185\t| IDLE, RUN | `rig.update(dt, { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing })`, the velocity gait; `sprint: true` with turbo |\n1186\t| STANCE3 (linemen) | mocap `Land_Three_Point` held at its last key (a hand on the ground), `mocapW` 1 |\n1187\t| STANCE2 (LB, WR, DB) | `pose: 'crouch'` blended 0.5, a lean of 0.25 |\n1188\t| QB_UC / QB_SG | `pose: 'crouch'` 0.35 with the hands forward (an attack spec held), or upright with the hands at the chest |\n1189\t| SNAP | a two-handed spec from low forward to between the legs, 0.25 s |\n1190\t| DROPBACK | the gait backward (verify the backpedal in a filmstrip; if it looks wrong, turn `facing` 25° off the motion) |\n1191\t| THROW | mocap `OverhandThrow`, `mocapMask: 'upper'` while moving (throwing on the run), time-scaled so the release lands on the sim's release frame |\n1192\t| HANDOFF give / take | specs: the arm extends / both arms form a pocket |\n1193\t| CARRY | the gait plus PoseFX `tuck` (the carrying hand to the chest side, the elbow in) |\n1194\t| CATCH_READY, CATCH | a two-handed spec reaching to the ball's height (`z1` from the arrival height); `air: true` with a jump |\n1195\t| DIVE, TACKLE_DIVE | PoseFX `tilt` forward 0→75° over 0.15 s, the arms forward (a two-handed `thrust`), `air: true`; on landing `down: 1` |\n1196\t| SPIN | the `facing` passed to `rig.update` turned through a full circle over the action (`facing + 2π·u`, eased); don't write `rig.spin` (the rig's own field for attack spins) |\n1197\t| STIFFARM | the `jab` move with the free hand, held 70% of the action |\n1198\t| HURDLE | mocap `Run_Jump_Over`, time-scaled to the jump |\n1199\t| BLOCK | mocap `Push_Loop` (`mocapMask: 'upper'`) + a lean of 0.2; feet from the gait |\n1200\t| SHED / SWIM | `E.MOVES.hook` (an arm over) |\n1201\t| BIGHIT | `E.MOVES.bash` + PoseFX `tilt` 25° |\n1202\t| TACKLED | mocap `Fall_On_Face` (tackled from behind) or `Hit_Knockback` (from the front), then DOWN |\n1203\t| FLY (a Big Hit victim) | PoseFX `tilt` back 70° + `roll` spin (Mega Hit), `air: true`, then DOWN |\n1204\t| DOWN | `down: 1` |\n1205\t| GETUP | mocap `Get_Up_Face_Down` or `Get_Up_From_Back`, by how he fell |\n1206\t| PILE | `down: 1` + PoseFX random `tilt`/`roll` and a z offset (stacked) |\n1207\t| KICK | `E.MOVES.kick` after a 3-step run-up |\n1208\t| HOLD | `pose: 'kneel'` + a hand low forward |\n1209\t| CELEBRATE(k) | §10.6 |\n1210\t| CHEER | mocap `Cheering_Two_Hands` (teammates), `pose: 'cheer'` (refs and coaches) |\n1211\t| DEJECTED | `pose: 'kneel'`, or PoseFX `handsOnHelmet` |\n1212\t| REF_TD, REF_FD, REF_INC, REF_SHRUG | specs: both arms up, an arm pointing, arms crossing back and forth, a shrug |\n1213\t| CHEERLEADER | mocap `Jumping Jacks` and `Cheering_Two_Hands`, alternating |\n1214\t| COACH_YELL | `expr: 'shout'`, `pose: 'hips'`, the headset |\n1215\tFaces act: `expr: 'shout'` on hits and celebrations, `'wince'` when hurt, `'smile'` when Blazing. Enemy specials\n1216\ttelegraph with a 0.25–0.35 s wind-up and a flash.\n1217\t\n1218\t### 12.4 Motion clips (the FIASCO set)\n1219\tCut once, from the engine repository (§3.2):\n1220\t```sh\n1221\tnode .cache/engine/tools/anim-set.mjs .cache/engine/src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js .cache/engine/src/mocap/sets/mesh2motion.js \\\n1222\t  .cache/engine/src/mocap/sets/cmu.js \\\n1223\t  --clips \"QUATERNIUS:OverhandThrow,QUATERNIUS:Push_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Dance_Loop,Dance Charleston,Dance Body Roll,Victory Fist Pump,Cheering_Two_Hands,Breakdance_Helicopter,Run_Jump_Over,Dive_Roll,Fall_On_Face,Get_Up_Face_Down,Get_Up_From_Back,QUATERNIUS:Hit_Knockback,MESH2MOTION:Land_Three_Point,Jumping Jacks,Front_Kick,MESH2MOTION:Backflip\" \\\n1224\t  --name FIASCO --credit \"Quaternius (CC0), Mesh2Motion (CC0), CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database (free for all uses)\" \\\n1225\t  --out vendor/anim/fiasco-anim.js\n1226\t```\n1227\tThis was run during planning. It writes 18 clips, 736 key poses, 222 KB. In the set the clips are named without the\n1228\t`SET:` prefix (`lib.clip('OverhandThrow')`). A headless probe confirmed that each drives an HD Humanoid (bulky, 1.3) on\n1229\tthe handoff engine: `Land_Three_Point` ends with the hand at z ≈ 1 (a three-point stance), and `OverhandThrow` raises\n1230\tthe hand to z ≈ 28 and comes through. Use:\n1231\t```js\n1232\tconst lib = Mocap.load(window.MOCAP.FIASCO);  Mocap.drive(rig, lib);           // once per rig\n1233\trig.mocap = lib.sample(lib.clip('OverhandThrow'), t); rig.mocapW = w; rig.mocapMask = 'upper';  // each step, before rig.update\n1234\t```\n1235\tFade clips in and out with `mocapW` over 0.1 s. Never snap.\n1236\t\n1237\t### 12.5 PoseFX (new animation by joint post-processing)\n1238\tWrap each athlete rig's `solvePose` (the API allows it): call the original, then apply the active transforms to\n1239\t`rig.J` (all joints are in the rig's own frame: forward, right, up):\n1240\t- `tilt(angle)` rotates every joint about the hip center around the right axis (forward dives, backward falls).\n1241\t- `roll(angle)` rotates about the forward axis.\n1242\t- `lift(dz)` raises everything.\n1243\t- `tuck(side)` moves the hand and elbow of that side to fixed points by the chest (ball security).\n1244\t- `handsOnHelmet` puts both hands at the head's sides.\n1245\tTransforms blend with weights so they ease in and out. This is how Emberdeep makes its dodge roll (AI_GUIDE, Building\n1246\ta big game).\n1247\t\n1248\t### 12.6 New shapes (`24-shapes.js`) and store props\n1249\tWrite these as `E.SHAPES` entries (docs/ASSETS.md format; 16 units = 1 m; face south). Look at each with\n1250\t`node .cache/engine/dist/handoff/tools/asset-sheet.mjs $PWD/src/24-shapes.js#<id>` and fix its lint notes:\n1251\t`pylon` (orange foam 2×2×7), `cone` (an orange traffic cone on a base), `dummy` (a red tackling dummy, r 4, h 22),\n1252\t`sled` (a blocking sled with two pads), `cooler` (an orange sports-drink cooler with a white lid and spigot), `cups`\n1253\t(a stacked paper cup tower), `teamBench` (a long bench, `params: { len }`, a team-color material slot), `lightTower` (a\n1254\tlattice tower h 200, a lamp bank in a glow material, `lights`), `oldScoreboard` (Tumbleweed's hand-flipped board;\n1255\tdigits drawn by code), `jumbotron` (a big dark screen on a pylon; the content drawn by code into its projected quad:\n1256\tthe score and \"MAKE SOME NOISE!\"), `downMarker` (an orange pole with a flip card; the down drawn by code),\n1257\t`chainPole`, `tvCamera` (a camera on a tripod), `podium`, `micStand`, `locker` (a metal locker 10×6×30 with vents and a\n1258\tteam-color door), `chalkboard` (on an easel; X's and O's by code), `trophy` (the Fiasco Cup: a gold lathe cup with\n1259\thandles and a football on top), `pickupTruck`, `waterTower` (\"TUMBLEWEED JCT\" by code), `airboat`, `neonSign` (glow\n1260\tletters by code), `snowbank` (snowy rock lumps), `pyroCannon`, `blimp` (a flattened ball with fins, drawn at z 300+),\n1261\t`stage` (a ceremony stage with bunting), `cake` (a tiered victory cake), `bulldozer` (yellow, blade, tracks),\n1262\t`goldCart` (a gold golf cart), `grill` (a tailgate grill; smoke from particles), `helmet` (a loose football helmet:\n1263\ta shell ball and facemask bars, mats per team), `inflatableHelmet` (the giant team-entrance tunnel helmet), `bassDrum`\n1264\t(held by band members through the gear hook).\n1265\t\n1266\tFrom the core library, no store needed: `bench`, `table`, `barrel`, `crate`, `lamppost`, `fence`, `pine`, `tree`,\n1267\t`bush`, `grass`, `rock`. `r.prop` built-ins: `banner`, `sign`, `lamp`, `streetlamp`, `awning`, `cactus`, `palm`,\n1268\t`lantern`, `trashcan`, `firedrum`, `vines`. Cut the few store entries into one set:\n1269\t```sh\n1270\tS=.cache/engine/dist/handoff/src/assets/sets\n1271\tnode .cache/engine/dist/handoff/tools/asset-set.mjs $S/kenney-survival.js $S/kenney-graveyard.js $S/kenney-pirate.js $S/kenney-nature.js $S/kenney-furniture.js \\\n1272\t  --ids kenney-survival:bucket,kenney-graveyard:hay-bale,kenney-pirate:flag,kenney-nature:tent-small-closed,kenney-furniture:speaker \\\n1273\t  --name fiasco-store --out vendor/assets/fiasco-store.js\n1274\t```\n1275\tThis was run during planning: 5 shapes, 10 materials, 1,799 tokens. Load it with\n1276\t`E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['fiasco-store'])`, which names the entries `fiasco-store:<id>`. The bucket is the sports-drink bucket dump. Use\n1277\t`asset-find.mjs` for anything else. The store sets are CC0: credit Kenney on the About screen.\n1278\t\n1279\t### 12.7 The football\n1280\tDrawn in `r.queue` at the ball's world position, or by the gear hook while carried. It is a prolate ellipse (a\n1281\t10-point polygon), 7×4 px at zoom 1, brown `#8a4a22` with an `E.tones` shade and highlight, a white lace stripe of 3\n1282\tstitches, and a white band at each tip. Its long axis follows the projected velocity\n1283\t(`r.w(p)` → `r.w(p + v·dt)`). In flight it spins: alternate the lace position each 1/30 s so it reads as a spiral.\n1284\tKicks tumble end over end (the axis rotates in screen space at 10 rad/s). Shadow below. A flame trail when Blazing, a\n1285\tgold trail on the Golden Spiral, white speed lines on Rocket Passes.\n1286\t\n1287\t### 12.8 Logos, field art and UI art\n1288\t- **Team logos** are string sprites (`E.sprite`), 16×16, with a 4–6 color palette per team: a flaming tumbleweed, a\n1289\t  hog head with tusks, neon owl eyes, a yeti footprint, a crown on a football, and a grey \"P\" on a whistle for the\n1290\t  Scrubs. Use them on the score bug (×1), menus (×3), the helmet ear dot (a 1–2 px dot of the main color), the\n1291\t  midfield paint (sampled as a bitmap at 1 sprite px = 0.5 yd) and the end-zone walls.\n1292\t- **The title logo:** `AMERICAN FOOTBALL` in `E.font.title` scale 3 (white, cream, orange, deep orange, extruded\n1293\t  purple), with `FIASCO` beneath in scale 5, colors fire yellow to orange to red, a crack line through it (`px.line`\n1294\t  in dark), and a cartoon football with motion lines bouncing off the \"O\". A short intro animation: the football hits\n1295\t  the word, which cracks and shakes.\n1296\t- **Play cards:** `E.ui.box` with a team-color gradient, a mini field strip (green with yard lines) where routes are\n1297\t  `px.line` with arrow heads in white and the team color, blocks as short T bars, and zones as dithered circles\n1298\t  (`px.polyDither`). The play name is font scale 2, plus a RUN/PASS/TRICK/KICK badge and the star badge for COACH\n1299\t  SAYS.\n1300\t- **Fiasco Cards:** a card frame in purple and gold with the card's art drawn by code (cleats with flames, glue\n1301\t  gloves, a brick wall, a hot sauce bottle, a big fist, butter, the mascot's head, a boot) and the name in big text.\n1302\t- Comic bursts, glyph chips (§9.3), the score bug, tabs and buttons all draw with engine primitives only (rule 2 of\n1303\t  API.md: no `ctx.arc`, `fillText` or canvas gradients on the game buffer).\n1304\t\n1305\t### 12.9 Checking the art\n1306\t`node .cache/engine/dist/handoff/tools/asset-sheet.mjs $PWD/src/24-shapes.js#<id>` for every shape. `node tools/filmstrip.mjs <page>#<deep link> --steps \"...\" --seed 1` for\n1307\tevery pose in §12.3 (the drill and dev deep links set them up). A swing must wind up, strike and settle back without\n1308\tjerks. Take screenshots only for the look (§21.6).\n1309\t\n1310\t---\n1311\t\n1312\t## 13. Audio (`20-audio-voice.js`, `21-audio-music.js`)\n1313\tAll sound is synthesized: the engine's chip synth (`audio.sfx`, `audio.music`, `audio.define`) plus our Web Audio\n1314\tnodes on engine buses (E6). There are no audio files. Every composition is original: write new melodies, and\n1315\tdon't transcribe known stadium tunes or fight songs.\n1316\t\n1317\t### 13.1 Music (`{ bpm, steps, tracks }`, named tracks for layers)\n1318\t| Song | For | Character |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49428dbe-779b-4248-8ac3-c582018d3c3d","uuid":"b2acc23f-8128-4853-ab3e-c4318c374d63","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:06:22.596Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-070556__xb697dc/work/PLAN.md","content":"### 10.1 Hot Streak (\"BLAZING!\")\n- **Big plays** are: a TD, a catch of 20+ yd, a run of 15+ yd, a sack, an INT, a forced fumble, and a Big Hit that\n  tackles. Each athlete keeps a heat count. +1 per big play by him. It resets when the opponents make a big play\n  against him (a sack of that QB, a tackle for a loss on that carrier, a pick of that QB) or when they score.\n- At heat 3 he goes **BLAZING** for `T.hotPlays` (6 plays), or until a reset event happens:\n  - unlimited turbo, +12% speed;\n  - offense: tackle p −0.15 against him;\n  - defense: tackle p +0.15, Big Hit fumble ×2;\n  - a QB: aim error ×0.6 and fire-trail passes;\n  - visuals: fire particles at his feet and shoulders (`particles.fire` every 0.05 s, emissive), a flaming ball while\n    he has it, an orange light on him at night;\n  - audio: the music's `hot` layer comes in (`audio.layer('hot', 1, .5)`), the crowd chants, the announcer's\n    `hotStreakOn` lines.\n- A team can have 2 blazing athletes. The HUD shows a flame icon by his name and a heat pip count (1–3) on held\n  athletes' tags.\n\n### 10.2 The Fiasco Meter and the Fiasco Cards (the items)\n**The Fiasco Meter** is the title's mechanic: every disaster is an opportunity. Each team's meter (0–100) fills when\nthings go wrong for it:\n\n| Event | Fill |\n|---|---|\n| fumble lost | 35 |\n| INT thrown | 35 |\n| safety allowed | 40 |\n| sacked | 20 |\n| turnover on downs | 25 |\n| opponent's TD | 20 |\n| dropped pass | 10 |\n| Big Hit received | 10 |\n| late hit received | 5 |\n\nWhen it fills, the team **draws a Fiasco Card** at random from its pool (story: the cards you've unlocked;\nexhibition: all 8), up to 3 held. Then the meter resets. A HUD flourish plays: a card flips in, \"FIASCO BREAK!\".\nEach team also starts a game with cards: story, a loadout of up to 3 picked on the chapter screen; exhibition, 1\nrandom card each; hub rounds, 1 each, dealt from `AIHub.rng('cards')`.\n\n**Using a card:** on the play-call screen press b4 (△) to open the card row and pick one (or click a slot). One card\nper play. A card on offense needs an offensive card and so on; a card that doesn't fit the side is greyed out. Its\neffect lasts as its text says. Cards are data: `{ id, name, side: 'off' | 'def' | 'any' | 'kick', text, art,\napply(ctx) }`. `apply` registers bus modifiers for the play or for N plays. The CPU trigger is in §8.5.\n\n| Card | Side | Effect | CPU uses it when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| ROCKET CLEATS | off | your carrier and receivers +20% speed this play | 3rd & 10+, or trailing in the last 2:00 |\n| GLUE GLOVES | off | your receivers can't drop the ball; contested catches +30% this play | a pass play on 3rd or 4th down |\n| BRICK WALL | off | your blockers can't be shed for 3.5 s | a pass play on 3rd & long |\n| HOT SAUCE | any | the held athlete (CPU: its best player) goes BLAZING for 3 plays | first chance in the 2nd half |\n| MEGA HIT | def | this play's first tackle is a Mega Hit: launch × 1.6, fumble chance 60%, the slow-mo cam | 3rd down defense, or the opponent in the red zone |\n| BUTTERFINGERS | def | opposing receivers' catch chance −35% this play | 3rd & long defense |\n| MASCOT MAYHEM | any | your mascot runs on as a 12th player for the play: he blocks the nearest defender on offense, rushes the passer on defense, with `noClip` through blockers. The announcers lose their minds. | trailing by 7+ |\n| SUPER FOOT | kick | the next kick: +15 yd, an accuracy band ×2.5, the power needle ×0.7 speed | a FG of 45+ yd, or a PAT in the last minute |\n\n### 10.3 Big Hits, Mega Hits, Dinged and the flying helmet\n- **Big Hit:** turbo + b1 (§7.4–7.5). Hit-stop 0.08 s, `game.shake(4)`, `game.hitFx` with an impact star, grass, mud\n  or snow bits, a camera punch-in to 1.25× for 0.35 s, slow motion (`timeScale` 0.4 for 0.3 s, honoring reduce\n  motion), a comic \"BOOM!\" / \"WHAM!\" / \"KER-RUNCH!\" burst over the hit, and the crowd \"OOOOH\".\n- **Mega Hit** (the card, or a 1-in-6 roll of a Blazing Big Hit): launch × 1.6, the victim spins in the air (PoseFX\n  spin), hit-stop 0.12, the slow-mo cam (`timeScale` 0.25 for 0.6 s), a white flash (`game.flash`, honoring the\n  flashes setting).\n- **Dinged:** the victim of a Mega Hit, or of 2 Big Hits in one drive, is Dinged for 2 plays: −10% speed and little\n  cartoon stars orbiting his helmet (3 tiny glints circling, emissive).\n- **The flying helmet:** on a Mega Hit (and 25% of Big Hits) the victim's helmet pops off as a separate bouncing\n  prop: a shape `helmet` in team colors, an `E.Body` with bounce 0.5. His hair shows until the next PRESNAP, when he\n  picks it up (cosmetic). The announcer says \"HIS HELMET IS IN A DIFFERENT AREA CODE!\"\n\n### 10.4 Late hits\nAfter the whistle, for 1.2 s, b1 near an opponent does a late hit (cosmetic knockdown). The refs throw their caps\n(Fiasco rules: no flags). A crowd reaction, the announcer's outrage lines, a stat. AI athletes late-hit too, by team\npersonality (the Mudhogs often, the Dynasty sneakily).\n\n### 10.5 Boss specials (story bosses; also in exhibition)\nEach special is used by the AI, or by a human holding that star (in exhibition or a hub round), who presses **lb and\nrb together** (L1 + R1, LB + RB, Q + E) within 0.1 s while its conditions hold. A single shoulder press waits those\n0.1 s before it becomes a lateral, so the chord never laterals by accident. For the Golden Spiral, press the chord,\nthen a receiver button within 1 s. A badge shows \"SPECIAL READY\" on the star's tag. NIGHT VISION is passive.\n\n| Star | Special | Rules |\n|---|---|---|\n| BIG BERTHA BOUDREAUX (Mudhogs RB #44) | **MUDSLIDE** | once per drive: for 1.2 s she lowers her shoulder; the first tackler in front is bowled over (down 1.2 s) unless it's a Big Hit from the front; mud spray FX |\n| LUMEN LOPEZ (Owls QB #1) | **NIGHT VISION** | always on: his reads see 1 extra yard of openness, and his aim error ×0.8 |\n| ZAP ZAPATA (Owls WR #11) | **AFTERBURNER** | once per play: a 1.0 s burst at ×1.35 speed that leaves neon light trails (`ghost` afterimages in cyan) |\n| AVALANCHE (Yetis DE #99) | **SNOWPLOW** | once per drive: his engagement drives the blocker straight back at 3× push for 1.5 s; a snow spray |\n| BROCK STERLING III (Dynasty QB #12) | **GOLDEN SPIRAL** | once per drive: a perfect pass, no aim error, it can't be intercepted (defenders may still deflect it with 0.15), gold sparkle trail |\n| THE MOUNTAIN, MALU FALEOLO (Dynasty LB #55) | **SEISMIC SACK** | once per half, when within 3 yd of the carrier: he leaps (0.6 s) and slams down; everyone within 2.5 yd is knocked down; a shockwave ring (`particles.ring`), shake 7, \"SEISMIC!\" |\nThe commentary has lines for each, and the HUD shows a banner with the star's portrait for 1.2 s when one fires.\n\n### 10.6 Celebrations\nAfter a TD the scorer celebrates. Locally the scorer's human picks one: b2 the Charleston, b3 the Body Roll, b4 the\nHelicopter (breakdance). Otherwise it's random by personality, from the list below. In hub sessions it's always\nrandom (no player-triggered emotes, §16.6).\n\n| Celebration | How it's animated |\n|---|---|\n| Spike | a throw-down attack spec, the ball bounces high |\n| Charleston, Body Roll | mocap `Dance Charleston` / `Dance Body Roll` |\n| Helicopter | mocap `Breakdance_Helicopter` |\n| Backflip | mocap `Backflip` |\n| Fist pump | mocap `Victory Fist Pump` |\n| Stands Dive | he leaps into the end zone stands: `body.jump`, the crowd lifts him, bodies bob |\n| Group Huddle Dance | 3 nearest teammates do `Dance_Loop` in a ring |\n\nTeammates near him do `Cheering_Two_Hands`. Defenders kneel (`pose: 'kneel'`) or put their hands on their helmets\n(PoseFX). Pyro cannons fire, confetti falls (`particles.bits` in team colors from z 160), the crowd goes wild.\n\n### 10.7 Mascots\nEach team has a mascot on the near sideline: a Humanoid in team colors with a big costume head drawn by the gear\nhook (§12.2). They react: dance on scores, slump on turnovers, and do a backflip on a Big Hit. They flip the coin, and\nrun on with Mascot Mayhem (`noClip`, a cartoon dust cloud, a squeaky sfx). Fumbles the Flaming Tumbleweed sets\nhimself on fire when the Fiascos score (fire particles), and trips over the power cable in chapter 3 (§15.1).\n\n### 10.8 Refs\nTwo refs on the field (an umpire 6 yd behind the defense, a back judge 20 yd deep) and a line judge on the near\nsideline. They're cosmetic Humanoids in striped shirts (the gear hook draws the stripes), with poses for signals:\nTOUCHDOWN (both arms up), FIRST DOWN (an arm pointing at the offense's goal), INCOMPLETE (arms crossing, a wave),\nFUMBLE / POSSESSION (pointing), and \"Sure, why not\" (a shrug) after a late hit. A play running through a ref knocks\nhim over comically (the announcer: \"AND THE REF GOES DOWN! HE'S FINE! HE'S... MOSTLY FINE!\").\n\n### 10.9 LIGHTS OUT (chapter 3's event; also a Dev toggle)\nFor 3 plays: `lights.ambient` 0.12, `darkness` 0.9, the light towers off. Every uniform's trim, the Owls' neon, the\nball, the yard lines and the Fiascos' glow paint (their trim turns `#7aff6a` with glow) stay bright as emissive (the\ngear hook draws trims with `px.glow` and queues them `emissive: true`). Camera flashes in the crowd sparkle.\nCommentary and the crowd play along, then the lights come back with a thunk and a flicker.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Presentation\n\n### 11.1 The camera director (`37-camera.js`)\nOur own smoothing (`E.smoothDamp` on x, y and zoom), `game.focus(x, y, z)` every update, `game.setZoom(z)`, and\n`cam.bounds = v => map.bounds(v)`. The player's own zoom (wheel, `-` `=`) multiplies ours.\n\n| Shot | When | Focus and zoom |\n|---|---|---|\n| PRESNAP | the formation | x = LOS + dir × 5 yd; y = the ball's y × 0.6 + MID_Y × 0.4; zoom 1.0 |\n| RUN | a carrier | the carrier + v × `T.camLead` (0.35 s); zoom 1.05 |\n| PASS_PRE | QB with the ball on a pass play | `cam.frame([qb, ...receivers within 30 yd], { margin: 40, zoom: [.62, 1] })` |\n| BALL_AIR | a pass in the air | between the ball's ground point and its landing point, zoomed to fit both (min .62) |\n| KICK | kickoffs and punts | follow the ball, zoom .75; on the catch, RUN on the returner |\n| KICKCAM | FG and PAT | cut (`{ fade: 0 }` style, 0.15 s dissolve) to the `kickcam` view behind the kicker; follow the ball to the posts; hold 1.2 s on the result; cut back |\n| PUNCH | a Big Hit or Mega Hit | zoom × 1.25 over 0.12 s, hold 0.25 s, ease back over 0.4 s |\n| CELEBRATE | after a TD | the scorer, zoom 1.35 |\n| CUTAWAY | after the celebration (50% of TDs) | pan up to the stands at the end zone for 1.2 s, zoom 1.2: \"the crowd goes wild\" |\n| REPLAY | §11.2 | `field`, `iso`, `reverse` views at 0.5× and 0.35× |\n| CUTSCENE | §15.1 | scripted tweens (`game.tween` on a camera target object) |\nViews are fixed per shot. Never animate the yaw continuously: each new yaw rebakes the floor.\n\n### 11.2 Instant replay and the highlight reel (`38-replay.js`)\n- **Recording:** from the snap to 1 s after the whistle, at 60 Hz (every 2nd step), record a frame per entity:\n  athletes `[x, y, z, facing, poseCode, poseU, flags]` (flags: carrying, hot, dinged, helmet off), the ball\n  `[x, y, z, state, spin]`, refs and the mascot. Record presentation events with their time: hit FX, particles\n  bursts, comic pops, sfx names, card banners. A 12 s ring buffer in `Float32Array`s.\n- **Playback** is a REPLAY sub-state of the match scene. The sim is frozen and untouched. Rigs are driven from the\n  frames (positions interpolated, velocity derived for the gait), the recorded events re-fire at their times, and\n  the audio plays the sfx (the commentary doesn't repeat; the crowd bed stays). Shots: 1) the `field` view following\n  the ball at 0.5× over the 3 s around the key moment; 2) the `iso` or `reverse` view at 0.35× for the impact. Then\n  back to the live view.\n- **The overlay:** a REPLAY badge with a blinking red dot, a VCR timecode, letterbox bars, \"✕ SKIP\" (b1 or a click\n  skips). The music ducks.\n- **Triggers:** a TD (when Replays is All big plays or Touchdowns only), a turnover, a Mega Hit, a Big Hit fumble, a\n  play of 40+ yd, a FG of 50+ yd, a Seismic Sack, a Mascot Mayhem play. Setting: Replays: All big plays (default) /\n  Touchdowns only / Off. In hub sessions: off.\n- **Highlight reel:** the 5 most exciting clips of the game, by an excitement score (event priority × yards), are\n  kept (8 s each). The results screen offers WATCH HIGHLIGHTS, which plays them back to back with captions\n  (\"Q2 3:12 — DOC DOBSON 48-YD TD RUN\").\n- **Invariant (tested):** the sim's state hash is the same before and after a replay.\n\n### 11.3 Commentary and on-field text (`39-commentary.js`)\n- **Two announcers:** CHET THUNDERBUNS (play-by-play: loud, excitable) and LOU \"THE TOE\" DIGGS (color: an ex-kicker,\n  folksy, deadpan).\n- **Events** have priorities (Appendix D): TD 10, turnover 9, Mega Hit 9, special 8, Big Hit 8, sack 8, long play 7,\n  Hot Streak 7, mascot 7, FG result 7, late hit 6, card 6, drop 5, first down 4, incomplete 3, weather 2, idle\n  chatter 1.\n- **Rules:** at most one line per 2.5 s. A higher priority interrupts a lower one. On events of priority ≥ 7, CHET\n  speaks and LOU answers 1.2 s later with chance 0.4. No line repeats within the last 8 for that event. Lines take\n  variables (`{player}`, `{team}`, `{opp}`, `{yards}`, `{score}`).\n- **The caption:** a non-modal box at the bottom left (keep clear of the prompt strip and the score bug). The\n  speaker's portrait (`rig.drawPortrait` of the announcer rig: a headset and a blazer) and name, the text typed at\n  45 chars/s with the babble voice (§13.4). It hides after its length / 15 + 1.5 s. The Commentary setting: On /\n  Subtitles only (no voice) / Off.\n- **On-field pops:** comic bursts in world space over the event: BOOM!, WHAM!, KER-RUNCH!, SACKED!, PICKED OFF!,\n  FUMBLE!, PANCAKE!, BROKEN TACKLE!, DOINK!, BLAZING!, FIASCO BREAK!, SEISMIC!, DROPPED!. `E.font.title` with an\n  outline over a jagged polygon burst (`px.poly`, 12 points with radii alternating 1 and 0.6). It scales from 0.4 to\n  1.1 to 1.0 (`outBack`) and lasts 0.9 s. Anchor it with `r.w(x, y, z + 40)`.\n- **Center text** for game events: TOUCHDOWN! (title scale 4 in the scoring team's colors with a shine sweep), FIRST\n  DOWN!, TURNOVER!, SAFETY!, IT'S GOOD! / NO GOOD!, TOUCHBACK, 4TH DOWN, RED ZONE, TWO-MINUTE WARNING (if quarters\n  are 2:00 or longer), LIGHTS OUT!\n\n### 11.4 The crowd (`26-crowd.js`)\n- **Fans** sit on the stand tiers: 2–3 per tile per tier (about 2,400 at the Mega Dome). Each is drawn like the SPORTS\n  kit's fans (`r.queue` with 2–3 `px.rect`s: shirt, head, an optional hat), with the team colors by section (home\n  sections, plus an away section by one end zone), and skin and hat variety from a seeded hash. 8% hold signs: a\n  6×4 rectangle with a tiny-font word (\"FIASCO!\", \"D!\", \"HOGS!\", \"HOOT!\", \"BRRR!\", \"$$$\"). 5% have foam fingers.\n- **Excitement E** (0–1): big events set it up, `T.crowdDecay` (0.15/s) brings it down. Above 0.6 the fans stand and\n  bob. On a TD the scoring side's fans jump (+5 z). Below 0.2 they sway.\n- **The Wave** rolls around the stands every 40–70 s when E is moderate and the home team leads: a sine wave of\n  stand-ups moving 10 tiles/s.\n- **Density** by stadium. Tumbleweed Field is 35% full until the story's ending, when it's 100%.\n- **Camera flashes** at night: random 1-px white dots with tiny lights, more on big plays.\n- **Audio:** the crowd bed and reactions (§13.3).\n\n### 11.5 FX (`40-fx.js`)\n- **Hits:** `game.hitFx(x, y, z, { power, angle })` with no damage number (leave `damage` out and check that none\n  shows), `particles.impact`, surface bits (grass `#4a8a3a`/`#2e5a22`, mud `#5a3a1a`, snow `#f0f4ff`), dust, and white\n  `particles.sparks` on helmet-to-helmet hits.\n- **Divots:** on Big Hits and dives, a persistent decal of torn turf at the spot, up to 40 per game (the oldest fade).\n- **Footprints** in snow and mud: small decals behind runners every 0.15 s, fading over 6 s, up to 200.\n- **Breath puffs** at Frostbite: `particles.smoke` at each head every 1.2 s, on the cosmetic RNG stream.\n- **Weather:** `game.weather = { kind: 'rain', amount: .6, wind: .2, lightning: .1 }` at the Hog Wallow;\n  `{ kind: 'snow', amount: .7, wind: .3 }` at Frostbite; set in the match's `enter` (weather ends with the scene).\n- **Celebrations:** confetti (`particles.bits` in team colors from z 160), fireworks in the sky\n  (`particles.explosion(..., { debris: false, shake: 0 })` and colored rings at z 300+ over the end zone), pyro columns\n  from the cannons (`particles.fire` + a light), streamers.\n- **Trails:** a Hot Streak's fire on the ball and athlete, Afterburner's neon ghosts (`r.actor(..., { ghost })`), the\n  Golden Spiral's gold glints.\n- **Lights** (`game.lights.enabled = true` in every stadium):\n  - Tumbleweed: dusk, `ambient` 0.62 warm, a low sun light from the west, string lights over the bleachers.\n  - Hog Wallow: overcast, 0.55, lightning flashes from the weather.\n  - Afterglow: night, 0.35, 4 light towers (radius 420, intensity 0.9) and colored neon lights.\n  - Frostbite: 0.5, the northern lights tint the sky, towers.\n  - Mega Dome: indoor 0.55, 6 spotlights sweeping on tweens, pyro lights.\n  - Try GPU lighting (`game.enableGPU({ map })`, ground views) for soft shadows from the stands. The canvas fallback\n    must look right too: set both ambients.\n- **Shadows:** `r.shadow` under every athlete, and under the ball with a radius and alpha that shrink with its\n  height. The ball's shadow is how players read a lob.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Art and animation\n\n### 12.1 The look target (from API.md: use every step)\n`res: 'ps1'` with `expand: true` (480×270 at 1080p, 427×240 at 1440p and 4K). Dressed HD characters 40–60 px tall\n(sizes 1.2–1.45; bosses 1.6–1.8). A backdrop behind the stands. A textured field and stands. 3–8 props on screen.\nEffects on every hit. Colors shaded with `E.tones`. Titles with `E.font.title`. Lights in every scene. Portraits in\nevery dialog. Compare screenshots with Metal Slug and Symphony of the Night, not NES games. `node tools/check.mjs`\ngives look notes: act on every one.\n\n### 12.2 Characters (`27-rigs.js`)\n**Rig recipes by position** (`new E.Humanoid({...})`, `weapon: null`, `sleeves: 'short'`, `outfit: 'shirt'`,\n`hat: { style: 'football', color, stripe, logo }` (E4)):\n\n| Position | build | size | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| OL, DL | bulky | 1.38–1.48 | `shoulderHalf` +0.6, `torsoW` +0.6, a lean of 0.1 |\n| LB | bulky or heroic | 1.3 | |\n| RB | heroic | 1.22 | stocky: `limbW` +0.3 |\n| WR, CB, S | heroic | 1.2 | lean: `limbW` −0.2 |\n| QB | heroic | 1.25 | |\n| K | heroic | 1.02 | the tiny kicker (a joke the announcer makes) |\n| Bosses: Bertha 1.6, The Mountain 1.7, Avalanche 1.8 | bulky | | Avalanche has a beard (gear hook) and `eyeGlow` off |\n| Refs | heroic | 1.15 | a cap (`hat: 'cap'`, white); stripes from the gear hook |\n| Coaches | bulky or heroic | 1.2 | a cap and a headset (gear hook), a polo |\n| Cheerleaders | heroic | 1.1 | `hair: 'ponytail'`, pom-poms (gear hook) |\n| Mascots | bulky | 1.3 | a costume head (gear hook), team colors |\n| Announcers (portraits only) | heroic | 1.2 | a headset, a blazer (`outfit: 'coat'`) |\n| Story cast (Mama Pearl, Sterling, ...) | per character | 1.2 | §18.1 |\n\n**The uniform from team colors:** `colors.cloth` is the jersey, `trim` the jersey trim (sleeve bands), `pants`,\n`belt`, `boot` the cleats, `glove` the gloves, the hat color the helmet. Away teams wear white jerseys with\nteam-color trim, and home teams wear their color. Skin tones (`#f0c8a8 #e0b090 #c89070 #a87050 #6a4028 #4a2c18`) and\nhair styles vary per player (data). Faces show: `face: { eyes: 'big' }` on story cast, default on athletes, and eye\nblack on athletes (gear hook).\n\n**The gear hook (E3)** draws, depth-sorted inside the rig:\n- **Shoulder pads:** a wide disc over each shoulder joint in the jersey color, with a darker rim. They sit over the\n  torso, so the silhouette reads as football at a glance.\n- **The jersey number:** 3×5 digits (`font: 'tiny'`, scale by `u`) in the trim color, on the chest when the torso\n  faces the camera (`dot(facing, view.fx/fy) > .3`), on the back when it faces away (< −.3), hidden edge-on. Placed at\n  `Sp(J.shC, ±torsoDepth, 0, -3)`.\n- **The carried ball:** at the carrying hand, a brown ellipse with white laces (below), at the hand's depth + 0.02.\n  The sim sets `rig.carry = 'R' | 'L' | null`.\n- **Eye black,** a headset on coaches, pom-poms on cheerleaders (discs at the hands, team colors), ref stripes (black\n  vertical lines over the torso).\n- **Mascot heads:** a big disc 2.2× the head with features. Fumbles is a twig ball (brown line scribbles) with googly\n  eyes. Hambone is a pink hog with a snout and ears. Hooty is an owl with neon eyes (glow). Abominable Al is a white\n  fur ball with horns. Goldie is a gold lion with a mane.\n- **Big Heads cheat:** `rig.o.headR × 1.9` live. Check it re-solves; if not, rebuild the rigs.\n- **The Fiascos' glow paint** in LIGHTS OUT: the trims drawn with `px.glow(g, 1)` and an emissive queue.\n\n### 12.3 Pose codes to animation (`FF.Rigs.drive(rig, athlete, dt)`)\nThe sim sets `pose` and `poseU` (Appendix C). The presentation maps each to rig inputs, from four sources: the\nengine's procedural rig (velocity gait, `pose`, `expr`, `air`, `down`, `stance`, `run`, `flip`, `land`), `E.MOVES`\nand attack specs, mocap clips (§12.4), and PoseFX (§12.5).\n\n| Pose | Drive |\n|---|---|\n| IDLE, RUN | `rig.update(dt, { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing })`, the velocity gait; `sprint: true` with turbo |\n| STANCE3 (linemen) | mocap `Land_Three_Point` held at its last key (a hand on the ground), `mocapW` 1 |\n| STANCE2 (LB, WR, DB) | `pose: 'crouch'` blended 0.5, a lean of 0.25 |\n| QB_UC / QB_SG | `pose: 'crouch'` 0.35 with the hands forward (an attack spec held), or upright with the hands at the chest |\n| SNAP | a two-handed spec from low forward to between the legs, 0.25 s |\n| DROPBACK | the gait backward (verify the backpedal in a filmstrip; if it looks wrong, turn `facing` 25° off the motion) |\n| THROW | mocap `OverhandThrow`, `mocapMask: 'upper'` while moving (throwing on the run), time-scaled so the release lands on the sim's release frame |\n| HANDOFF give / take | specs: the arm extends / both arms form a pocket |\n| CARRY | the gait plus PoseFX `tuck` (the carrying hand to the chest side, the elbow in) |\n| CATCH_READY, CATCH | a two-handed spec reaching to the ball's height (`z1` from the arrival height); `air: true` with a jump |\n| DIVE, TACKLE_DIVE | PoseFX `tilt` forward 0→75° over 0.15 s, the arms forward (a two-handed `thrust`), `air: true`; on landing `down: 1` |\n| SPIN | the `facing` passed to `rig.update` turned through a full circle over the action (`facing + 2π·u`, eased); don't write `rig.spin` (the rig's own field for attack spins) |\n| STIFFARM | the `jab` move with the free hand, held 70% of the action |\n| HURDLE | mocap `Run_Jump_Over`, time-scaled to the jump |\n| BLOCK | mocap `Push_Loop` (`mocapMask: 'upper'`) + a lean of 0.2; feet from the gait |\n| SHED / SWIM | `E.MOVES.hook` (an arm over) |\n| BIGHIT | `E.MOVES.bash` + PoseFX `tilt` 25° |\n| TACKLED | mocap `Fall_On_Face` (tackled from behind) or `Hit_Knockback` (from the front), then DOWN |\n| FLY (a Big Hit victim) | PoseFX `tilt` back 70° + `roll` spin (Mega Hit), `air: true`, then DOWN |\n| DOWN | `down: 1` |\n| GETUP | mocap `Get_Up_Face_Down` or `Get_Up_From_Back`, by how he fell |\n| PILE | `down: 1` + PoseFX random `tilt`/`roll` and a z offset (stacked) |\n| KICK | `E.MOVES.kick` after a 3-step run-up |\n| HOLD | `pose: 'kneel'` + a hand low forward |\n| CELEBRATE(k) | §10.6 |\n| CHEER | mocap `Cheering_Two_Hands` (teammates), `pose: 'cheer'` (refs and coaches) |\n| DEJECTED | `pose: 'kneel'`, or PoseFX `handsOnHelmet` |\n| REF_TD, REF_FD, REF_INC, REF_SHRUG | specs: both arms up, an arm pointing, arms crossing back and forth, a shrug |\n| CHEERLEADER | mocap `Jumping Jacks` and `Cheering_Two_Hands`, alternating |\n| COACH_YELL | `expr: 'shout'`, `pose: 'hips'`, the headset |\nFaces act: `expr: 'shout'` on hits and celebrations, `'wince'` when hurt, `'smile'` when Blazing. Enemy specials\ntelegraph with a 0.25–0.35 s wind-up and a flash.\n\n### 12.4 Motion clips (the FIASCO set)\nCut once, from the engine repository (§3.2):\n```sh\nnode .cache/engine/tools/anim-set.mjs .cache/engine/src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js .cache/engine/src/mocap/sets/mesh2motion.js \\\n  .cache/engine/src/mocap/sets/cmu.js \\\n  --clips \"QUATERNIUS:OverhandThrow,QUATERNIUS:Push_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Dance_Loop,Dance Charleston,Dance Body Roll,Victory Fist Pump,Cheering_Two_Hands,Breakdance_Helicopter,Run_Jump_Over,Dive_Roll,Fall_On_Face,Get_Up_Face_Down,Get_Up_From_Back,QUATERNIUS:Hit_Knockback,MESH2MOTION:Land_Three_Point,Jumping Jacks,Front_Kick,MESH2MOTION:Backflip\" \\\n  --name FIASCO --credit \"Quaternius (CC0), Mesh2Motion (CC0), CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database (free for all uses)\" \\\n  --out vendor/anim/fiasco-anim.js\n```\nThis was run during planning. It writes 18 clips, 736 key poses, 222 KB. In the set the clips are named without the\n`SET:` prefix (`lib.clip('OverhandThrow')`). A headless probe confirmed that each drives an HD Humanoid (bulky, 1.3) on\nthe handoff engine: `Land_Three_Point` ends with the hand at z ≈ 1 (a three-point stance), and `OverhandThrow` raises\nthe hand to z ≈ 28 and comes through. Use:\n```js\nconst lib = Mocap.load(window.MOCAP.FIASCO);  Mocap.drive(rig, lib);           // once per rig\nrig.mocap = lib.sample(lib.clip('OverhandThrow'), t); rig.mocapW = w; rig.mocapMask = 'upper';  // each step, before rig.update\n```\nFade clips in and out with `mocapW` over 0.1 s. Never snap.\n\n### 12.5 PoseFX (new animation by joint post-processing)\nWrap each athlete rig's `solvePose` (the API allows it): call the original, then apply the active transforms to\n`rig.J` (all joints are in the rig's own frame: forward, right, up):\n- `tilt(angle)` rotates every joint about the hip center around the right axis (forward dives, backward falls).\n- `roll(angle)` rotates about the forward axis.\n- `lift(dz)` raises everything.\n- `tuck(side)` moves the hand and elbow of that side to fixed points by the chest (ball security).\n- `handsOnHelmet` puts both hands at the head's sides.\nTransforms blend with weights so they ease in and out. This is how Emberdeep makes its dodge roll (AI_GUIDE, Building\na big game).\n\n### 12.6 New shapes (`24-shapes.js`) and store props\nWrite these as `E.SHAPES` entries (docs/ASSETS.md format; 16 units = 1 m; face south). Look at each with\n`node .cache/engine/dist/handoff/tools/asset-sheet.mjs $PWD/src/24-shapes.js#<id>` and fix its lint notes:\n`pylon` (orange foam 2×2×7), `cone` (an orange traffic cone on a base), `dummy` (a red tackling dummy, r 4, h 22),\n`sled` (a blocking sled with two pads), `cooler` (an orange sports-drink cooler with a white lid and spigot), `cups`\n(a stacked paper cup tower), `teamBench` (a long bench, `params: { len }`, a team-color material slot), `lightTower` (a\nlattice tower h 200, a lamp bank in a glow material, `lights`), `oldScoreboard` (Tumbleweed's hand-flipped board;\ndigits drawn by code), `jumbotron` (a big dark screen on a pylon; the content drawn by code into its projected quad:\nthe score and \"MAKE SOME NOISE!\"), `downMarker` (an orange pole with a flip card; the down drawn by code),\n`chainPole`, `tvCamera` (a camera on a tripod), `podium`, `micStand`, `locker` (a metal locker 10×6×30 with vents and a\nteam-color door), `chalkboard` (on an easel; X's and O's by code), `trophy` (the Fiasco Cup: a gold lathe cup with\nhandles and a football on top), `pickupTruck`, `waterTower` (\"TUMBLEWEED JCT\" by code), `airboat`, `neonSign` (glow\nletters by code), `snowbank` (snowy rock lumps), `pyroCannon`, `blimp` (a flattened ball with fins, drawn at z 300+),\n`stage` (a ceremony stage with bunting), `cake` (a tiered victory cake), `bulldozer` (yellow, blade, tracks),\n`goldCart` (a gold golf cart), `grill` (a tailgate grill; smoke from particles), `helmet` (a loose football helmet:\na shell ball and facemask bars, mats per team), `inflatableHelmet` (the giant team-entrance tunnel helmet), `bassDrum`\n(held by band members through the gear hook).\n\nFrom the core library, no store needed: `bench`, `table`, `barrel`, `crate`, `lamppost`, `fence`, `pine`, `tree`,\n`bush`, `grass`, `rock`. `r.prop` built-ins: `banner`, `sign`, `lamp`, `streetlamp`, `awning`, `cactus`, `palm`,\n`lantern`, `trashcan`, `firedrum`, `vines`. Cut the few store entries into one set:\n```sh\nS=.cache/engine/dist/handoff/src/assets/sets\nnode .cache/engine/dist/handoff/tools/asset-set.mjs $S/kenney-survival.js $S/kenney-graveyard.js $S/kenney-pirate.js $S/kenney-nature.js $S/kenney-furniture.js \\\n  --ids kenney-survival:bucket,kenney-graveyard:hay-bale,kenney-pirate:flag,kenney-nature:tent-small-closed,kenney-furniture:speaker \\\n  --name fiasco-store --out vendor/assets/fiasco-store.js\n```\nThis was run during planning: 5 shapes, 10 materials, 1,799 tokens. Load it with\n`E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['fiasco-store'])`, which names the entries `fiasco-store:<id>`. The bucket is the sports-drink bucket dump. Use\n`asset-find.mjs` for anything else. The store sets are CC0: credit Kenney on the About screen.\n\n### 12.7 The football\nDrawn in `r.queue` at the ball's world position, or by the gear hook while carried. It is a prolate ellipse (a\n10-point polygon), 7×4 px at zoom 1, brown `#8a4a22` with an `E.tones` shade and highlight, a white lace stripe of 3\nstitches, and a white band at each tip. Its long axis follows the projected velocity\n(`r.w(p)` → `r.w(p + v·dt)`). In flight it spins: alternate the lace position each 1/30 s so it reads as a spiral.\nKicks tumble end over end (the axis rotates in screen space at 10 rad/s). Shadow below. A flame trail when Blazing, a\ngold trail on the Golden Spiral, white speed lines on Rocket Passes.\n\n### 12.8 Logos, field art and UI art\n- **Team logos** are string sprites (`E.sprite`), 16×16, with a 4–6 color palette per team: a flaming tumbleweed, a\n  hog head with tusks, neon owl eyes, a yeti footprint, a crown on a football, and a grey \"P\" on a whistle for the\n  Scrubs. Use them on the score bug (×1), menus (×3), the helmet ear dot (a 1–2 px dot of the main color), the\n  midfield paint (sampled as a bitmap at 1 sprite px = 0.5 yd) and the end-zone walls.\n- **The title logo:** `AMERICAN FOOTBALL` in `E.font.title` scale 3 (white, cream, orange, deep orange, extruded\n  purple), with `FIASCO` beneath in scale 5, colors fire yellow to orange to red, a crack line through it (`px.line`\n  in dark), and a cartoon football with motion lines bouncing off the \"O\". A short intro animation: the football hits\n  the word, which cracks and shakes.\n- **Play cards:** `E.ui.box` with a team-color gradient, a mini field strip (green with yard lines) where routes are\n  `px.line` with arrow heads in white and the team color, blocks as short T bars, and zones as dithered circles\n  (`px.polyDither`). The play name is font scale 2, plus a RUN/PASS/TRICK/KICK badge and the star badge for COACH\n  SAYS.\n- **Fiasco Cards:** a card frame in purple and gold with the card's art drawn by code (cleats with flames, glue\n  gloves, a brick wall, a hot sauce bottle, a big fist, butter, the mascot's head, a boot) and the name in big text.\n- Comic bursts, glyph chips (§9.3), the score bug, tabs and buttons all draw with engine primitives only (rule 2 of\n  API.md: no `ctx.arc`, `fillText` or canvas gradients on the game buffer).\n\n### 12.9 Checking the art\n`node .cache/engine/dist/handoff/tools/asset-sheet.mjs $PWD/src/24-shapes.js#<id>` for every shape. `node tools/filmstrip.mjs <page>#<deep link> --steps \"...\" --seed 1` for\nevery pose in §12.3 (the drill and dev deep links set them up). A swing must wind up, strike and settle back without\njerks. Take screenshots only for the look (§21.6).\n\n---\n\n## 13. Audio (`20-audio-voice.js`, `21-audio-music.js`)\nAll sound is synthesized: the engine's chip synth (`audio.sfx`, `audio.music`, `audio.define`) plus our Web Audio\nnodes on engine buses (E6). There are no audio files. Every composition is original: write new melodies, and\ndon't transcribe known stadium tunes or fight songs.\n\n### 13.1 Music (`{ bpm, steps, tracks }`, named tracks for layers)\n| Song | For | Character |","numLines":420,"startLine":899,"totalLines":2515}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018BRYMLW8W2QqRwT7gNG3uG","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi1v6vRutL7Uy8LyA5g5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GbFh5KLhLVkmM9NfkeWCsQ","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-070556__xb697dc/work/PLAN.md","offset":1319,"limit":500},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20451,"cache_read_input_tokens":38995,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20451},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49428dbe-779b-4248-8ac3-c582018d3c3d","uuid":"e5425d43-0fac-4608-afd1-d8c800336150","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:06:23.620Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi1v6fYkpPZK2F6cZfom","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GbFh5KLhLVkmM9NfkeWCsQ":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-070556__xb697dc/work/PLAN.md","offset":1319,"limit":500}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GbFh5KLhLVkmM9NfkeWCsQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1319\t|---|---|---|\n1320\t| FIASCO ANTHEM | the title, the story hub | stadium rock, 132 bpm: a square lead, saw bass, a `k . s .` beat, a cheer-like hook |\n1321\t| LOCKER ROOM FUNK | menus, setup | 110 bpm, a slap-bass `pulse12` line, offbeat hats |\n1322\t| HUDDLE UP | the play-call screen | a drumline loop (drums only plus a low triangle ostinato), 120 bpm, 2 bars, rising tension |\n1323\t| DUST DEVIL STOMP | Tumbleweed Field | a western shuffle, triangle bass, a twangy pulse lead, 128 bpm |\n1324\t| SWAMP STOMP | The Hog Wallow | a blues shuffle, saw bass, a harmonica-like pulse with vibrato, 96 bpm |\n1325\t| NEON NIGHTDRIVE | Afterglow Arena | synthwave, saw arpeggios, a square lead, 118 bpm |\n1326\t| FROSTBITE FANFARE | Frostbite Field | bells (triangle and sine arpeggios), 100 bpm |\n1327\t| MEGA DOME ANTHEM | the Mega Dome | epic brass (3 squares in fifths), 140 bpm |\n1328\t| HALFTIME SHOW | halftime | a marching band: `k s s` drums, a brass melody |\n1329\t| ARCADE ATTRACT | the attract mode | a 150 bpm remix of the anthem |\n1330\t| FIASCO FOREVER | the credits | a slow ballad version of the anthem |\n1331\t| Stings | `audio.sting` | TD fanfare, FG good, first-down organ riff, defense chant riff, Fiasco Break \"wah-wah\", victory jingle, defeat jingle (a sad sliding saw) |\n1332\t\n1333\tIn matches the stadium song plays low under the crowd bed, with layers `hot` (more drums and a guitar-like saw, for a\n1334\tBlazing athlete), `redzone` (bass pulses inside the 20) and `final` (`audio.tempo` +8% in the last minute). Between\n1335\tplays, original stadium-organ riffs (square and triangle chords with vibrato) play as stings on first downs, and a\n1336\tdefense-chant riff plays on 3rd down.\n1337\t\n1338\t### 13.2 Sound effects (`audio.define` each; the engine warns on unknown names, and a test fails on such a warning)\n1339\thike (the QB's \"HUT\" voice + a snap thump), whistle, helmetClang (square 1800→1200 + a triangle ring), padsCrunch\n1340\t(lowpass noise 900→200 + sine 120→50), bigHit (crunch + clang + a boom sine 80→30), tackleThud, dive (whoosh),\n1341\tspinWhoosh, stiffArm (punch), hurdle (jump2), catchSlap (bandpass noise 1200, short), drop (thunk), throwWhoosh,\n1342\trocketPass (a saw sweep), kickThump (sine 150→60 + noise), doink (a triangle 1400 ring), airHorn (3 saw voices\n1343\t220/277/330, 0.6 s), cannon (boom), fireworks (explode + crackle bursts), confettiPop, coinFlip (blip arpeggio),\n1344\tcardFlip, fiascoBreak (a descending arpeggio + wah), hotOn (a fire whoosh + a rising arpeggio), pileThumps, refCapPop,\n1345\tmascotSqueak, lightsOut (a power-down sweep), lightsOn (a thunk + hum), menuMove, menuSelect, menuBack, meterTick,\n1346\tmeterSet. Crowd one-shots: roar, boo, oooh, groan, gasp, cheer swell (bandpassed noise shapes on the crowd bus).\n1347\t\n1348\t### 13.3 The crowd bed\n1349\tA long-lived looping noise source on the `crowd` bus, through a bandpass (500–1500 Hz), with gain\n1350\t`0.12 + 0.38 × E` (E from §11.4), plus a lower \"murmur\" layer. Reactions are the one-shots above. Chants are 6\n1351\tdetuned babble voices in rhythm with the team's chant syllables (\"FI-AS-CO!\", \"HOGS! HOGS! HOGS!\", \"HOOT-HOOT!\",\n1352\t\"BRRR-BRRR!\", \"DY-NAS-TY!\"), on the beat (`audio.onBeat`) when E > 0.4. Stadium size scales it: Tumbleweed is thin\n1353\tand quiet (until the ending), the Mega Dome thick.\n1354\t\n1355\t### 13.4 Voices: the babble synth (Animalese and Simlish)\n1356\t**The API:** `FF.voice.say(text, profile, { onSyllable })` plans syllables, schedules them on the `voices` bus and\n1357\treturns the plan. `FF.voice.letter(ch, profile)` is the E5 dialog hook, which groups typed letters into syllables\n1358\tlive. `FF.voice.stop(profile)`.\n1359\t\n1360\t**Two styles, one synth:**\n1361\t- **Animalese** (the story cast, refs, mascot noises): letter-driven. Each vowel group in the typed text is one\n1362\t  syllable, with its onset taken from the preceding consonant(s). Quick, high and cute.\n1363\t- **Simlish** (the announcers, coaches on the radio, the crowd chants): count the line's syllables, then speak that\n1364\t  many syllables drawn from a gibberish bank (`ba do zee ka fla nu ree bo shma gli va tor mip zub lo neh`), picked by\n1365\t  a hash of each real word so the same line sounds the same every time. More fluent, with less pitch jitter.\n1366\t\n1367\t**A syllable** = onset + nucleus:\n1368\t- **Onset** by consonant class: plosives (p b t d k g c q) are an 8 ms broadband noise click; fricatives (f s z v h\n1369\t  x, sh, th) are 25–40 ms of bandpassed or highpassed noise (s at 5 kHz, f at 3 kHz, h at 1.2 kHz); nasals (m n) are\n1370\t  30 ms of lowpassed voiced hum; liquids (l r w y) are a formant glide into the vowel.\n1371\t- **Nucleus:** an oscillator (the profile's wave) through two parallel bandpass filters at the vowel's formants\n1372\t  (a 800/1200, e 500/1900, i 320/2300, o 500/900, u 350/800 Hz, × the profile's formant scale; Q 6 and 10), with an\n1373\t  envelope of 6 ms attack, a sustain, and a 25 ms release. The duration is (1 / rate) × 0.6–1.0.\n1374\t- **Pitch** = base × 2^((jitter + contour) / 12). The jitter is ±2 semitones from a hash of the syllable, so it's\n1375\t  deterministic. The contour: questions rise +4 on the last 2 syllables, exclamations +3 and +30% volume, statements\n1376\t  fall −2 at the end, ALL-CAPS words +2 and louder.\n1377\t- The voice is monophonic per speaker: a new syllable cuts the previous one. A lowpass at 3.5 kHz on the bus softens\n1378\t  it.\n1379\t- Build the nodes on `game.audio.ctx` (null until the first key press or click, and always null headless: then plan\n1380\t  only). For `pulse` and `pulse12` waves, reuse the engine's PeriodicWave (`audio._pulse(.25)`, `audio._pulse(.125)`).\n1381\t  For noise, reuse `audio._noise`. Connect to the `voices` bus (E6).\n1382\t\n1383\t**Speaker profiles** (`{ base Hz, rate syl/s, wave, formant, breath, style }`):\n1384\t\n1385\t| Speaker | Profile |\n1386\t|---|---|\n1387\t| CHET THUNDERBUNS | 125, 13, saw, 0.95, 0.05, simlish, excited contours |\n1388\t| LOU DIGGS | 105, 9, triangle, 0.9, 0.08, simlish, falling contours |\n1389\t| COACH GUS BLUSTER | 140, 14, square, 1.0, 0.15, animalese, shouty |\n1390\t| MAMA PEARL | 210, 10, triangle, 1.15, 0.05, animalese, warm |\n1391\t| HAP HAZARD | 165, 12, saw, 1.05, 0.03, animalese |\n1392\t| BROCK STERLING III | 150, 11, pulse, 1.0, 0.02, animalese, smug (rise then fall) |\n1393\t| MONTGOMERY STERLING II | 115, 8, saw, 0.92, 0.06, animalese, pompous |\n1394\t| BIG BERTHA | 190, 9, square, 1.1, 0.1, animalese |\n1395\t| GATOR GUIDRY | 120, 10, saw, 0.95, 0.12, animalese |\n1396\t| LUMEN LOPEZ | 140, 11, pulse, 1.0, 0.02, animalese |\n1397\t| ZAP ZAPATA | 190, 16, pulse12, 1.1, 0.0, animalese |\n1398\t| DJ HOOT | 130, 12, pulse, 1.0, 0.04, animalese, vibrato |\n1399\t| COACH ICEBERG | 100, 6, sine, 0.85, 0.05, animalese, slow and solemn |\n1400\t| AVALANCHE | growls only: lowpass noise + a 70 Hz sine, no syllables |\n1401\t| THE MOUNTAIN | 90, 7, square, 0.8, 0.1, animalese |\n1402\t| refs | 150, 12, square, 1.0, 0.0, animalese, short |\n1403\t| QBs | the QB's own profile, cadence \"SET... HUT!\" (2–4 syllables + a strong plosive \"HUT\" on the snap) |\n1404\t| crowd chant | 6 voices, ±15 cents detuned, simlish |\n1405\tVoices are on whenever text is spoken: subtitles always show. Settings: Voices volume (the `voices` bus), Commentary\n1406\t(On / Subtitles only / Off). Headless, the synth schedules nothing and returns the plan, so tests can check that\n1407\tsyllables were planned.\n1408\t\n1409\t---\n1410\t\n1411\t## 14. Screens and UX (10-foot, controller-first)\n1412\t\n1413\t### 14.1 Rules for every screen\n1414\t- **Text size** on the 480×270 / 427×240 canvas: everything the player must read is `E.font` scale 2 (14 px glyphs,\n1415\t  56–84 px on a TV). Secondary text is scale 1 with a shadow. Titles are scale 3–5. `font: 'tiny'` only for jersey\n1416\t  numbers, signs and dev overlays.\n1417\t- **Few, big things:** at most 6–7 focusable items on a screen, one primary action highlighted, big cards, and\n1418\t  generous spacing. Focus shows as a pulsing border plus the `▸` marker. Results have at most 4 stat tiles, team\n1419\t  select 4 bars, records 6 rows a page. No tables of numbers outside the Dev mode.\n1420\t- **Navigation:** d-pad and stick with repeat (`input.repeat`); confirm and back; mouse hover moves the focus and a\n1421\t  click selects; the wheel scrolls lists. Every screen has a way back (○, Esc or the on-screen BACK).\n1422\t- **The prompt bar:** every screen's bottom edge shows its actions as chips for the current device (§9.3).\n1423\t- **Safe margins:** HUD and menus stay 8 px in from the edges (`T.safeMargin`, TV overscan) and clear of\n1424\t  `game.cornerArea()`.\n1425\t- **Contrast:** text over the field sits on dark translucent panels (`E.ui.box`, alpha 0.85) or has an outline.\n1426\t- **The HTML screens** (pause, settings, controls, help, dev) use the engine Shell with the 10-foot scale (E9: body\n1427\t  text ≥ 22 px at 1080p, buttons ≥ 56 px tall). Theme: `{ ink: '#f4f0e6', paper: 'rgba(14,16,34,.92)', accent:\n1428\t  '#ffb02e', muted: '#a9a6c0', danger: '#ff6a5a', line: 'rgba(255,176,46,.35)', font: 'system-ui, sans-serif',\n1429\t  titleFont: '\"Arial Black\", Impact, system-ui, sans-serif' }`: a sports-broadcast look.\n1430\t- **Every screen works with keyboard alone, pad alone, and mouse plus keyboard.** Tests drive them all three ways\n1431\t  (§21.3).\n1432\t\n1433\t### 14.2 Title\n1434\t- Tumbleweed Field at dusk in the broadcast view. Two lines of players face each other at midfield in stance, Fumbles\n1435\t  dances, the crowd sways. Every 6–8 s a scripted gag plays (Hap throws, a lineman catches it with his face; the\n1436\t  kicker whiffs; Fumbles catches fire).\n1437\t- The logo animates in (§12.8). \"PRESS START\" pulses with chips. Before any input, show both chips (Enter and ✕);\n1438\t  after that, the device's. The version label (`E.versionLabel()` + the game's version) is small at the bottom left.\n1439\t- 10 s idle starts the attract mode (§15.4). Touch-only devices: §14.12.\n1440\t\n1441\t### 14.3 Main menu\n1442\tSTORY: THE FIASCO CUP (Continue, New Game), EXHIBITION, PRACTICE, HALL OF FIASCO, OPTIONS (opens\n1443\t`game.menu('settings')`), ABOUT & CREDITS. A big vertical list on the left. On the right, a live vignette for the\n1444\tfocused item: the bracket board, two helmets clashing, a tackling dummy getting flattened, the trophy case, spinning\n1445\tgears, the announcers' booth. 10 s idle starts the attract mode.\n1446\t\n1447\t### 14.4 Exhibition setup (two steps)\n1448\t1. **CONTROLLERS & TEAMS.** Three columns: HOME (left), CPU (middle), AWAY (right). `game.allowJoin({ max: 4 })`:\n1449\t   Start on a free pad, or 2 on the keyboard (the right half), joins. Each player's device icon (a pad with P#, the\n1450\t   keyboard, or a keyboard half) starts in the middle. Left and right move it to a side. Up and down change that\n1451\t   side's team (the first human on a side chooses). The team panel shows the helmet (a portrait of a rig in that\n1452\t   helmet, turning slowly), the logo, the name, 4 rating bars, and the star player's portrait and special. ✕ readies.\n1453\t   A side with no human is the CPU, and P1 changes its team with △. When everyone is ready, go to step 2.\n1454\t2. **GAME OPTIONS.** Stadium (the home team's by default; arrows cycle with a preview), weather (Stadium / Clear /\n1455\t   Rain / Snow), quarter length, difficulty, then the big **PLAY BALL!** button.\n1456\tA coin toss starts the match. After the results: REMATCH, CHANGE TEAMS, MAIN MENU.\n1457\t\n1458\t### 14.5 The play-call screen (`53-playcall.js`)\n1459\t- **Layout:** a full-width panel when one side is human. With humans on both sides, split halves (home left, away\n1460\t  right), each player's choice hidden from the other: after picking, a panel turns its cards face down (\"READY\").\n1461\t  Co-op on one side: one panel with two cursors.\n1462\t- **The top bar:** the team logo, OFFENSE or DEFENSE, the down and distance, the ball spot, the play clock (big\n1463\t  digits, red under 4 s) and the team's Fiasco Meter.\n1464\t- **Tabs:** offense RUN | PASS | TRICK | SPECIAL (punt, field goal, fake punt, kneel). Defense BASE | PRESSURE |\n1465\t  SPECIAL (prevent, goal line, FG block). Kickoffs, PATs and returns show their own choices. L1/R1 or Q/E change the\n1466\t  tab; so does moving past the grid's edge, or a click on a tab.\n1467\t- **The grid:** 3×2 cards (§12.8). The focused card scales to 1.08. ✕ picks. □ flips (a FLIP badge, the routes\n1468\t  mirrored). The COACH SAYS card has a ★.\n1469\t- **The card row:** △ moves the focus to the 3 held Fiasco Cards, ✕ arms one (only one; greyed when it doesn't fit),\n1470\t  and ○ goes back to the grid.\n1471\t- **Co-op:** player 2's cursor picks his receiver (□ cycles).\n1472\t- **The timer:** when it runs out, the COACH SAYS play is picked.\n1473\t- **Behind:** the field, dimmed. The music is HUDDLE UP.\n1474\t\n1475\t### 14.6 The HUD (`41-hud.js`)\n1476\t- **The score bug** (bottom center, broadcast style, about 230×20): logo, abbreviation and score for each team, a\n1477\t  possession arrow, the quarter, the clock, the down and distance, and the ball spot. A thin Fiasco Meter bar under\n1478\t  each team, and flame icons for Blazing athletes. The scores flip on change.\n1479\t- **Player panels** for each local human, in their own corner (P1 top left, P2 top right, P3 bottom left above the\n1480\t  caption, P4 bottom right above the strip): the name tag, a big turbo bar (60×6), the held card count and SPECIAL\n1481\t  READY.\n1482\t- **The prompt strip** (§9.3), the caption (§11.3), center event text, the play clock in PRESNAP (from 5 s), and the\n1483\t  REPLAY overlay.\n1484\t- **In the world:** rings under held athletes; receiver chips with their glyphs; the pass target marker; the line of\n1485\t  scrimmage and first-down lines; the kick meter; tags; the down marker on the near sideline shows the down.\n1486\t- The HUD hides during replays (except the REPLAY overlay) and cutscenes.\n1487\t\n1488\t### 14.7 The kick meter\n1489\t- An arc meter (64×36 px) above the kicker in screen space. The power fill goes green, yellow, red. The accuracy\n1490\t  needle crosses a center band.\n1491\t- An aim line on the field: a dashed line from the ball along the aim, with the predicted landing marker for punts\n1492\t  and kickoffs. FGs show it in the Kick Cam with the posts in view.\n1493\t- Prompts step through ✕ KICK, ✕ SET POWER, ✕ SET AIM.\n1494\t\n1495\t### 14.8 Results\n1496\t- FINAL, both logos and scores huge, a winner banner.\n1497\t- PLAYER OF THE GAME: a portrait, his name and 2 key stats.\n1498\t- 4 stat tiles: total yards, turnovers, biggest hit (launch in yards), longest play.\n1499\t- Buttons: WATCH HIGHLIGHTS, then CONTINUE (story), or REMATCH / MAIN MENU (exhibition). In a hub session, the\n1500\t  results stay up under the hub's own results overlay.\n1501\t\n1502\t### 14.9 Hall of Fiasco (records)\n1503\t- `E.store('ff:records')`, 6 per page: longest TD, longest FG, biggest hit, most points in a game, most sacks in a\n1504\t  game, the fastest Fiasco Cup, and each chapter's stars.\n1505\t- Each row shows the team logo, the player, the value and the date.\n1506\t- Updated after exhibition and story games. Never written in hub sessions or the attract mode.\n1507\t\n1508\t### 14.10 About & Credits\n1509\tPages turned with ←/→ (L1/R1, clicks on the arrows), big text, scrolled with up/down when long:\n1510\t1. SOURCE INFORMATION: every field of TASK.md's list.\n1511\t2. TESTING FEEDBACK: the 4 answers.\n1512\t3. ENGINE FEEDBACK: the 6 answers.\n1513\t4. PROMPT FEEDBACK: the 4 answers.\n1514\t5. CREDITS: the engine my-3D2dge (MIT, michaelcrosato), the AI Hub client, motion clips (Quaternius CC0, Mesh2Motion\n1515\t   CC0, the CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database), store props (Kenney CC0), and who built it and from what\n1516\t   (`PLAN.md`).\n1517\t6. ENGINE CHANGES: the summary from ENGINE-CHANGES.md.\n1518\t\n1519\tAll of it comes from `window.FF_ABOUT` (§23). Never type these texts in two places.\n1520\t\n1521\t### 14.11 Settings\n1522\tThe game's own (group `Game`, through `menu.settings`): Difficulty (Rookie / Pro / Fiasco; Pro), Quarter length\n1523\t(1:00 / 1:30 / 2:00 / 3:00 / 5:00; 2:00), Camera (Broadcast / Sky Cam / Blimp), Replays (All big plays / Touchdowns\n1524\tonly / Off), Commentary (On / Subtitles only / Off), Voices (slider, 0.8), Crowd (slider, 0.7), Auto-switch on\n1525\tdefense (On), Show routes (On: your receivers' route lines while you're the QB), Pass target marker (On), Late hits\n1526\t(On), Big Heads (Off; locked until the story is finished, or unlocked in the Dev mode).\n1527\tPlus the engine's: Display (full screen, pixel scaling, the screen filter: Clean / Scanlines / CRT), Sound, Comfort\n1528\t(reduce motion, screen shake, flashes), and **Controller: Button symbols (PlayStation / Xbox; PlayStation)** (E2).\n1529\tEverything applies live. The Controls screen (engine) rebinds every action per player.\n1530\t\n1531\t### 14.12 Touch-only devices\n1532\t- **Detection:** `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')` matches, `(any-pointer: fine)` doesn't, `navigator.maxTouchPoints`\n1533\t  > 0, no gamepad is connected, and no key has been pressed.\n1534\t- **Then:** turn the touch controls off (`game.input.touchEnabled = false`, the Touch setting hidden, no scene\n1535\t  declares `touch` buttons). The title replaces PRESS START with **CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED** and a big\n1536\t  **SETTINGS** button (a tap calls `game.menu('settings')`). The corner's menu button stays. The attract mode runs\n1537\t  after 10 s as usual, and a tap goes back to the title.\n1538\t- **Unlock** the game the moment a gamepad connects (`gamepadconnected`, or `input.lastDevice === 'gamepad'`) or a key\n1539\t  is pressed.\n1540\t- In a hub session on such a device, the card says the same, and that seat is played by the AI until a controller or\n1541\t  keyboard input arrives. Don't call `AIHub.fail`, because from a host it would void the round.\n1542\t\n1543\t### 14.13 The pause menu\n1544\tResume (engine), then the game's items: Dev Mode, Restart (exhibition and practice). Then the engine's Settings,\n1545\tControls, Full screen, Help, and \"Quit to menu\" (made by `menu.quit: 'menu'`; don't add a quit item of your own).\n1546\tIn story mode, Quit to menu returns to the story board. Help comes from our Shell's `screens.help`: the\n1547\tcontrols by context in short sections (Offense, Ball carrier, Defense, Kicking, Menus), each line a key and what it\n1548\tdoes, for the device last used. Cutscenes aren't pausable: hold ○ or Esc for 1 s (a fill ring) to skip one.\n1549\t\n1550\t---\n1551\t\n1552\t## 15. Modes\n1553\t\n1554\t### 15.1 Story: THE FIASCO CUP (`54-scene-story.js`, `14-data-story.js`)\n1555\t**The hub** is the bracket board, a corkboard in the Fiascos' locker room. It holds 5 chapter cards, each locked,\n1556\topen or done with 0–3 stars. Below them sit the Fiasco Card collection and the **loadout**: up to 3 cards picked for\n1557\tthe next chapter. CONTINUE plays the next chapter. A chapter runs: intro cutscene → gameplay (a scenario) → halftime\n1558\tcutscene (chapters 2 and 5) → outro cutscene on a win, or the loss screen → reward → autosave\n1559\t(`game.saves.autosave()`, with the place, the chapter and the time played). Main menu CONTINUE loads\n1560\t`game.saves.latest()`. Wire the slots once at boot:\n1561\t`game.saves.write = () => ({ data: { story: story.state(), done, stars, collection, loadout, unlocked, playTime },\n1562\tplace: 'THE FIASCO CUP', level: nextChapter })` and `game.saves.read = s => restoreStory(s.data)`, with\n1563\t`menu: { saves: { version: 1 } }` so a future version can `migrate`. Records and settings live in `E.store`, not in\n1564\tthe slots.\n1565\t\n1566\t| # | Chapter | Stadium | Opponent | Scenario | Win condition | Shows | Reward |\n1567\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1568\t| 0 | PROLOGUE | Tumbleweed, night | — | a cutscene | — | the stakes | — |\n1569\t| 1 | TRYOUTS | Tumbleweed, dusk | the Scrubs | drills D1–D9 (§15.2) | finish D1–D8; D9 scored | every control | HOT SAUCE, SUPER FOOT |\n1570\t| 2 | THE MUD BOWL | Hog Wallow (rain, mud) | Mudhogs | a full game, 4 × 1:30 | win | run defense, tackling, fumbles, weather, halftime choice | MEGA HIT |\n1571\t| 3 | LIGHTS OUT | Afterglow (night) | Nite Owls | from the start of Q3, 1:30 quarters, trailing 7–21, Owls kick off | win | passing, pass defense, Hot Streak, the LIGHTS OUT event at the 4th play of Q3 | ROCKET CLEATS, GLUE GLOVES |\n1572\t| 4 | FROSTBITE | Frostbite (snow, ice) | Yetis | Q4 with 1:30 left, trailing 17–20, your ball 1st & 20 at your 20 | win (a FG ties: sudden death OT) | the two-minute drill, sidelines, the clock, laterals, ice, Snowplow | MASCOT MAYHEM |\n1573\t| 5 | THE FIASCO BOWL | Mega Dome | Dynasty | a full game, 4 × 2:00 | win | everything, both bosses, the halftime show | the trophy, the ending, the credits, Big Heads |\n1574\t\n1575\t- The collection starts with BRICK WALL and BUTTERFINGERS.\n1576\t- **Difficulty** per chapter: ch2 Rookie+, ch3 Pro−, ch4 Pro, ch5 Pro+ (a blend of the §8.4 columns), shifted one\n1577\t  step by the Difficulty setting.\n1578\t- **Stars:** 1 for the win, +1 for the bonus (ch2: force 2 fumbles; ch3: win by 7+; ch4: score with 20+ s left; ch5:\n1579\t  hold the Dynasty to 14 or fewer), +1 for no turnovers.\n1580\t- **Loss:** a \"THAT'S A FIASCO!\" screen with the coach's loss line and RETRY, RETRY EASIER (one step lower for this\n1581\t  chapter) or STORY MENU.\n1582\t\n1583\t**Cutscenes.** A cutscene is `{ set, stadium, cast: [{ who, at: [x, y], facing, pose }], camera: { view, focus,\n1584\tzoom }, node }`. Its node is an `E.Story` node list. `event` steps stage it: move an actor (a tween), set a pose or\n1585\tmocap clip, play an sfx, FX, a camera tween, a wait. The dialog is an `E.Dialog` with a live portrait of the speaker's\n1586\trig and `voice: ch => FF.voice.letter(ch, profile)` (E5). Hold ○ or Esc to skip to the end, keeping flags and\n1587\trewards. Sets are small TileMaps in the `field` view, built in code:\n1588\t- **LOCKER ROOM:** a row of lockers, benches, the chalkboard, the cooler and a team banner, a flickering lamp\n1589\t  (light). It is recolored for each team.\n1590\t- **OFFICE:** Mama Pearl's Pickle Barn: pickle barrels, a desk, a framed photo of the 1974 team, a lamp.\n1591\t- **PRESS ROOM:** the podium with mics, a backdrop wall painted with logos, chairs, TV cameras, camera flashes\n1592\t  (`game.flash` at 0.1 strength, honoring the flashes setting).\n1593\t- **FIELD:** the match stadium itself at midfield, with the trophy stage for the ending.\n1594\tThe lines are in §18.6.\n1595\t\n1596\t### 15.2 Tutorial and practice drills (`55-scene-drills.js`, `15-data-drills.js`)\n1597\t| Drill | Setup | Goal | Teaches |\n1598\t|---|---|---|---|\n1599\t| D1 RUN THE CONES | Hap at the 20, 5 cones zigzagging, a finish gate 15 yd past the last cone | pass within 1.5 yd of each cone in order and cross the gate within 9 s | move, turbo |\n1600\t| D2 HIKE & HANDOFF | offense, 3 dummies, HB DIVE called | hike, the RB takes the ball, gain 10 yd | hike, handoff, running |\n1601\t| D3 MOVES | the RB in a lane against 3 scrubs (a standing tackler, a frontal tackler, a diver), the goal line at 25 yd | beat each with the right move, then dive into the end zone | spin, stiff arm, hurdle, dive |\n1602\t| D4 PASSING | QB, 3 receivers on SLANTS, 2 slow defenders | complete 2 passes, then a Rocket Pass to the covered man | receiver buttons, Rocket Pass |\n1603\t| D5 CATCHING | you are Wheels (WR); the coach lobs high balls | catch 2 of 3 with a jump | jump catch, the target marker |\n1604\t| D6 DEFENSE | defense against a scrub runner, then a scrub QB | switch to the nearest defender and tackle; Big Hit to force a fumble and recover it; intercept a pass with a jump | switch, tackle, Big Hit, fumble recovery, INT |\n1605\t| D7 KICKING | a 37-yd FG, then a kickoff | make the FG; kick off 50+ yd | the meter, the Kick Cam |\n1606\t| D8 PLAY CALL | the play-call screen, HOT SAUCE given | pick a PASS play, flip it, use HOT SAUCE, run it Blazing | play calling, cards, Hot Streak |\n1607\t| D9 SCRIMMAGE | one drive against the Scrubs from your 30 | score a TD in 4 downs | all of it together |\n1608\t- Each drill opens with a big instruction card (2 lines with chips) and Coach Bluster's line, and shows a progress\n1609\t  counter. Success gives a star burst and praise. A failure restarts at once (b2 also restarts). After 2 failures,\n1610\t  \"□ SKIP DRILL\" appears.\n1611\t- Every drill has a `bot(ctx)` that completes it through intents. The tests and the attract mode use it.\n1612\t- **PRACTICE** (main menu) offers a grid of the 9 drills, any of them replayable, with best times kept.\n1613\t\n1614\t### 15.3 Exhibition\n1615\tSetup (§14.4), the coin toss, the match, the results, then REMATCH, CHANGE TEAMS or MAIN MENU. 1–4 local humans in\n1616\tany split, or CPU vs CPU (no humans: a \"spectate\" exhibition; P1 can press Start to take over a side).\n1617\t\n1618\t### 15.4 The attract mode (`56-scene-attract.js`, `17-data-attract.js`)\n1619\t- **Trigger:** 10 s with no input on the title, the main menu or the exhibition setup, with no Shell screen open.\n1620\t  Input means: any action pressed by any player, a click, the pointer moving more than 6 px, the wheel, a touch, or a\n1621\t  gamepad axis past the dead zone.\n1622\t- **Exit:** any input goes back to the screen it came from with a quick fade, and that input is consumed.\n1623\t- **Content:** a looping director, about 100 s a cycle. Each segment is a scenario with forced play calls and the\n1624\t  cheats it needs (TASK.md allows the attract AI to cheat freely):\n1625\t\n1626\t| # | Segment | Where | Shows | Cheats |\n1627\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1628\t| 1 | Logo sting, 3 s | — | the title logo cracking | — |\n1629\t| 2 | Kickoff return, 8 s | Tumbleweed, dusk; Fiascos vs Mudhogs | the meter, a return with a spin and a stiff arm | returner god mode |\n1630\t| 3 | Play call, 3 s | same | the play-call screen, both cursors picking DEEP POST and COVER 2, HOT SAUCE armed | — |\n1631\t| 4 | Blazing TD, 10 s | same | a deep pass, a jump catch, flames, the TD, a dance, the replay (field and iso) | forceCatch, noTackle |\n1632\t| 5 | Mud fumble, 8 s | Hog Wallow, rain | Bertha's MUDSLIDE, a Big Hit fumble, a pile-up | forceFumble |\n1633\t| 6 | Kick Cam FG, 6 s | Hog Wallow | a 52-yd FG, DOINK off the upright and in | forced accuracy |\n1634\t| 7 | Pick six, 7 s | Afterglow, night | Zap's AFTERBURNER, an INT returned for a TD, a late hit, a ref flattened | forceINT |\n1635\t| 8 | Mascot Mayhem, 6 s | Afterglow | Hooty runs on and sacks the QB | — |\n1636\t| 9 | Lights out, 5 s | Afterglow | glowing uniforms in the dark | — |\n1637\t| 10 | Snowplow, 6 s | Frostbite, snow | Avalanche's SNOWPLOW sack, divots, breath puffs | — |\n1638\t| 11 | Story snippet, 6 s | the press room | Brock's \"pickles\" line with his babble voice | — |\n1639\t| 12 | Halftime show, 5 s | Mega Dome | cheerleaders, the band, pyro, the blimp | — |\n1640\t| 13 | Seismic Sack, 5 s | Mega Dome | The Mountain's slam and shockwave | — |\n1641\t| 14 | Champions, 5 s | Mega Dome | the trophy stage, confetti, the bucket dump | — |\n1642\t| 15 | Hall of Fiasco, 5 s | — | the records | — |\n1643\t| 16 | Title, 5 s | — | the title, then the loop again | — |\n1644\t\n1645\t- **The overlay:** DEMO PLAY at the top, PRESS ANY BUTTON pulsing at the bottom, the ARCADE ATTRACT music,\n1646\t  commentary on with voices at 60%. Nothing is saved and no records are written.\n1647\t- Both teams are played by the normal brains. The director only forces play calls, the listed outcomes and the story\n1648\t  snippet's camera. The attract mode runs the same on touch-only devices.\n1649\t\n1650\t---\n1651\t\n1652\t## 16. Multiplayer (`80-net.js`)\n1653\t\n1654\t### 16.1 How TASK.md's multiplayer line is met\n1655\t- **The game on its own:** full local multiplayer for 1–4 on one machine (pads and a shared keyboard), in exhibition.\n1656\t  Story and practice are single player.\n1657\t- **In AI Hub:** sessions of the AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in **shared-world** mode for 1–4 players, each on their\n1658\t  own device. One player plays against the CPU; 2–4 play head to head or 2-on-1 and 2-on-2 with CPU teammates. The\n1659\t  hub's relay only exists inside a session, so outside one the game is unaffected (`AIHub.active` is false) and plays\n1660\t  as above.\n1661\t\n1662\t### 16.2 The page head\n1663\t`session.js` goes right after `<meta charset>`, unmodified and first:\n1664\t```html\n1665\t<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n1666\t<script>/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 … (the whole file, unmodified) */</script>\n1667\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n1668\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n1669\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n1670\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n1671\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"6\">\n1672\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Outscore the other side over one half of arcade football\">\n1673\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD run · ✕/Space hike, dive, tackle · ✕○□△ or 1-4 throw · R2/Shift turbo\">\n1674\t<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\"><meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1–4\"><meta name=\"hub:source\" content=\"American football\">\n1675\t```\n1676\t\n1677\t### 16.3 A session, step by step (when `AIHub.active`)\n1678\t1. Boot skips the title, attract mode and menus. The boot steps build everything.\n1679\t2. `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If it returns `null`, play\n1680\t   as on its own.\n1681\t3. **The setup** comes from `AIHub.rng('setup')`, the same on every copy: a stadium (one of the 5), two different\n1682\t   teams (never the Scrubs), the stadium's weather. Seats map to sides: 0 home, 1 away, 2 home, 3 away. With one\n1683\t   player, seat 0 is home against a CPU away team.\n1684\t4. **The card scene** (`57-scene-hubcard.js`):\n1685\t   - It shows the two helmets facing off over the stadium backdrop, the team logos, the players by side in their seat\n1686\t     colors with ready ticks (`card.ready`), \"HOW TO WIN: OUTSCORE THEM OVER ONE HALF\", this device's controls as\n1687\t     chips, and the countdown (`card.left`; PAUSED while `card.paused`).\n1688\t   - **READY** (Enter, ✕ or a tap) calls `AIHub.answer('ready')`. **MORE TIME** (△, T or a tap) calls\n1689\t     `AIHub.answer('more')`; pressing again takes it back.\n1690\t   - It has no menus or choices, and nothing on it changes the round. Any randomness comes from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n1691\t   - Call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as the match is built, without a key press.\n1692\t5. On `start`, show a 3-2-1 countdown over the opening kickoff setup while `AIHub.time() < 0`. Kick off at ≥ 0.\n1693\t6. **The match** is one half: 2 quarters of 1:30. A play takes about 17 s of real time for about 16 s of game clock\n1694\t   (live play plus the runoff), plus about 8 s per TD celebration, so plan on 1.3 real seconds per clock second. When\n1695\t   `info.limitMs` is short, use `quarter = clamp((limitMs / 1000 − 60) / 2 / 1.3, 45, 90)` seconds (a 300 s limit\n1696\t   gives 90; a 200 s limit gives 54). No overtime: a tie is a tie.\n1697\t7. At the end of Q2, or on `time-up` (within `graceMs`), the host calls\n1698\t   `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })` and sends a last reliable snapshot with `over: 1`. Every copy\n1699\t   shows the final score (§14.8) until `end`.\n1700\t8. On `end`: take no more input, send nothing, `audio.music(null)` and mute. `reason` picks the message: finished,\n1701\t   ROUND CANCELLED (void, host-left) or YOU SAT THIS ONE OUT (sat-out).\n1702\t\n1703\t### 16.4 Roles\n1704\t- **Host** (`info.isHost`): runs the sim, the AI and the rules for every seat. Its own seat, if any, plays locally\n1705\t  with no prediction needed.\n1706\t- **Others:** predict their own held athlete, render snapshots, and run their local UI (the play call and the kick\n1707\t  meter).\n1708\t- **Server** (`info.server`): a host with no player of its own. It runs the same host code with every seat remote,\n1709\t  draws nothing (`draw` fills the screen once and returns), plays no audio, and owns no camera or input.\n1710\t- **Control** (§9.4) is keyed by seat. The host owns the assignment and broadcasts changes as events.\n1711\t\n1712\t### 16.5 Messages, rates, prediction (formats in Appendix B)\n1713\t- Client → host: `i`, its state and inputs, unreliable at 15 Hz. `call`, its play call, reliable. `kick`, its kick\n1714\t  meter result, reliable.\n1715\t- Host → all: `s`, the snapshot, unreliable at **14 Hz**, **at most 1,100 bytes** (under the hub's ~1,200\n1716\t  fragmentation size). `e`, events, reliable, at most 4/s: phase changes with the plays, control changes, scores,\n1717\t  stats, card draws, `over`. One `send()` to everyone counts as one message.\n1718\t- **The budget:** each copy sends at most 18 messages/s. The host sends 14 + ≤ 4. A client sends 15 + about 1\n1719\t  reliable (`call` or `kick`). The hub allows 20/s with bursts of 40, and the client drops the rest. `FF.net.budget` is\n1720\t  a token bucket at 18/s that refuses sends past it: it drops the oldest queued unreliable message, never a reliable\n1721\t  one, and delays the next snapshot rather than skipping an event. Tests check this.\n1722\t- **Client prediction** (the arena example's rule: \"your controls never wait for the network\"):\n1723\t  - The client moves its held athlete locally with the same movement code, plus a soft push from the snapshot's\n1724\t    nearby athletes. It sends its position, velocity, facing, intent bits and an **action log**: the last 8 actions\n1725\t    with sequence numbers. The host runs each new sequence number once, so losing a packet loses nothing.\n1726\t  - The host accepts the reported position unless the athlete is `locked` (tackled, engaged, in an action the host\n1727\t    started, a dead ball) or it is farther than top speed × elapsed + 8 units from the host's last position.\n1728\t    Otherwise it keeps its own and flags `corr`.\n1729\t  - The client snaps to the host when the difference is over 2 yd, or `corr` or `locked` is set. While locked it\n1730\t    stops predicting.\n1731\t- **Interpolation:** others and the ball render 100 ms behind the newest snapshot, interpolated, extrapolated up to\n1732\t  150 ms when late.\n1733\t- **The play call:** each client opens its play-call UI on the host's `e: phase PLAYCALL` and sends `call`. The host\n1734\t  waits for every human side or its own timer, then sends `e: phase PRESNAP` with both plays.\n1735\t- **The kick meter** runs on the kicking human's copy. Its `{ power, acc, aim }` goes as `kick` and the host executes\n1736\t  it.\n1737\t- **Leaving:** on `leave { id }`, that seat's athletes go back to the AI (a CPU tag over them) and the match goes on.\n1738\t  When the host leaves, the hub voids the round and the clients show ROUND CANCELLED on `end`.\n1739\t\n1740\t### 16.6 Session rules (the protocol's, and what they mean here)\n1741\t- No title, menus, attract mode or story. No quit or restart (`menu.quit: false`, no Restart item, no Dev Mode item).\n1742\t- **No world freeze:** `AIHub.active` is known from the page's first line, so in a session the game is constructed\n1743\t  with `new E.Game({ autoPause: false, ... })` and the match scene is `pausable: false`. The match scene reads the\n1744\t  `pause` action itself: Options (or Esc) opens a small local canvas overlay with SETTINGS\n1745\t  (`game.menu('settings', { pause: false })`, E8) and CONTROLS. While it is open, that player's athlete is driven by\n1746\t  the AI.\n1747\t- **Create + Options is the hub's:** each step, while Pad8 (Create) is held on any pad, call\n1748\t  `input.suppress('pause')` and `input.suppress('start')`.\n1749\t- **No player-to-player communication:** celebrations are random, there are no taunts, and names come only from the\n1750\t  hub. They're drawn in the pixel font, where characters outside its set become `?`. Never insert them as HTML.\n1751\t- No replays, cutscenes or halftime show (one half has no halftime). Saves and records are never written.\n1752\t- `Math.random` isn't seeded in a shared world: the host's sim uses `FF.rng.sim` seeded from `AIHub.rng('match')`.\n1753\t  Clients don't run the sim.\n1754\t\n1755\t### 16.7 Results\n1756\t- **Standings** by team: the winners' ids, then the losers' (a tie puts everyone in one array).\n1757\t- **One player against the CPU:** `standings: [[0]], won: true | false`.\n1758\t- `scores`: each player's team score.\n1759\t- `stats` per id: `{ Yards, TDs, Tackles, Sacks }`.\n1760\t- `awards`: `[{ id, title: 'Player of the Game', detail }, { id, title: 'Biggest Hit', detail: '12-yard launch' }]`.\n1761\t\n1762\t---\n1763\t\n1764\t## 17. Dev mode (`70-dev.js`)\n1765\t- **Entry:** the pause menu's **Dev Mode** (never in hub sessions), the deep link `#dev`, and Backquote once Dev mode\n1766\t  has been opened in this visit.\n1767\t- **The Dev screens** are Shell screens (E7) with page buttons across the top: TUNING, CHEATS, JUMP TO, PLAY LAB,\n1768\t  OVERLAYS, TOOLS. Each page lists 6–10 rows. Back returns to the pause menu.\n1769\t- **TUNING:**\n1770\t  - Sub-pages Movement, Passing, Catching, Tackling, Blocking, Kicking, AI, Rules, Presentation.\n1771\t  - Every tunable in §22 is a live slider row (min, max, step, unit). The sim reads `FF.T` on every use, so a change\n1772\t    applies at once.\n1773\t  - **Reset this page** and **Reset all to defaults**.\n1774\t  - Values persist as `Dev …` settings, so a designer's tuning survives a reload.\n1775\t  - **Copy values** puts the current tuning as JSON on the clipboard, or shows it in a text panel where clipboard\n1776\t    access isn't allowed, to paste into `02-tuning.js`.\n1777\t- **CHEATS** (toggles): god mode (your carriers can't be tackled), infinite turbo, always catch, always intercept,\n1778\t  force a fumble on the next hit, no tackles by the CPU, CPU vs CPU (your side played by the AI), unlimited cards,\n1779\t  always Blazing, Big Heads, lights out, slow motion (0.25 / 0.5 / 1 / 2), freeze the clock, win now / lose now.\n1780\t- **JUMP TO:**\n1781\t  - Situations: 4th & goal at the 1, 3rd & 25, the last 0:10 trailing by 4, a kickoff, an onside kick, a 52-yd FG,\n1782\t    overtime, the red zone, backed up at your own 1.\n1783\t  - Any story chapter (start, halftime, outro), any cutscene, any drill, any stadium and weather.\n1784\t  - Set the score, the clock, the down and the distance with sliders, then Apply.\n1785\t  - Give a card, or set Blazing on the held athlete.\n1786\t  - Trigger: a Mega Hit on the next tackle, a fumble now, a replay of the last play, the TD celebration, the halftime\n1787\t    show, lights out, Mascot Mayhem, each boss special.\n1788\t- **PLAY LAB:**\n1789\t  - Choose an offensive play, a defensive play, the teams, the difficulty and n (10 / 30 / 100).\n1790\t  - RUN ON FIELD loops the matchup with overlays. RUN HEADLESS shows its stats (§8.6) and an all-defenses sweep for\n1791\t    the play. The dev screens are the one place a small table is fine.\n1792\t- **OVERLAYS:**\n1793\t  - AI debug: each athlete's behavior name, target lines, routes, zones as circles, man assignments, intercept\n1794\t    points, blocking pairs with shed timers.\n1795\t  - Hitboxes: `rig.debug(r)` skeletons plus body circles.\n1796\t  - The ball's predicted path and landing point; the camera target and bounds.\n1797\t  - FPS and ms per update and draw; the last 12 bus events; each player's device, stick vector and held actions.\n1798\t- **TOOLS:** frame step (the sim paused, b1 steps 1/120 s, b4 steps 0.1 s), a free camera (`cam.free`), HUD off for\n1799\t  clean screenshots, presentation off, record a session and Save session (`E.session`), reseed the RNG, reset save\n1800\t  data (asks first), unlock all (chapters, cards, Big Heads).\n1801\t- **Hotkeys while Dev mode is on:** Backquote toggles the overlays, `[` and `]` change the time scale, `\\` steps a\n1802\t  frame. Leave F5, F11 and F12 to the browser.\n1803\t\n1804\t---\n1805\t\n1806\t## 18. Content\n1807\t\n1808\t### 18.1 Teams and rosters (`10-data-teams.js`)\n1809\t**Base ratings by position** (1–10). A player is the base for his position, plus his team's modifier, plus his own\n1810\tline below (clamped 1–10):\n1811\t\n1812\t| Pos | SPD | ACC | STR | HND | TCK | ARM | AIM | AWR | KCK |\n1813\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1814\t| QB | 5 | 5 | 4 | 5 | 2 | 7 | 6 | 6 | 1 |\n1815\t| RB | 7 | 7 | 6 | 5 | 3 | 1 | 1 | 5 | 1 |\n1816\t| WR | 8 | 7 | 3 | 7 | 2 | 1 | 1 | 5 | 1 |\n1817\t| C, G | 2 | 3 | 7 | 3 | 3 | 1 | 1 | 5 | 1 |\n1818\t| DE | 5 | 5 | 6 | 3 | 6 | 1 | 1 | 5 | 1 |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49428dbe-779b-4248-8ac3-c582018d3c3d","uuid":"4722afa6-6663-43d1-a96a-b1bb4c3e5480","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:06:23.766Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-070556__xb697dc/work/PLAN.md","content":"|---|---|---|\n| FIASCO ANTHEM | the title, the story hub | stadium rock, 132 bpm: a square lead, saw bass, a `k . s .` beat, a cheer-like hook |\n| LOCKER ROOM FUNK | menus, setup | 110 bpm, a slap-bass `pulse12` line, offbeat hats |\n| HUDDLE UP | the play-call screen | a drumline loop (drums only plus a low triangle ostinato), 120 bpm, 2 bars, rising tension |\n| DUST DEVIL STOMP | Tumbleweed Field | a western shuffle, triangle bass, a twangy pulse lead, 128 bpm |\n| SWAMP STOMP | The Hog Wallow | a blues shuffle, saw bass, a harmonica-like pulse with vibrato, 96 bpm |\n| NEON NIGHTDRIVE | Afterglow Arena | synthwave, saw arpeggios, a square lead, 118 bpm |\n| FROSTBITE FANFARE | Frostbite Field | bells (triangle and sine arpeggios), 100 bpm |\n| MEGA DOME ANTHEM | the Mega Dome | epic brass (3 squares in fifths), 140 bpm |\n| HALFTIME SHOW | halftime | a marching band: `k s s` drums, a brass melody |\n| ARCADE ATTRACT | the attract mode | a 150 bpm remix of the anthem |\n| FIASCO FOREVER | the credits | a slow ballad version of the anthem |\n| Stings | `audio.sting` | TD fanfare, FG good, first-down organ riff, defense chant riff, Fiasco Break \"wah-wah\", victory jingle, defeat jingle (a sad sliding saw) |\n\nIn matches the stadium song plays low under the crowd bed, with layers `hot` (more drums and a guitar-like saw, for a\nBlazing athlete), `redzone` (bass pulses inside the 20) and `final` (`audio.tempo` +8% in the last minute). Between\nplays, original stadium-organ riffs (square and triangle chords with vibrato) play as stings on first downs, and a\ndefense-chant riff plays on 3rd down.\n\n### 13.2 Sound effects (`audio.define` each; the engine warns on unknown names, and a test fails on such a warning)\nhike (the QB's \"HUT\" voice + a snap thump), whistle, helmetClang (square 1800→1200 + a triangle ring), padsCrunch\n(lowpass noise 900→200 + sine 120→50), bigHit (crunch + clang + a boom sine 80→30), tackleThud, dive (whoosh),\nspinWhoosh, stiffArm (punch), hurdle (jump2), catchSlap (bandpass noise 1200, short), drop (thunk), throwWhoosh,\nrocketPass (a saw sweep), kickThump (sine 150→60 + noise), doink (a triangle 1400 ring), airHorn (3 saw voices\n220/277/330, 0.6 s), cannon (boom), fireworks (explode + crackle bursts), confettiPop, coinFlip (blip arpeggio),\ncardFlip, fiascoBreak (a descending arpeggio + wah), hotOn (a fire whoosh + a rising arpeggio), pileThumps, refCapPop,\nmascotSqueak, lightsOut (a power-down sweep), lightsOn (a thunk + hum), menuMove, menuSelect, menuBack, meterTick,\nmeterSet. Crowd one-shots: roar, boo, oooh, groan, gasp, cheer swell (bandpassed noise shapes on the crowd bus).\n\n### 13.3 The crowd bed\nA long-lived looping noise source on the `crowd` bus, through a bandpass (500–1500 Hz), with gain\n`0.12 + 0.38 × E` (E from §11.4), plus a lower \"murmur\" layer. Reactions are the one-shots above. Chants are 6\ndetuned babble voices in rhythm with the team's chant syllables (\"FI-AS-CO!\", \"HOGS! HOGS! HOGS!\", \"HOOT-HOOT!\",\n\"BRRR-BRRR!\", \"DY-NAS-TY!\"), on the beat (`audio.onBeat`) when E > 0.4. Stadium size scales it: Tumbleweed is thin\nand quiet (until the ending), the Mega Dome thick.\n\n### 13.4 Voices: the babble synth (Animalese and Simlish)\n**The API:** `FF.voice.say(text, profile, { onSyllable })` plans syllables, schedules them on the `voices` bus and\nreturns the plan. `FF.voice.letter(ch, profile)` is the E5 dialog hook, which groups typed letters into syllables\nlive. `FF.voice.stop(profile)`.\n\n**Two styles, one synth:**\n- **Animalese** (the story cast, refs, mascot noises): letter-driven. Each vowel group in the typed text is one\n  syllable, with its onset taken from the preceding consonant(s). Quick, high and cute.\n- **Simlish** (the announcers, coaches on the radio, the crowd chants): count the line's syllables, then speak that\n  many syllables drawn from a gibberish bank (`ba do zee ka fla nu ree bo shma gli va tor mip zub lo neh`), picked by\n  a hash of each real word so the same line sounds the same every time. More fluent, with less pitch jitter.\n\n**A syllable** = onset + nucleus:\n- **Onset** by consonant class: plosives (p b t d k g c q) are an 8 ms broadband noise click; fricatives (f s z v h\n  x, sh, th) are 25–40 ms of bandpassed or highpassed noise (s at 5 kHz, f at 3 kHz, h at 1.2 kHz); nasals (m n) are\n  30 ms of lowpassed voiced hum; liquids (l r w y) are a formant glide into the vowel.\n- **Nucleus:** an oscillator (the profile's wave) through two parallel bandpass filters at the vowel's formants\n  (a 800/1200, e 500/1900, i 320/2300, o 500/900, u 350/800 Hz, × the profile's formant scale; Q 6 and 10), with an\n  envelope of 6 ms attack, a sustain, and a 25 ms release. The duration is (1 / rate) × 0.6–1.0.\n- **Pitch** = base × 2^((jitter + contour) / 12). The jitter is ±2 semitones from a hash of the syllable, so it's\n  deterministic. The contour: questions rise +4 on the last 2 syllables, exclamations +3 and +30% volume, statements\n  fall −2 at the end, ALL-CAPS words +2 and louder.\n- The voice is monophonic per speaker: a new syllable cuts the previous one. A lowpass at 3.5 kHz on the bus softens\n  it.\n- Build the nodes on `game.audio.ctx` (null until the first key press or click, and always null headless: then plan\n  only). For `pulse` and `pulse12` waves, reuse the engine's PeriodicWave (`audio._pulse(.25)`, `audio._pulse(.125)`).\n  For noise, reuse `audio._noise`. Connect to the `voices` bus (E6).\n\n**Speaker profiles** (`{ base Hz, rate syl/s, wave, formant, breath, style }`):\n\n| Speaker | Profile |\n|---|---|\n| CHET THUNDERBUNS | 125, 13, saw, 0.95, 0.05, simlish, excited contours |\n| LOU DIGGS | 105, 9, triangle, 0.9, 0.08, simlish, falling contours |\n| COACH GUS BLUSTER | 140, 14, square, 1.0, 0.15, animalese, shouty |\n| MAMA PEARL | 210, 10, triangle, 1.15, 0.05, animalese, warm |\n| HAP HAZARD | 165, 12, saw, 1.05, 0.03, animalese |\n| BROCK STERLING III | 150, 11, pulse, 1.0, 0.02, animalese, smug (rise then fall) |\n| MONTGOMERY STERLING II | 115, 8, saw, 0.92, 0.06, animalese, pompous |\n| BIG BERTHA | 190, 9, square, 1.1, 0.1, animalese |\n| GATOR GUIDRY | 120, 10, saw, 0.95, 0.12, animalese |\n| LUMEN LOPEZ | 140, 11, pulse, 1.0, 0.02, animalese |\n| ZAP ZAPATA | 190, 16, pulse12, 1.1, 0.0, animalese |\n| DJ HOOT | 130, 12, pulse, 1.0, 0.04, animalese, vibrato |\n| COACH ICEBERG | 100, 6, sine, 0.85, 0.05, animalese, slow and solemn |\n| AVALANCHE | growls only: lowpass noise + a 70 Hz sine, no syllables |\n| THE MOUNTAIN | 90, 7, square, 0.8, 0.1, animalese |\n| refs | 150, 12, square, 1.0, 0.0, animalese, short |\n| QBs | the QB's own profile, cadence \"SET... HUT!\" (2–4 syllables + a strong plosive \"HUT\" on the snap) |\n| crowd chant | 6 voices, ±15 cents detuned, simlish |\nVoices are on whenever text is spoken: subtitles always show. Settings: Voices volume (the `voices` bus), Commentary\n(On / Subtitles only / Off). Headless, the synth schedules nothing and returns the plan, so tests can check that\nsyllables were planned.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Screens and UX (10-foot, controller-first)\n\n### 14.1 Rules for every screen\n- **Text size** on the 480×270 / 427×240 canvas: everything the player must read is `E.font` scale 2 (14 px glyphs,\n  56–84 px on a TV). Secondary text is scale 1 with a shadow. Titles are scale 3–5. `font: 'tiny'` only for jersey\n  numbers, signs and dev overlays.\n- **Few, big things:** at most 6–7 focusable items on a screen, one primary action highlighted, big cards, and\n  generous spacing. Focus shows as a pulsing border plus the `▸` marker. Results have at most 4 stat tiles, team\n  select 4 bars, records 6 rows a page. No tables of numbers outside the Dev mode.\n- **Navigation:** d-pad and stick with repeat (`input.repeat`); confirm and back; mouse hover moves the focus and a\n  click selects; the wheel scrolls lists. Every screen has a way back (○, Esc or the on-screen BACK).\n- **The prompt bar:** every screen's bottom edge shows its actions as chips for the current device (§9.3).\n- **Safe margins:** HUD and menus stay 8 px in from the edges (`T.safeMargin`, TV overscan) and clear of\n  `game.cornerArea()`.\n- **Contrast:** text over the field sits on dark translucent panels (`E.ui.box`, alpha 0.85) or has an outline.\n- **The HTML screens** (pause, settings, controls, help, dev) use the engine Shell with the 10-foot scale (E9: body\n  text ≥ 22 px at 1080p, buttons ≥ 56 px tall). Theme: `{ ink: '#f4f0e6', paper: 'rgba(14,16,34,.92)', accent:\n  '#ffb02e', muted: '#a9a6c0', danger: '#ff6a5a', line: 'rgba(255,176,46,.35)', font: 'system-ui, sans-serif',\n  titleFont: '\"Arial Black\", Impact, system-ui, sans-serif' }`: a sports-broadcast look.\n- **Every screen works with keyboard alone, pad alone, and mouse plus keyboard.** Tests drive them all three ways\n  (§21.3).\n\n### 14.2 Title\n- Tumbleweed Field at dusk in the broadcast view. Two lines of players face each other at midfield in stance, Fumbles\n  dances, the crowd sways. Every 6–8 s a scripted gag plays (Hap throws, a lineman catches it with his face; the\n  kicker whiffs; Fumbles catches fire).\n- The logo animates in (§12.8). \"PRESS START\" pulses with chips. Before any input, show both chips (Enter and ✕);\n  after that, the device's. The version label (`E.versionLabel()` + the game's version) is small at the bottom left.\n- 10 s idle starts the attract mode (§15.4). Touch-only devices: §14.12.\n\n### 14.3 Main menu\nSTORY: THE FIASCO CUP (Continue, New Game), EXHIBITION, PRACTICE, HALL OF FIASCO, OPTIONS (opens\n`game.menu('settings')`), ABOUT & CREDITS. A big vertical list on the left. On the right, a live vignette for the\nfocused item: the bracket board, two helmets clashing, a tackling dummy getting flattened, the trophy case, spinning\ngears, the announcers' booth. 10 s idle starts the attract mode.\n\n### 14.4 Exhibition setup (two steps)\n1. **CONTROLLERS & TEAMS.** Three columns: HOME (left), CPU (middle), AWAY (right). `game.allowJoin({ max: 4 })`:\n   Start on a free pad, or 2 on the keyboard (the right half), joins. Each player's device icon (a pad with P#, the\n   keyboard, or a keyboard half) starts in the middle. Left and right move it to a side. Up and down change that\n   side's team (the first human on a side chooses). The team panel shows the helmet (a portrait of a rig in that\n   helmet, turning slowly), the logo, the name, 4 rating bars, and the star player's portrait and special. ✕ readies.\n   A side with no human is the CPU, and P1 changes its team with △. When everyone is ready, go to step 2.\n2. **GAME OPTIONS.** Stadium (the home team's by default; arrows cycle with a preview), weather (Stadium / Clear /\n   Rain / Snow), quarter length, difficulty, then the big **PLAY BALL!** button.\nA coin toss starts the match. After the results: REMATCH, CHANGE TEAMS, MAIN MENU.\n\n### 14.5 The play-call screen (`53-playcall.js`)\n- **Layout:** a full-width panel when one side is human. With humans on both sides, split halves (home left, away\n  right), each player's choice hidden from the other: after picking, a panel turns its cards face down (\"READY\").\n  Co-op on one side: one panel with two cursors.\n- **The top bar:** the team logo, OFFENSE or DEFENSE, the down and distance, the ball spot, the play clock (big\n  digits, red under 4 s) and the team's Fiasco Meter.\n- **Tabs:** offense RUN | PASS | TRICK | SPECIAL (punt, field goal, fake punt, kneel). Defense BASE | PRESSURE |\n  SPECIAL (prevent, goal line, FG block). Kickoffs, PATs and returns show their own choices. L1/R1 or Q/E change the\n  tab; so does moving past the grid's edge, or a click on a tab.\n- **The grid:** 3×2 cards (§12.8). The focused card scales to 1.08. ✕ picks. □ flips (a FLIP badge, the routes\n  mirrored). The COACH SAYS card has a ★.\n- **The card row:** △ moves the focus to the 3 held Fiasco Cards, ✕ arms one (only one; greyed when it doesn't fit),\n  and ○ goes back to the grid.\n- **Co-op:** player 2's cursor picks his receiver (□ cycles).\n- **The timer:** when it runs out, the COACH SAYS play is picked.\n- **Behind:** the field, dimmed. The music is HUDDLE UP.\n\n### 14.6 The HUD (`41-hud.js`)\n- **The score bug** (bottom center, broadcast style, about 230×20): logo, abbreviation and score for each team, a\n  possession arrow, the quarter, the clock, the down and distance, and the ball spot. A thin Fiasco Meter bar under\n  each team, and flame icons for Blazing athletes. The scores flip on change.\n- **Player panels** for each local human, in their own corner (P1 top left, P2 top right, P3 bottom left above the\n  caption, P4 bottom right above the strip): the name tag, a big turbo bar (60×6), the held card count and SPECIAL\n  READY.\n- **The prompt strip** (§9.3), the caption (§11.3), center event text, the play clock in PRESNAP (from 5 s), and the\n  REPLAY overlay.\n- **In the world:** rings under held athletes; receiver chips with their glyphs; the pass target marker; the line of\n  scrimmage and first-down lines; the kick meter; tags; the down marker on the near sideline shows the down.\n- The HUD hides during replays (except the REPLAY overlay) and cutscenes.\n\n### 14.7 The kick meter\n- An arc meter (64×36 px) above the kicker in screen space. The power fill goes green, yellow, red. The accuracy\n  needle crosses a center band.\n- An aim line on the field: a dashed line from the ball along the aim, with the predicted landing marker for punts\n  and kickoffs. FGs show it in the Kick Cam with the posts in view.\n- Prompts step through ✕ KICK, ✕ SET POWER, ✕ SET AIM.\n\n### 14.8 Results\n- FINAL, both logos and scores huge, a winner banner.\n- PLAYER OF THE GAME: a portrait, his name and 2 key stats.\n- 4 stat tiles: total yards, turnovers, biggest hit (launch in yards), longest play.\n- Buttons: WATCH HIGHLIGHTS, then CONTINUE (story), or REMATCH / MAIN MENU (exhibition). In a hub session, the\n  results stay up under the hub's own results overlay.\n\n### 14.9 Hall of Fiasco (records)\n- `E.store('ff:records')`, 6 per page: longest TD, longest FG, biggest hit, most points in a game, most sacks in a\n  game, the fastest Fiasco Cup, and each chapter's stars.\n- Each row shows the team logo, the player, the value and the date.\n- Updated after exhibition and story games. Never written in hub sessions or the attract mode.\n\n### 14.10 About & Credits\nPages turned with ←/→ (L1/R1, clicks on the arrows), big text, scrolled with up/down when long:\n1. SOURCE INFORMATION: every field of TASK.md's list.\n2. TESTING FEEDBACK: the 4 answers.\n3. ENGINE FEEDBACK: the 6 answers.\n4. PROMPT FEEDBACK: the 4 answers.\n5. CREDITS: the engine my-3D2dge (MIT, michaelcrosato), the AI Hub client, motion clips (Quaternius CC0, Mesh2Motion\n   CC0, the CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database), store props (Kenney CC0), and who built it and from what\n   (`PLAN.md`).\n6. ENGINE CHANGES: the summary from ENGINE-CHANGES.md.\n\nAll of it comes from `window.FF_ABOUT` (§23). Never type these texts in two places.\n\n### 14.11 Settings\nThe game's own (group `Game`, through `menu.settings`): Difficulty (Rookie / Pro / Fiasco; Pro), Quarter length\n(1:00 / 1:30 / 2:00 / 3:00 / 5:00; 2:00), Camera (Broadcast / Sky Cam / Blimp), Replays (All big plays / Touchdowns\nonly / Off), Commentary (On / Subtitles only / Off), Voices (slider, 0.8), Crowd (slider, 0.7), Auto-switch on\ndefense (On), Show routes (On: your receivers' route lines while you're the QB), Pass target marker (On), Late hits\n(On), Big Heads (Off; locked until the story is finished, or unlocked in the Dev mode).\nPlus the engine's: Display (full screen, pixel scaling, the screen filter: Clean / Scanlines / CRT), Sound, Comfort\n(reduce motion, screen shake, flashes), and **Controller: Button symbols (PlayStation / Xbox; PlayStation)** (E2).\nEverything applies live. The Controls screen (engine) rebinds every action per player.\n\n### 14.12 Touch-only devices\n- **Detection:** `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')` matches, `(any-pointer: fine)` doesn't, `navigator.maxTouchPoints`\n  > 0, no gamepad is connected, and no key has been pressed.\n- **Then:** turn the touch controls off (`game.input.touchEnabled = false`, the Touch setting hidden, no scene\n  declares `touch` buttons). The title replaces PRESS START with **CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED** and a big\n  **SETTINGS** button (a tap calls `game.menu('settings')`). The corner's menu button stays. The attract mode runs\n  after 10 s as usual, and a tap goes back to the title.\n- **Unlock** the game the moment a gamepad connects (`gamepadconnected`, or `input.lastDevice === 'gamepad'`) or a key\n  is pressed.\n- In a hub session on such a device, the card says the same, and that seat is played by the AI until a controller or\n  keyboard input arrives. Don't call `AIHub.fail`, because from a host it would void the round.\n\n### 14.13 The pause menu\nResume (engine), then the game's items: Dev Mode, Restart (exhibition and practice). Then the engine's Settings,\nControls, Full screen, Help, and \"Quit to menu\" (made by `menu.quit: 'menu'`; don't add a quit item of your own).\nIn story mode, Quit to menu returns to the story board. Help comes from our Shell's `screens.help`: the\ncontrols by context in short sections (Offense, Ball carrier, Defense, Kicking, Menus), each line a key and what it\ndoes, for the device last used. Cutscenes aren't pausable: hold ○ or Esc for 1 s (a fill ring) to skip one.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Modes\n\n### 15.1 Story: THE FIASCO CUP (`54-scene-story.js`, `14-data-story.js`)\n**The hub** is the bracket board, a corkboard in the Fiascos' locker room. It holds 5 chapter cards, each locked,\nopen or done with 0–3 stars. Below them sit the Fiasco Card collection and the **loadout**: up to 3 cards picked for\nthe next chapter. CONTINUE plays the next chapter. A chapter runs: intro cutscene → gameplay (a scenario) → halftime\ncutscene (chapters 2 and 5) → outro cutscene on a win, or the loss screen → reward → autosave\n(`game.saves.autosave()`, with the place, the chapter and the time played). Main menu CONTINUE loads\n`game.saves.latest()`. Wire the slots once at boot:\n`game.saves.write = () => ({ data: { story: story.state(), done, stars, collection, loadout, unlocked, playTime },\nplace: 'THE FIASCO CUP', level: nextChapter })` and `game.saves.read = s => restoreStory(s.data)`, with\n`menu: { saves: { version: 1 } }` so a future version can `migrate`. Records and settings live in `E.store`, not in\nthe slots.\n\n| # | Chapter | Stadium | Opponent | Scenario | Win condition | Shows | Reward |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | PROLOGUE | Tumbleweed, night | — | a cutscene | — | the stakes | — |\n| 1 | TRYOUTS | Tumbleweed, dusk | the Scrubs | drills D1–D9 (§15.2) | finish D1–D8; D9 scored | every control | HOT SAUCE, SUPER FOOT |\n| 2 | THE MUD BOWL | Hog Wallow (rain, mud) | Mudhogs | a full game, 4 × 1:30 | win | run defense, tackling, fumbles, weather, halftime choice | MEGA HIT |\n| 3 | LIGHTS OUT | Afterglow (night) | Nite Owls | from the start of Q3, 1:30 quarters, trailing 7–21, Owls kick off | win | passing, pass defense, Hot Streak, the LIGHTS OUT event at the 4th play of Q3 | ROCKET CLEATS, GLUE GLOVES |\n| 4 | FROSTBITE | Frostbite (snow, ice) | Yetis | Q4 with 1:30 left, trailing 17–20, your ball 1st & 20 at your 20 | win (a FG ties: sudden death OT) | the two-minute drill, sidelines, the clock, laterals, ice, Snowplow | MASCOT MAYHEM |\n| 5 | THE FIASCO BOWL | Mega Dome | Dynasty | a full game, 4 × 2:00 | win | everything, both bosses, the halftime show | the trophy, the ending, the credits, Big Heads |\n\n- The collection starts with BRICK WALL and BUTTERFINGERS.\n- **Difficulty** per chapter: ch2 Rookie+, ch3 Pro−, ch4 Pro, ch5 Pro+ (a blend of the §8.4 columns), shifted one\n  step by the Difficulty setting.\n- **Stars:** 1 for the win, +1 for the bonus (ch2: force 2 fumbles; ch3: win by 7+; ch4: score with 20+ s left; ch5:\n  hold the Dynasty to 14 or fewer), +1 for no turnovers.\n- **Loss:** a \"THAT'S A FIASCO!\" screen with the coach's loss line and RETRY, RETRY EASIER (one step lower for this\n  chapter) or STORY MENU.\n\n**Cutscenes.** A cutscene is `{ set, stadium, cast: [{ who, at: [x, y], facing, pose }], camera: { view, focus,\nzoom }, node }`. Its node is an `E.Story` node list. `event` steps stage it: move an actor (a tween), set a pose or\nmocap clip, play an sfx, FX, a camera tween, a wait. The dialog is an `E.Dialog` with a live portrait of the speaker's\nrig and `voice: ch => FF.voice.letter(ch, profile)` (E5). Hold ○ or Esc to skip to the end, keeping flags and\nrewards. Sets are small TileMaps in the `field` view, built in code:\n- **LOCKER ROOM:** a row of lockers, benches, the chalkboard, the cooler and a team banner, a flickering lamp\n  (light). It is recolored for each team.\n- **OFFICE:** Mama Pearl's Pickle Barn: pickle barrels, a desk, a framed photo of the 1974 team, a lamp.\n- **PRESS ROOM:** the podium with mics, a backdrop wall painted with logos, chairs, TV cameras, camera flashes\n  (`game.flash` at 0.1 strength, honoring the flashes setting).\n- **FIELD:** the match stadium itself at midfield, with the trophy stage for the ending.\nThe lines are in §18.6.\n\n### 15.2 Tutorial and practice drills (`55-scene-drills.js`, `15-data-drills.js`)\n| Drill | Setup | Goal | Teaches |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| D1 RUN THE CONES | Hap at the 20, 5 cones zigzagging, a finish gate 15 yd past the last cone | pass within 1.5 yd of each cone in order and cross the gate within 9 s | move, turbo |\n| D2 HIKE & HANDOFF | offense, 3 dummies, HB DIVE called | hike, the RB takes the ball, gain 10 yd | hike, handoff, running |\n| D3 MOVES | the RB in a lane against 3 scrubs (a standing tackler, a frontal tackler, a diver), the goal line at 25 yd | beat each with the right move, then dive into the end zone | spin, stiff arm, hurdle, dive |\n| D4 PASSING | QB, 3 receivers on SLANTS, 2 slow defenders | complete 2 passes, then a Rocket Pass to the covered man | receiver buttons, Rocket Pass |\n| D5 CATCHING | you are Wheels (WR); the coach lobs high balls | catch 2 of 3 with a jump | jump catch, the target marker |\n| D6 DEFENSE | defense against a scrub runner, then a scrub QB | switch to the nearest defender and tackle; Big Hit to force a fumble and recover it; intercept a pass with a jump | switch, tackle, Big Hit, fumble recovery, INT |\n| D7 KICKING | a 37-yd FG, then a kickoff | make the FG; kick off 50+ yd | the meter, the Kick Cam |\n| D8 PLAY CALL | the play-call screen, HOT SAUCE given | pick a PASS play, flip it, use HOT SAUCE, run it Blazing | play calling, cards, Hot Streak |\n| D9 SCRIMMAGE | one drive against the Scrubs from your 30 | score a TD in 4 downs | all of it together |\n- Each drill opens with a big instruction card (2 lines with chips) and Coach Bluster's line, and shows a progress\n  counter. Success gives a star burst and praise. A failure restarts at once (b2 also restarts). After 2 failures,\n  \"□ SKIP DRILL\" appears.\n- Every drill has a `bot(ctx)` that completes it through intents. The tests and the attract mode use it.\n- **PRACTICE** (main menu) offers a grid of the 9 drills, any of them replayable, with best times kept.\n\n### 15.3 Exhibition\nSetup (§14.4), the coin toss, the match, the results, then REMATCH, CHANGE TEAMS or MAIN MENU. 1–4 local humans in\nany split, or CPU vs CPU (no humans: a \"spectate\" exhibition; P1 can press Start to take over a side).\n\n### 15.4 The attract mode (`56-scene-attract.js`, `17-data-attract.js`)\n- **Trigger:** 10 s with no input on the title, the main menu or the exhibition setup, with no Shell screen open.\n  Input means: any action pressed by any player, a click, the pointer moving more than 6 px, the wheel, a touch, or a\n  gamepad axis past the dead zone.\n- **Exit:** any input goes back to the screen it came from with a quick fade, and that input is consumed.\n- **Content:** a looping director, about 100 s a cycle. Each segment is a scenario with forced play calls and the\n  cheats it needs (TASK.md allows the attract AI to cheat freely):\n\n| # | Segment | Where | Shows | Cheats |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Logo sting, 3 s | — | the title logo cracking | — |\n| 2 | Kickoff return, 8 s | Tumbleweed, dusk; Fiascos vs Mudhogs | the meter, a return with a spin and a stiff arm | returner god mode |\n| 3 | Play call, 3 s | same | the play-call screen, both cursors picking DEEP POST and COVER 2, HOT SAUCE armed | — |\n| 4 | Blazing TD, 10 s | same | a deep pass, a jump catch, flames, the TD, a dance, the replay (field and iso) | forceCatch, noTackle |\n| 5 | Mud fumble, 8 s | Hog Wallow, rain | Bertha's MUDSLIDE, a Big Hit fumble, a pile-up | forceFumble |\n| 6 | Kick Cam FG, 6 s | Hog Wallow | a 52-yd FG, DOINK off the upright and in | forced accuracy |\n| 7 | Pick six, 7 s | Afterglow, night | Zap's AFTERBURNER, an INT returned for a TD, a late hit, a ref flattened | forceINT |\n| 8 | Mascot Mayhem, 6 s | Afterglow | Hooty runs on and sacks the QB | — |\n| 9 | Lights out, 5 s | Afterglow | glowing uniforms in the dark | — |\n| 10 | Snowplow, 6 s | Frostbite, snow | Avalanche's SNOWPLOW sack, divots, breath puffs | — |\n| 11 | Story snippet, 6 s | the press room | Brock's \"pickles\" line with his babble voice | — |\n| 12 | Halftime show, 5 s | Mega Dome | cheerleaders, the band, pyro, the blimp | — |\n| 13 | Seismic Sack, 5 s | Mega Dome | The Mountain's slam and shockwave | — |\n| 14 | Champions, 5 s | Mega Dome | the trophy stage, confetti, the bucket dump | — |\n| 15 | Hall of Fiasco, 5 s | — | the records | — |\n| 16 | Title, 5 s | — | the title, then the loop again | — |\n\n- **The overlay:** DEMO PLAY at the top, PRESS ANY BUTTON pulsing at the bottom, the ARCADE ATTRACT music,\n  commentary on with voices at 60%. Nothing is saved and no records are written.\n- Both teams are played by the normal brains. The director only forces play calls, the listed outcomes and the story\n  snippet's camera. The attract mode runs the same on touch-only devices.\n\n---\n\n## 16. Multiplayer (`80-net.js`)\n\n### 16.1 How TASK.md's multiplayer line is met\n- **The game on its own:** full local multiplayer for 1–4 on one machine (pads and a shared keyboard), in exhibition.\n  Story and practice are single player.\n- **In AI Hub:** sessions of the AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in **shared-world** mode for 1–4 players, each on their\n  own device. One player plays against the CPU; 2–4 play head to head or 2-on-1 and 2-on-2 with CPU teammates. The\n  hub's relay only exists inside a session, so outside one the game is unaffected (`AIHub.active` is false) and plays\n  as above.\n\n### 16.2 The page head\n`session.js` goes right after `<meta charset>`, unmodified and first:\n```html\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script>/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 … (the whole file, unmodified) */</script>\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"6\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Outscore the other side over one half of arcade football\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD run · ✕/Space hike, dive, tackle · ✕○□△ or 1-4 throw · R2/Shift turbo\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\"><meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1–4\"><meta name=\"hub:source\" content=\"American football\">\n```\n\n### 16.3 A session, step by step (when `AIHub.active`)\n1. Boot skips the title, attract mode and menus. The boot steps build everything.\n2. `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If it returns `null`, play\n   as on its own.\n3. **The setup** comes from `AIHub.rng('setup')`, the same on every copy: a stadium (one of the 5), two different\n   teams (never the Scrubs), the stadium's weather. Seats map to sides: 0 home, 1 away, 2 home, 3 away. With one\n   player, seat 0 is home against a CPU away team.\n4. **The card scene** (`57-scene-hubcard.js`):\n   - It shows the two helmets facing off over the stadium backdrop, the team logos, the players by side in their seat\n     colors with ready ticks (`card.ready`), \"HOW TO WIN: OUTSCORE THEM OVER ONE HALF\", this device's controls as\n     chips, and the countdown (`card.left`; PAUSED while `card.paused`).\n   - **READY** (Enter, ✕ or a tap) calls `AIHub.answer('ready')`. **MORE TIME** (△, T or a tap) calls\n     `AIHub.answer('more')`; pressing again takes it back.\n   - It has no menus or choices, and nothing on it changes the round. Any randomness comes from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n   - Call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as the match is built, without a key press.\n5. On `start`, show a 3-2-1 countdown over the opening kickoff setup while `AIHub.time() < 0`. Kick off at ≥ 0.\n6. **The match** is one half: 2 quarters of 1:30. A play takes about 17 s of real time for about 16 s of game clock\n   (live play plus the runoff), plus about 8 s per TD celebration, so plan on 1.3 real seconds per clock second. When\n   `info.limitMs` is short, use `quarter = clamp((limitMs / 1000 − 60) / 2 / 1.3, 45, 90)` seconds (a 300 s limit\n   gives 90; a 200 s limit gives 54). No overtime: a tie is a tie.\n7. At the end of Q2, or on `time-up` (within `graceMs`), the host calls\n   `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })` and sends a last reliable snapshot with `over: 1`. Every copy\n   shows the final score (§14.8) until `end`.\n8. On `end`: take no more input, send nothing, `audio.music(null)` and mute. `reason` picks the message: finished,\n   ROUND CANCELLED (void, host-left) or YOU SAT THIS ONE OUT (sat-out).\n\n### 16.4 Roles\n- **Host** (`info.isHost`): runs the sim, the AI and the rules for every seat. Its own seat, if any, plays locally\n  with no prediction needed.\n- **Others:** predict their own held athlete, render snapshots, and run their local UI (the play call and the kick\n  meter).\n- **Server** (`info.server`): a host with no player of its own. It runs the same host code with every seat remote,\n  draws nothing (`draw` fills the screen once and returns), plays no audio, and owns no camera or input.\n- **Control** (§9.4) is keyed by seat. The host owns the assignment and broadcasts changes as events.\n\n### 16.5 Messages, rates, prediction (formats in Appendix B)\n- Client → host: `i`, its state and inputs, unreliable at 15 Hz. `call`, its play call, reliable. `kick`, its kick\n  meter result, reliable.\n- Host → all: `s`, the snapshot, unreliable at **14 Hz**, **at most 1,100 bytes** (under the hub's ~1,200\n  fragmentation size). `e`, events, reliable, at most 4/s: phase changes with the plays, control changes, scores,\n  stats, card draws, `over`. One `send()` to everyone counts as one message.\n- **The budget:** each copy sends at most 18 messages/s. The host sends 14 + ≤ 4. A client sends 15 + about 1\n  reliable (`call` or `kick`). The hub allows 20/s with bursts of 40, and the client drops the rest. `FF.net.budget` is\n  a token bucket at 18/s that refuses sends past it: it drops the oldest queued unreliable message, never a reliable\n  one, and delays the next snapshot rather than skipping an event. Tests check this.\n- **Client prediction** (the arena example's rule: \"your controls never wait for the network\"):\n  - The client moves its held athlete locally with the same movement code, plus a soft push from the snapshot's\n    nearby athletes. It sends its position, velocity, facing, intent bits and an **action log**: the last 8 actions\n    with sequence numbers. The host runs each new sequence number once, so losing a packet loses nothing.\n  - The host accepts the reported position unless the athlete is `locked` (tackled, engaged, in an action the host\n    started, a dead ball) or it is farther than top speed × elapsed + 8 units from the host's last position.\n    Otherwise it keeps its own and flags `corr`.\n  - The client snaps to the host when the difference is over 2 yd, or `corr` or `locked` is set. While locked it\n    stops predicting.\n- **Interpolation:** others and the ball render 100 ms behind the newest snapshot, interpolated, extrapolated up to\n  150 ms when late.\n- **The play call:** each client opens its play-call UI on the host's `e: phase PLAYCALL` and sends `call`. The host\n  waits for every human side or its own timer, then sends `e: phase PRESNAP` with both plays.\n- **The kick meter** runs on the kicking human's copy. Its `{ power, acc, aim }` goes as `kick` and the host executes\n  it.\n- **Leaving:** on `leave { id }`, that seat's athletes go back to the AI (a CPU tag over them) and the match goes on.\n  When the host leaves, the hub voids the round and the clients show ROUND CANCELLED on `end`.\n\n### 16.6 Session rules (the protocol's, and what they mean here)\n- No title, menus, attract mode or story. No quit or restart (`menu.quit: false`, no Restart item, no Dev Mode item).\n- **No world freeze:** `AIHub.active` is known from the page's first line, so in a session the game is constructed\n  with `new E.Game({ autoPause: false, ... })` and the match scene is `pausable: false`. The match scene reads the\n  `pause` action itself: Options (or Esc) opens a small local canvas overlay with SETTINGS\n  (`game.menu('settings', { pause: false })`, E8) and CONTROLS. While it is open, that player's athlete is driven by\n  the AI.\n- **Create + Options is the hub's:** each step, while Pad8 (Create) is held on any pad, call\n  `input.suppress('pause')` and `input.suppress('start')`.\n- **No player-to-player communication:** celebrations are random, there are no taunts, and names come only from the\n  hub. They're drawn in the pixel font, where characters outside its set become `?`. Never insert them as HTML.\n- No replays, cutscenes or halftime show (one half has no halftime). Saves and records are never written.\n- `Math.random` isn't seeded in a shared world: the host's sim uses `FF.rng.sim` seeded from `AIHub.rng('match')`.\n  Clients don't run the sim.\n\n### 16.7 Results\n- **Standings** by team: the winners' ids, then the losers' (a tie puts everyone in one array).\n- **One player against the CPU:** `standings: [[0]], won: true | false`.\n- `scores`: each player's team score.\n- `stats` per id: `{ Yards, TDs, Tackles, Sacks }`.\n- `awards`: `[{ id, title: 'Player of the Game', detail }, { id, title: 'Biggest Hit', detail: '12-yard launch' }]`.\n\n---\n\n## 17. Dev mode (`70-dev.js`)\n- **Entry:** the pause menu's **Dev Mode** (never in hub sessions), the deep link `#dev`, and Backquote once Dev mode\n  has been opened in this visit.\n- **The Dev screens** are Shell screens (E7) with page buttons across the top: TUNING, CHEATS, JUMP TO, PLAY LAB,\n  OVERLAYS, TOOLS. Each page lists 6–10 rows. Back returns to the pause menu.\n- **TUNING:**\n  - Sub-pages Movement, Passing, Catching, Tackling, Blocking, Kicking, AI, Rules, Presentation.\n  - Every tunable in §22 is a live slider row (min, max, step, unit). The sim reads `FF.T` on every use, so a change\n    applies at once.\n  - **Reset this page** and **Reset all to defaults**.\n  - Values persist as `Dev …` settings, so a designer's tuning survives a reload.\n  - **Copy values** puts the current tuning as JSON on the clipboard, or shows it in a text panel where clipboard\n    access isn't allowed, to paste into `02-tuning.js`.\n- **CHEATS** (toggles): god mode (your carriers can't be tackled), infinite turbo, always catch, always intercept,\n  force a fumble on the next hit, no tackles by the CPU, CPU vs CPU (your side played by the AI), unlimited cards,\n  always Blazing, Big Heads, lights out, slow motion (0.25 / 0.5 / 1 / 2), freeze the clock, win now / lose now.\n- **JUMP TO:**\n  - Situations: 4th & goal at the 1, 3rd & 25, the last 0:10 trailing by 4, a kickoff, an onside kick, a 52-yd FG,\n    overtime, the red zone, backed up at your own 1.\n  - Any story chapter (start, halftime, outro), any cutscene, any drill, any stadium and weather.\n  - Set the score, the clock, the down and the distance with sliders, then Apply.\n  - Give a card, or set Blazing on the held athlete.\n  - Trigger: a Mega Hit on the next tackle, a fumble now, a replay of the last play, the TD celebration, the halftime\n    show, lights out, Mascot Mayhem, each boss special.\n- **PLAY LAB:**\n  - Choose an offensive play, a defensive play, the teams, the difficulty and n (10 / 30 / 100).\n  - RUN ON FIELD loops the matchup with overlays. RUN HEADLESS shows its stats (§8.6) and an all-defenses sweep for\n    the play. The dev screens are the one place a small table is fine.\n- **OVERLAYS:**\n  - AI debug: each athlete's behavior name, target lines, routes, zones as circles, man assignments, intercept\n    points, blocking pairs with shed timers.\n  - Hitboxes: `rig.debug(r)` skeletons plus body circles.\n  - The ball's predicted path and landing point; the camera target and bounds.\n  - FPS and ms per update and draw; the last 12 bus events; each player's device, stick vector and held actions.\n- **TOOLS:** frame step (the sim paused, b1 steps 1/120 s, b4 steps 0.1 s), a free camera (`cam.free`), HUD off for\n  clean screenshots, presentation off, record a session and Save session (`E.session`), reseed the RNG, reset save\n  data (asks first), unlock all (chapters, cards, Big Heads).\n- **Hotkeys while Dev mode is on:** Backquote toggles the overlays, `[` and `]` change the time scale, `\\` steps a\n  frame. Leave F5, F11 and F12 to the browser.\n\n---\n\n## 18. Content\n\n### 18.1 Teams and rosters (`10-data-teams.js`)\n**Base ratings by position** (1–10). A player is the base for his position, plus his team's modifier, plus his own\nline below (clamped 1–10):\n\n| Pos | SPD | ACC | STR | HND | TCK | ARM | AIM | AWR | KCK |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| QB | 5 | 5 | 4 | 5 | 2 | 7 | 6 | 6 | 1 |\n| RB | 7 | 7 | 6 | 5 | 3 | 1 | 1 | 5 | 1 |\n| WR | 8 | 7 | 3 | 7 | 2 | 1 | 1 | 5 | 1 |\n| C, G | 2 | 3 | 7 | 3 | 3 | 1 | 1 | 5 | 1 |\n| DE | 5 | 5 | 6 | 3 | 6 | 1 | 1 | 5 | 1 |","numLines":500,"startLine":1319,"totalLines":2515}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GbFh5KLhLVkmM9NfkeWCsQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
