{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014f2GTgwTwvHr1tXMrSgYRL","type":"tool_result","content":"1818\t| DE | 5 | 5 | 6 | 3 | 6 | 1 | 1 | 5 | 1 |\n1819\t| NT | 2 | 3 | 8 | 2 | 6 | 1 | 1 | 5 | 1 |\n1820\t| LB | 5 | 5 | 6 | 4 | 7 | 1 | 1 | 6 | 1 |\n1821\t| CB | 8 | 7 | 3 | 5 | 4 | 1 | 1 | 5 | 1 |\n1822\t| S | 7 | 6 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 1 | 1 | 6 | 1 |\n1823\t| K | 3 | 3 | 2 | 3 | 1 | 4 | 3 | 5 | 7 |\n1824\t\n1825\tEach team has an offense of QB, C, LG, RG, RB, WR1, WR2; a defense of DE1, NT, DE2, LB1, LB2, CB, S; and a K, who\n1826\talso punts and replaces the QB slot on kick plays (the QB holds for FGs). Skin tones are indexes into the §12.2 list\n1827\t(1 lightest to 6 darkest). The AI tendencies are `{ run, pass, trick }` play weights, `blitz`, `lateHit`.\n1828\t\n1829\t**1. TUMBLEWEED JUNCTION FIASCOS** (TUM; the player's team in story mode)\n1830\t- **Colors:** jersey burnt orange `#e8742a`, purple `#4a2a6a`, cream trim `#f4e8c8`. The helmet is orange with a\n1831\t  purple stripe, the pants cream, the cleats black.\n1832\t- **Logo:** a flaming tumbleweed. **Home:** Tumbleweed Field. **Chant:** \"FI-AS-CO!\"\n1833\t- **Team modifier:** −1 to every rating except those of the stars below. They're bad, and the player's skill and\n1834\t  cards carry them. **AI tendencies:** {.45, .45, .10}, blitz .25, late hits .10.\n1835\t- **Offense:**\n1836\t  - QB #7 HAP HAZARD: skin 2, short brown hair, a big grin. ARM +2, AWR +1. The rookie: a pickle-barrel hauler with\n1837\t    a cannon arm.\n1838\t  - RB #22 \"DOC\" DOBSON: skin 4, bald, a mustache. ACC +1. A dentist on weekdays.\n1839\t  - WR #88 WHEELS WASHINGTON: skin 5, spiky hair, a gold chain. SPD +2. Fast, vain.\n1840\t  - WR #81 PETEY PICKENS: skin 1, red hair, freckles. HND −1. The owner's nephew: brave, butterfingered.\n1841\t  - C #50 TANK TANKERSLEY: skin 3. STR +2. A gentle giant who cries at sad movies and in big moments.\n1842\t  - G #63 SPUD MURPHY: skin 1, a ginger beard. He always has a potato.\n1843\t  - G #66 LUGNUT LOPEZ: skin 3, a ponytail. A mechanic.\n1844\t- **Defense:**\n1845\t  - DE #91 GRIZZ GRIZZWOLD: skin 2, a huge beard. STR +1.\n1846\t  - NT #95 MOOSE MALONEY: skin 4.\n1847\t  - DE #97 \"RATTLESNAKE\" RITA RUIZ: skin 3, a ponytail. ACC +2, SPD +1. The team's best player, and she knows it.\n1848\t  - LB #52 BUCK BOONE: skin 1, a buzz cut.\n1849\t  - LB #54 SAGEBRUSH SAM: skin 5, a mustache.\n1850\t  - CB #24 DUST DEVIL DIAZ: skin 3, spiky hair. SPD +1.\n1851\t  - S #31 PREACHER PRUITT: skin 6. AWR +2. He quotes scripture about tackling.\n1852\t- **K** #3 TOE-JAM TOMMY: skin 1, long hair, size 1.0.\n1853\t- **Cast:** Coach GUS BLUSTER (bulky, a red face, a too-small polo, a cap, a whistle, a megaphone in the drills).\n1854\t  Owner MAMA PEARL PICKENS (heroic 1.15, grey ponytail, an apron with a pickle on it; she runs Pickens' Pickle Barn).\n1855\t  Mascot FUMBLES THE FLAMING TUMBLEWEED.\n1856\t\n1857\t**2. BAYOU MUDHOGS** (BAY)\n1858\t- **Colors:** swamp green `#4a6a2a`, mud brown `#6a4a2a`, gold trim `#e8c040`. The helmet is green with a gold\n1859\t  stripe, the pants brown.\n1860\t- **Logo:** a hog head with tusks. **Home:** The Hog Wallow. **Chant:** \"HOGS! HOGS! HOGS!\"\n1861\t- **Team modifier:** STR +2 on OL, DL and LB; SPD −1 on everyone. **AI tendencies:** {.70, .25, .05}, blitz .30,\n1862\t  late hits .35.\n1863\t- **Offense:**\n1864\t  - QB #10 CLETUS THIBODEAUX: ARM −2, AIM −1, SPD +2. A scrambler.\n1865\t  - RB #44 BIG BERTHA BOUDREAUX: the boss; bulky 1.6; STR 10, SPD 6, ACC 4. Special MUDSLIDE.\n1866\t  - WR #80 CRAWDAD COMEAUX.\n1867\t  - WR #84 SKEETER LANDRY.\n1868\t  - C #60 GUMBO GUIDRY JR.\n1869\t  - G #71 BOUDIN BROUSSARD.\n1870\t  - G #75 TOOTIE TRAHAN.\n1871\t- **Defense:**\n1872\t  - DE #90 BAYOU BILLY BREAUX.\n1873\t  - NT #98 HOG JAW HEBERT.\n1874\t  - DE #92 CATFISH CORMIER.\n1875\t  - LB #51 MOSSY MOUTON.\n1876\t  - LB #57 RUSTY ROBICHAUX.\n1877\t  - CB #21 PIROGUE PREJEAN.\n1878\t  - S #33 GATOR BAIT GUILLORY.\n1879\t- **K** #8 BOOTS BOUDREAUX (Bertha's cousin).\n1880\t- **Cast:** Coach \"GATOR\" GUIDRY (an alligator-hide cap in green, a toothpick). Mascot HAMBONE (hog head).\n1881\t\n1882\t**3. NEON NITE OWLS** (NEO)\n1883\t- **Colors:** black `#1a1a2a`, neon cyan `#3af0f0` (glowing), magenta trim `#f03ab0`. The helmet is black with a\n1884\t  cyan glow stripe, the pants black.\n1885\t- **Logo:** neon owl eyes. **Home:** Afterglow Arena. **Chant:** \"HOOT-HOOT!\"\n1886\t- **Team modifier:** SPD +2 and HND +1 on QB, RB, WR, CB and S; STR −1 on OL and DL. **AI tendencies:**\n1887\t  {.25, .65, .10}, blitz .15, late hits .10.\n1888\t- **Offense:**\n1889\t  - QB #1 LUMEN LOPEZ: ARM 9, AIM 9. Special NIGHT VISION.\n1890\t  - RB #26 STROBE STEVENS.\n1891\t  - WR #11 ZAP ZAPATA: SPD 10, ACC 9. Special AFTERBURNER.\n1892\t  - WR #17 PIXEL PARK.\n1893\t  - C #55 BASS DROP BAKER.\n1894\t  - G #64 SUBWOOFER SMITH.\n1895\t  - G #68 REVERB REYES.\n1896\t- **Defense:**\n1897\t  - DE #93 NEON NIKKI NAKAMURA.\n1898\t  - NT #96 BLACKLIGHT BRUNO.\n1899\t  - DE #99 GLOWSTICK GUS.\n1900\t  - LB #50 LASER LARUE.\n1901\t  - LB #58 DISCO DAN.\n1902\t  - CB #2 SPARKLE SPARKS.\n1903\t  - S #20 MIDNIGHT MOSS.\n1904\t- **K** #4 RAVE RAVENSWOOD.\n1905\t- **Cast:** Coach DJ HOOT (headphones, sunglasses at night). Mascot HOOTY (owl head with glowing eyes).\n1906\t\n1907\t**4. GLACIER BAY YETIS** (GLB)\n1908\t- **Colors:** ice blue `#8ac8f0`, white `#f0f4f8`, navy trim `#2a3a6a`. The helmet is white with an ice-blue stripe,\n1909\t  the pants navy.\n1910\t- **Logo:** a yeti footprint. **Home:** Frostbite Field. **Chant:** \"BRRR! BRRR!\"\n1911\t- **Team modifier:** STR +2 and TCK +2 on DL and LB; HND +1 on everyone (ball security); SPD −1 on everyone.\n1912\t  **AI tendencies:** {.50, .45, .05}, blitz .45, late hits .15.\n1913\t- **Offense:**\n1914\t  - QB #9 SLEET SORENSEN.\n1915\t  - RB #30 PLOW PETERSON.\n1916\t  - WR #82 FLURRY FINN.\n1917\t  - WR #87 ICICLE IVERSEN.\n1918\t  - C #61 TUNDRA THORSON.\n1919\t  - G #70 PERMAFROST PAULSEN.\n1920\t  - G #77 GLACIER GUNDERSON.\n1921\t- **Defense:**\n1922\t  - DE #99 AVALANCHE: the boss; bulky 1.8, a beard; STR 10, SPD 6, TCK 9. Special SNOWPLOW. He speaks only in\n1923\t    growls.\n1924\t  - NT #94 BERG BJORKLUND.\n1925\t  - DE #91 HAILSTORM HANSEN.\n1926\t  - LB #53 FROSTY FJELD.\n1927\t  - LB #59 SNOWBALL SVENSSON.\n1928\t  - CB #23 POWDER PEDERSEN.\n1929\t  - S #36 WHITEOUT WALLIN.\n1930\t- **K** #5 SNOWSHOE SAMUELSSON.\n1931\t- **Cast:** Coach BJORN ICEBERG (fur coat, speaks in proverbs). Mascot ABOMINABLE AL.\n1932\t\n1933\t**5. GOLD COAST DYNASTY** (GCD; the final boss team)\n1934\t- **Colors:** gold `#f0c040`, black `#18161e`, white trim `#f4f4f0`. The helmet is gold with a black stripe, the\n1935\t  pants black.\n1936\t- **Logo:** a crown on a football. **Home:** The Mega Dome. **Chant:** \"DY-NAS-TY!\"\n1937\t- **Team modifier:** +1 to everything. **AI tendencies:** {.45, .50, .05}, blitz .30, late hits .20 (sneaky).\n1938\t- **Offense:**\n1939\t  - QB #12 BROCK STERLING III: the boss; ARM 10, AIM 9, AWR 8. Special GOLDEN SPIRAL. The owner's son: smug, never\n1940\t    been hit.\n1941\t  - RB #28 CHASE MONEY.\n1942\t  - WR #13 TREY GOLD: SPD +1.\n1943\t  - WR #19 PRESTON PLATINUM.\n1944\t  - C #52 BLUE CHIP BIXBY.\n1945\t  - G #67 TRUST FUND TUCKER.\n1946\t  - G #74 OFFSHORE OSGOOD.\n1947\t- **Defense:**\n1948\t  - DE #90 GOLDEN GATE GRAYSON.\n1949\t  - NT #97 VAULT VANCE.\n1950\t  - DE #94 DIAMOND DUKE.\n1951\t  - LB #55 \"THE MOUNTAIN\" MALU FALEOLO: the boss; bulky 1.7; STR 9, TCK 10, SPD 6. Special SEISMIC SACK.\n1952\t  - LB #50 ROYCE ROLLINS.\n1953\t  - CB #22 SILVER SPOON SINCLAIR.\n1954\t  - S #29 HEDGE FUND HARRINGTON.\n1955\t- **K** #1 PENNY PINCHER PERKINS: KCK 9.\n1956\t- **Cast:** Coach PRESCOTT PRIMROSE (a cashmere sweater over the shoulders). Owner MONTGOMERY STERLING II (a gold\n1957\t  suit, a cane; he wants Tumbleweed Field for a parking lot). Mascot GOLDIE (a gold lion head).\n1958\t\n1959\t**6. THE SCRUBS** (PRC; the practice squad: drills and the chapter 1 scrimmage only, hidden in exhibition)\n1960\t- **Colors:** grey practice jerseys `#8a8a90`, red trim `#c83a3a`. **Logo:** a whistle with a \"P\".\n1961\t- **Team modifier:** −2 to everything. **AI tendencies:** {.60, .40, 0}, blitz .10, late hits 0.\n1962\t- **Players:** BACKUP BOB, SCOUT TEAM SCOTT, PRACTICE PAT, CLIPBOARD CARL, WATERBOY WALT, DUMMY DAN, FILLER FRANK,\n1963\t  BENCH BRENDA, TRYOUT TROY, SPARE SPENCER, UNDERSTUDY URSULA, DEPTH CHART DEV, SUB SUSIE, PINNIE PETE, and the\n1964\t  kicker LONG SHOT LARRY. Numbers 60–99.\n1965\t\n1966\t**Other cast:** the announcers CHET THUNDERBUNS (play-by-play) and LOU \"THE TOE\" DIGGS (color). Head ref ZEBRA ZEKE\n1967\tand two more refs. A cheer squad of 4 per team in team colors with pom-poms. The Mega Dome's marching band of 8\n1968\t(bass drums and horns drawn by the gear hook). Photographers, a chain gang of 2, TV camera operators.\n1969\t\n1970\t### 18.2 Stadiums (`12-data-stadiums.js`)\n1971\t| | TUMBLEWEED FIELD | THE HOG WALLOW | AFTERGLOW ARENA | FROSTBITE FIELD | THE MEGA DOME |\n1972\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1973\t| Home | Fiascos | Mudhogs | Nite Owls | Yetis | Dynasty |\n1974\t| Light | dusk, ambient .62, warm sun from the west; a night variant for the prologue (.3, one flickering light) | overcast .55 | night .35, 4 towers, neon colors | cold day .5, towers | indoor .55, cool white, 6 sweeping spots |\n1975\t| Weather | clear | rain .6, wind .2, lightning .1 | clear | snow .7, wind .3 | none |\n1976\t| Field | worn grass, dirt patches | mud blotches between the hashes and at midfield (`mud`), shiny puddle decals | dark synthetic turf, glowing yard lines | snow-dusted grass, ice strips by the sidelines (`ice`), footprints | pristine turf, gold end zones, a giant crown at midfield |\n1977\t| Backdrop | a sunset sky, mesas, desert hills, cactus silhouettes | a grey sky, bald cypress with moss, fog | a city skyline at night with lit windows, neon billboards | snowy mountains and animated northern lights (green and purple bands) | the dome's dark ceiling truss with lights, banners |\n1978\t| Stands | 3 tiers of wooden bleachers (`plank`), 35% full (100% in the ending) | 5 tin-roof tiers (`metal`), 80%, ponchos | 7 concrete tiers with neon trims, 90%, glow sticks | 6 tiers, 75%, parkas and fur hats | 8 concrete tiers, 100%, gold and black sections |\n1979\t| Props | a water tower, a pickup truck, string lights, the hand-flipped scoreboard, hay bales, cacti, an old bench | an airboat, crab traps (crates), a smoking grill, lanterns, a HOG WALLOW sign | neon signs (HOOT, AFTERGLOW), laser emitters (sweeping emissive lines), a DJ booth (speakers, a table), towers | snow-capped pines, a plow (the bulldozer shape in blue), heaters (fire drums), a yeti ice sculpture (crystal) | 4 pyro cannons, the inflatable helmet tunnel, the indoor blimp, the jumbotron, TV cameras, confetti cannons, the trophy stage (the ending) |\n1980\t| Music | DUST DEVIL STOMP | SWAMP STOMP | NEON NIGHTDRIVE | FROSTBITE FANFARE | MEGA DOME ANTHEM |\n1981\t| Special | crickets at night | lightning, puddle splashes | LIGHTS OUT (ch3, and a Dev toggle), lasers on TDs | breath puffs, slippery edges | pyro on scores, the halftime band, the blimp's message board |\n1982\t\n1983\t### 18.3 Plays (`11-data-plays.js`; coordinates in yards from the ball spot, x downfield, y + to the offense's right)\n1984\t**Offensive formations** (C, LG and RG are always at `[-0.6, 0]`, `[-0.8, -1.4]`, `[-0.8, 1.4]`):\n1985\t\n1986\t| Formation | QB | RB | WR1 | WR2 |\n1987\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1988\t| PRO | [-1.4, 0] | [-6, 0] | [-0.8, -13] | [-0.8, 12] |\n1989\t| SHOTGUN | [-5, 0] | [-5, 1.8] | [-0.8, -13] | [-0.8, 12] |\n1990\t| TIGHT | [-1.4, 0] | [-5, 0] | [-0.8, -6] | [-0.8, 3.4] |\n1991\t| SPREAD | [-5, 0] | [-0.8, 7] | [-0.8, -15] | [-0.8, 15] |\n1992\t\n1993\t| Kick formation | Slots |\n1994\t|---|---|\n1995\t| PUNT | the K replaces the QB at [-12, 0]; RB up-back [-5, 1.5]; WR1 and WR2 gunners at [-0.8, ∓20] |\n1996\t| FIELD GOAL | QB holder [-7, 0]; K [-9.5, -1.2]; RB wing [-1, -2.6]; WR2 wing [-1, 2.6]; WR1 sits out |\n1997\t| KICKOFF | the defense unit with the K for the NT; the K at [-6, 0] behind the spot; the others on the line at y −20, −12, −5, 5, 12, 20 |\n1998\t\n1999\t**Offensive plays** (QB reads in order; `readT` is when reading starts):\n2000\t\n2001\t| Tab | Play | Formation | Assignments |\n2002\t|---|---|---|---|\n2003\t| RUN | HB DIVE | PRO | QB hands off at 0.45 s, then fakes a drop to [-5, 1]. RB carries [-2.5, 0.6] → [2, 0.8] → [8, 0.8]. C drives the NT. LG seals DE1 (drive [0.3, -1]). RG climbs to LB2. WR1 blocks the CB, WR2 the S. |\n2004\t| RUN | HB SWEEP | PRO | QB pitches at 0.3 s. RB carries [-5, 4] → [-1, 11] → [6, 13]. LG pulls [-1.8, 1.5] → [0.5, 9], then leads. C reaches the NT. RG seals DE2 inside. WR2 crack-blocks LB2. WR1 blocks the CB. |\n2005\t| RUN | HB DRAW | SHOTGUN | QB drops to [-6.5, 0] and hands off at 0.9 s. RB waits, then carries [-4.5, 0.5] → [3, 0] → [9, 0]. The OL pass-sets for 0.9 s, then run-blocks the nearest man. WR1 and WR2 run go routes to clear out. |\n2006\t| RUN | QB SNEAK | TIGHT | QB keeps: [0.5, 0.3] → [4, 0.3]. RB leads into his back. The OL drives straight ahead. WRs block. |\n2007\t| RUN | COUNTER | PRO | QB hands off at 0.55 s. RB steps [-6, -1.5], then cuts: [-4, 0.5] → [1, 2.6] → [8, 3.5]. LG pulls [-2, 0] → [0, 3] and kicks out DE2. C blocks the NT. RG blocks LB1. WRs block the CB and S. |\n2008\t| RUN | TOSS | SHOTGUN | QB tosses at 0.2 s. RB carries [-5, -4] → [0, -11] → [6, -13]. WR1 crack-blocks LB1. C and LG reach left. RG cuts off the NT. WR2 blocks the S. |\n2009\t| PASS | SLANTS | SHOTGUN | Drop [-6, 0]; reads WR2, WR1, RB; readT 0.6. WR1 [2.5, -13] → [9, -6]. WR2 [2.5, 12] → [9, 5]. RB flat [-2, 5] → [1, 10]. |\n2010\t| PASS | CURLS | SHOTGUN | Drop [-6.5, 0]; reads WR1, WR2, RB. WR1 [11, -13] → [9, -12]. WR2 [11, 12] → [9, 11]. RB swing [-3, -6] → [1, -11]. |\n2011\t| PASS | DEEP POST | PRO | Drop [-7, 0]; reads WR2, WR1, RB; readT 1.0. WR1 post [12, -13] → [28, -3]. WR2 go [35, 12]. RB blocks 1.2 s, then [2, 3] → [5, 6]. |\n2012\t| PASS | MESH | SHOTGUN | Reads WR1, WR2, RB. WR1 crosses [5, -13] → [5, 10]. WR2 crosses [7, 12] → [7, -10]. RB wheel [-3, 5] → [2, 10] → [18, 12]. |\n2013\t| PASS | OUT & UP | SHOTGUN | Reads WR2, WR1, RB; readT 0.9. WR2 [8, 12] → [8, 16] → [30, 17]. WR1 dig [12, -13] → [12, -2]. RB flat [-1, -4] → [2, -9]. |\n2014\t| PASS | QUICK OUTS | SHOTGUN | Drop [-5.5, 0]; reads WR2, WR1, RB; readT 0.5. WR1 [5, -13] → [5, -18]. WR2 [5, 12] → [5, 17]. RB seam [-1, 0.5] → [6, 0.5]. |\n2015\t| TRICK | HB SCREEN | SHOTGUN | Drop [-7.5, 0]; reads RB only; readT 1.4. RB to [-3, 5] and waits. The OL pass-sets 0.8 s, then releases to [1, 5], [0, 7], [2, 8] and leads. WR1 go [25, -13]. WR2 blocks. |\n2016\t| TRICK | FLEA FLICKER | PRO | QB hands off at 0.5 s. RB to [-2, 0.5] and pitches back to the QB at 1.3 s (automatic). QB at [-5, 0] reads WR1, WR2 from 1.8 s. WR1 [30, -8]. WR2 [25, 10]. The OL pass-blocks. |\n2017\t| TRICK | HOOK & LATERAL | SHOTGUN | Reads WR1 only; readT 0.9. WR1 hook [10, -12] → [9, -12]. WR2 [6, 12] → [9, -7], trailing behind WR1. After the catch, the lateral to WR2 (lb/rb; the CPU laterals by itself when WR2 is within 4 yd behind). RB blocks. |\n2018\t| TRICK | FUMBLEROOSKI | PRO | QB sets the ball down behind the C at 0.2 s. The C scoops it at 0.6 s and carries [1, -2] → [6, -4] → [12, -5]. QB and RB fake a sweep right ([-4, 6] → [0, 11]). Defenders are fooled for 0.8 s (they chase the RB). LG and RG block. |\n2019\t| TRICK | HAIL MARY | SPREAD | Drop [-9, 0]; reads WR1, WR2, RB; readT 2.2. WR1 [40, -2]. WR2 [42, 2]. RB [38, 0]. Maximum protection. |\n2020\t| SPECIAL | PUNT | PUNT | A long snap, the meter, the shield protects 1.5 s, then everyone covers. The gunners sprint. |\n2021\t| SPECIAL | FIELD GOAL | FIELD GOAL | The snap to the holder, the plant, the kick, the Kick Cam. |\n2022\t| SPECIAL | FAKE PUNT | PUNT | The punter rolls right and throws to WR1 at [8, -10], or runs when open. |\n2023\t| SPECIAL | KNEEL | PRO | The QB kneels at once; the clock runs `T.runoff`. |\n2024\tKickoff choices: DEEP KICK, SQUIB KICK, ONSIDE KICK. PAT choices: KICK XP, GO FOR 2.\n2025\t\n2026\t**Defensive formations** (x = yards off the ball on the defense's side; y in the offense's frame):\n2027\t\n2028\t| Formation | DE1 | NT | DE2 | LB1 | LB2 | CB | S |\n2029\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n2030\t| BASE 3-2-2 | [1.2, -2.8] | [1.0, 0] | [1.2, 2.8] | [4.5, -3.5] | [4.5, 3.5] | [6, over WR1] | [12, 0] |\n2031\t| PRESSURE | as BASE | as BASE | as BASE | [3, -2.5] | [3, 2.5] | [5, over WR1] | [10, over WR2] |\n2032\t| PREVENT | [1.2, -2.8] | [3, 0] | [1.2, 2.8] | [10, -8] | [10, 8] | [20, -8] | [20, 8] |\n2033\t| GOAL LINE | [0.9, -2.6] | [0.8, 0] | [0.9, 2.6] | [2.2, -1.5] | [2.2, 1.5] | [1.5, over WR1] | [3, over WR2] |\n2034\t\n2035\t**Defensive plays:**\n2036\t\n2037\t| Tab | Play | Formation | Assignments |\n2038\t|---|---|---|---|\n2039\t| BASE | COVER 2 | BASE | DE1 and DE2 contain, NT rushes the A gap. LB1 zone [6, -7] r5, LB2 zone [6, 7] r5. CB zone [16, -9] r10, S zone [16, 9] r10. |\n2040\t| BASE | MAN-TO-MAN | BASE | The DL rushes. CB on WR1, S on WR2, LB2 on the RB. LB1 robber zone [8, 0] r6. |\n2041\t| BASE | QB SPY | BASE | The DL rushes. LB1 spies the QB. CB on WR1, S on WR2, LB2 on the RB. |\n2042\t| PRESSURE | LB BLITZ | PRESSURE | The DL rushes; LB1 rushes the A gap, LB2 the B gap. CB on WR1, S on WR2. The RB is free. |\n2043\t| PRESSURE | ZONE BLITZ | PRESSURE | The NT drops to zone [5, 0] r6. LB1, DE1 and DE2 rush. LB2 zone [6, 6] r5. CB zone [15, -9] r10, S zone [15, 9] r10. |\n2044\t| PRESSURE | FIASCO BLITZ | PRESSURE | Six rush (everyone but the S). S zone [18, 0] r14. All or nothing. |\n2045\t| SPECIAL | PREVENT | PREVENT | DE1 and DE2 rush, the NT spies the QB. LB1 zone [10, -8] r7, LB2 zone [10, 8] r7, CB zone [22, -8] r12, S zone [22, 8] r12. |\n2046\t| SPECIAL | GOAL LINE | GOAL LINE | The DL and LBs fill the A, B and C gaps. CB on WR1, S on WR2. |\n2047\t| SPECIAL | FG BLOCK | GOAL LINE | Everyone rushes; the NT and LB1 jump at the kick. |\n2048\tReturn choices: RETURN MIDDLE, RETURN LEFT, RETURN RIGHT (the wedge's lane), HANDS TEAM (against an onside kick).\n2049\tPunt returns: RETURN, BLOCK THE PUNT.\n2050\t\n2051\t### 18.4 Fiasco Cards\n2052\tThe 8 cards and their rules are in §10.2. Each card needs its art (§12.8), its commentary line (§18.5) and its CPU\n2053\ttrigger.\n2054\t\n2055\t### 18.5 Commentary line banks (`16-data-lines.js`)\n2056\tWrite at least 8 lines for each of the main events (kickoff, bigRun, td, bigHit, megaHit, sack, int, fumble, drop,\n2057\tlateHit, hotOn, final) and at least 3 for the rest, in this voice: short (at most 48 characters a line, so they fit\n2058\ttwo caption lines at 10 feet), CHET in ALL CAPS and LOU in sentence case, puns and broadcast clichés, never cruel, no\n2059\treal teams, players or leagues, no real broadcasters' catchphrases, and no profanity (\"DAG NABBIT!\" is as far as it\n2060\tgoes). The samples set the tone:\n2061\t\n2062\t| Event | Samples |\n2063\t|---|---|\n2064\t| kickoff | CHET: \"HERE WE GO! THE BALL IS IN THE AIR!\" · LOU: \"I used to kick those. Then my leg retired.\" |\n2065\t| bigRun | \"{player} FINDS DAYLIGHT!\" · \"THE 40! THE 30! SOMEBODY TACKLE HIM!\" · \"LOOK AT THOSE WHEELS!\" |\n2066\t| td | \"TOUCH! DOWN! {team}!\" · \"HE IS GONE! LIKE MY HAIRLINE!\" · \"SIX POINTS AND A SIDE OF FRIES!\" · LOU: \"Somebody call the mayor.\" |\n2067\t| bigHit | \"OH! THAT HIT HAD A ZIP CODE!\" · \"HE JUST GOT DELIVERED!\" · \"SOMEBODY CALL HIS MAMA!\" |\n2068\t| megaHit | \"OH, THE HUMANITY OF IT ALL!\" · \"HE'S IN ORBIT! NASA, ARE YOU SEEING THIS?\" · \"HIS HELMET IS IN A DIFFERENT AREA CODE!\" |\n2069\t| sack | \"SACKED! {player} PUTS HIM IN A BAG!\" · \"BROUGHT DOWN LIKE THE GROCERIES!\" |\n2070\t| int | \"PICKED OFF! {player} HAS IT!\" · \"THAT'S A GIFT WITH A BOW ON IT!\" · \"INTERCEPTED! HE'S TAKING IT TO THE HOUSE!\" |\n2071\t| fumble | \"FUMBLE! THE BALL IS LOOSE!\" · \"THAT'S A FIASCO, FOLKS!\" · \"BUTTERFINGERS!\" |\n2072\t| pile | \"WHO'S GOT IT?! THERE'S A PILE OF HUMANITY!\" · LOU: \"I see a shoe. I see an elbow. I see a sandwich?\" |\n2073\t| drop | \"DROPPED! RIGHT IN THE BREADBASKET!\" · LOU: \"Hands of stone, Chet. Granite.\" |\n2074\t| lateHit | \"THE WHISTLE BLEW, FOLKS! HE DID NOT CARE!\" · \"LATE HIT! AND THE REF JUST SHRUGS!\" |\n2075\t| hotOn | \"{player} IS BLAZING!\" · \"IS IT HOT IN HERE OR IS IT JUST {player}?\" · \"SOMEBODY GET A FIRE EXTINGUISHER!\" |\n2076\t| hotOff | \"AND THE FIRE IS OUT. RESET THE SMOKE ALARMS.\" |\n2077\t| card | ROCKET CLEATS \"THOSE SHOES ARE ILLEGAL IN FOUR STATES!\" · GLUE GLOVES \"NOTHING'S GETTING LOOSE NOW!\" · BRICK WALL \"WHERE'D THEY GET THE BRICKS?!\" · HOT SAUCE \"HE DRANK THE WHOLE BOTTLE!\" · MEGA HIT \"SOMEBODY'S GOING TO ORBIT!\" · BUTTERFINGERS \"THAT BALL IS SLICK AS A GREASED PIG!\" · MASCOT MAYHEM \"IS THAT {mascot} ON THE FIELD?! IT IS!\" · SUPER FOOT \"THAT LEG IS INSURED FOR A MILLION BUCKS!\" |\n2078\t| fiascoBreak | \"FIASCO BREAK! EVERY DISASTER IS AN OPPORTUNITY!\" |\n2079\t| fgGood / fgMiss | \"IT'S GOOD! RIGHT DOWN THE PIPE!\" · \"DOINK... AND IN! LUCKY, LUCKY!\" / \"NO GOOD! WIDE LEFT! WIDE EVERYTHING!\" |\n2080\t| punt | \"BOOMING PUNT!\" · LOU: \"Beautiful spiral. I'd know. I never had one.\" |\n2081\t| safety | \"SAFETY! TWO POINTS AND A LOT OF SHAME!\" |\n2082\t| firstDown / thirdLong / fourthDown / redZone | \"MOVE THE CHAINS!\" / \"THIRD AND A COUNTY MILE!\" / \"FOURTH DOWN! DECISION TIME!\" / \"RED ZONE! THE CROWD IS ON ITS FEET!\" |\n2083\t| halftime / final | \"THAT'S THE HALF! {team} LEADS {score}!\" / \"THAT'S THE BALL GAME! {team} WINS IT {score}!\" · close: \"WHAT A FINISH! I NEED A NAP!\" · blowout, LOU: \"That wasn't a game, Chet. That was a crime scene.\" |\n2084\t| specials | MUDSLIDE \"BERTHA IS BULLDOZING THROUGH!\" · AFTERBURNER \"ZAP JUST BROKE THE SOUND BARRIER!\" · SNOWPLOW \"AVALANCHE IS CLEARING THE ROAD!\" · GOLDEN SPIRAL \"THE GOLDEN SPIRAL! YOU CAN'T TOUCH IT!\" · SEISMIC SACK \"THAT ONE REGISTERED ON THE RICHTER SCALE!\" |\n2085\t| mascot, refDown, lightsOut | \"IS THAT A TUMBLEWEED ON THE FIELD?! AND IT'S ON FIRE!\" · \"AND THE REF GOES DOWN! HE'S FINE! HE'S... MOSTLY FINE!\" · \"THE LIGHTS ARE OUT AT THE AFTERGLOW!\" |\n2086\t| weather, idle | LOU: \"It's raining sideways, Chet.\" · LOU: \"I can't feel my microphone.\" · LOU: \"Football's a lot like life, Chet. Mostly running into things.\" |\n2087\t| incomplete, brokenTackle, pancake | \"INCOMPLETE. THE BALL HAD OTHER PLANS.\" · \"HE SHRUGGED HIM OFF LIKE A BAD HABIT!\" · \"PANCAKE! WITH SYRUP!\" |\n2088\t- **Refs** (babble plus a tiny speech bubble): \"FIRST DOWN!\", \"TOUCHDOWN!\", \"INCOMPLETE!\", \"BALL'S HERE!\", \"...SURE,\n2089\t  WHY NOT.\"\n2090\t- **QB cadences** (a small bubble over the QB): Hap \"PICKLE 7! PICKLE 7! HUT!\"; Brock \"GOLD! GOLD! HUT HUT!\"; Lumen\n2091\t  \"LIGHTS! CAMERA! HUT!\"; Cletus \"MUD 44! MUD 44! HUT!\"; Sleet \"COLD! COLDER! HUT!\"; others \"BLUE 42! SET... HUT!\"\n2092\t\n2093\t### 18.6 The story scripts (`14-data-story.js`; [stage directions] become E.Story `event` steps)\n2094\t**PROLOGUE: TUMBLEWEED FIELD, 11:58 PM.** [night, one flickering light, crickets; the team mopes at midfield]\n2095\t- CHET (radio): \"LIVE FROM TUMBLEWEED JUNCTION... WHERE FOOTBALL COMES TO DIE!\"\n2096\t- LOU (radio): \"Ninety-nine losses in a row, Chet. You have to admire the consistency.\"\n2097\t- MAMA PEARL: \"Ninety-nine losses, one leaky roof, and zero quit. That's my Fiascos.\"\n2098\t- [a gold golf cart rolls in; a bulldozer rumbles behind it, headlights on]\n2099\t- STERLING: \"Pearl! Sign the papers. This dirt patch would make a lovely parking lot.\"\n2100\t- MAMA PEARL: \"Over my pickled body, Montgomery.\"\n2101\t- BROCK: \"Dad, it smells like a pickle barrel exploded out here.\"\n2102\t- STERLING: \"Fine. The Fiasco Cup. Win it, keep your field. Lose it... and I pave it.\"\n2103\t- COACH BLUSTER: \"You got yourself a bet! ...Wait. What's the Fiasco Cup?\"\n2104\t- LOU (radio): \"Only the most over-the-top football tournament on Earth, Gus.\"\n2105\t- CHET (radio): \"FOUR GAMES! NO RULES! ONE TROPHY! IT'S THE FIASCO CUP!\"\n2106\t- MAMA PEARL: \"Then we need a quarterback. A real one.\"\n2107\t- [a spotlight finds HAP, who is carrying two pickle barrels]\n2108\t- HAP: \"I can throw a pickle barrel sixty yards. Does that count?\"\n2109\t- COACH BLUSTER: \"Kid... tryouts are at dawn.\" [title card: THE FIASCO CUP]\n2110\t\n2111\t**CH1 TRYOUTS.**\n2112\t- **Intro** [dawn, cones and dummies]:\n2113\t  - COACH: \"Listen up, Hazard! This is tryouts. You fail, you go back to pickles.\"\n2114\t  - COACH: \"First drill: run the cones. Then hit the turbo like it owes you money!\"\n2115\t- **Between drills,** one line each:\n2116\t  - D2: \"Hike it! The ball goes to the man in the backfield, not the man in the stands!\"\n2117\t  - D3: \"Spin, stiff arm, hurdle! Like a ballerina with anger issues!\"\n2118\t  - D4: \"See the button over his head? Press it! Football is easy!\"\n2119\t  - D5: \"Jump at the top! The ball's shadow tells you where!\"\n2120\t  - D6: \"Defense wins championships! Offense wins... also championships. Hit somebody!\"\n2121\t  - D7: \"Three taps, son. Power, then aim. Don't kick the holder. AGAIN.\"\n2122\t  - D8: \"Pick a play. Flip it. And Pearl's hot sauce? That's for emergencies.\"\n2123\t  - D9: \"One drive. Score, and you're my quarterback.\"\n2124\t- **Outro:**\n2125\t  - COACH: \"Hazard, you might be the worst thing to happen to this franchise...\"\n2126\t  - COACH: \"...which makes you the best thing to happen to this franchise.\"\n2127\t  - MAMA PEARL: \"Here, sugar. Pearl's Five-Alarm Hot Sauce. For emergencies only.\"\n2128\t  - [cards: HOT SAUCE and SUPER FOOT]\n2129\t\n2130\t**CH2 THE MUD BOWL.**\n2131\t- **Intro** [the press room at the Hog Wallow, rain drumming on the tin roof]:\n2132\t  - CHET: \"ROUND ONE! THE FIASCOS VISIT THE BAYOU MUDHOGS IN THE HOG WALLOW!\"\n2133\t  - GATOR: \"Y'all ever play in mud this deep? We got crawdads livin' in the end zone.\"\n2134\t  - BIG BERTHA: \"I'm gonna run through y'all like hot butter through grits.\"\n2135\t  - COACH: \"Grits don't tackle, ma'am. ...Do they?\"\n2136\t  - HAP: \"Coach, why are we wearing snorkels?\"\n2137\t  - COACH: \"Mud management, son. Tackle low, hold the ball tight, watch for the MUDSLIDE.\"\n2138\t  - LOU: \"Rain's coming in sideways, Chet. Fumbles are gonna fly like bats.\"\n2139\t- **Halftime** [the visitors' locker room]:\n2140\t  - COACH: \"We're {score} at the half! Somebody tell me what we do about it!\" [choice]\n2141\t  - The choices (each effect lasts the second half): **GROUND AND POUND** (+10% run blocking, carriers break\n2142\t    tackles +0.05), **AIR IT OUT** (catch +0.06, aim error ×0.9), **HIT 'EM HARDER** (tackle +0.05, Big Hit fumble\n2143\t    +5%), **TRICKERY** (draw a Fiasco Card).\n2144\t- **Win:**\n2145\t  - BIG BERTHA: \"Well I'll be. Y'all hit like a family reunion. Respect.\"\n2146\t  - GATOR: \"Come on back for the crawfish boil. Bring that rookie.\"\n2147\t  - CHET: \"THE FIASCOS WIN A FOOTBALL GAME! I REPEAT! THE FIASCOS WIN A FOOTBALL GAME!\"\n2148\t  - [card: MEGA HIT]\n2149\t- **Loss:** COACH: \"We got mud in places mud shouldn't go. Again!\"\n2150\t\n2151\t**CH3 LIGHTS OUT.**\n2152\t- **Intro** [the Afterglow tunnel, neon, bass thumping]:\n2153\t  - CHET: \"THE QUARTERFINAL! THE NEON NITE OWLS AT THE AFTERGLOW!\"\n2154\t  - DJ HOOT: \"Welcome to the Afterglow, small town. Hope your eyes can keep up.\"\n2155\t  - LUMEN: \"I see the open man in the dark. I AM the open man in the dark.\"\n2156\t  - ZAP: \"You blinked. I'm already in the end zone.\"\n2157\t  - [card: 3RD QUARTER. OWLS 21, FIASCOS 7]\n2158\t  - COACH: \"We're down fourteen because SOMEBODY slept through the first half!\"\n2159\t  - WHEELS: \"...I needed my beauty rest, Coach.\"\n2160\t- **In-game, at the 4th play of Q3** (radio, non-modal):\n2161\t  - CHET: \"WAIT, THE LIGHTS! THE LIGHTS ARE OUT AT THE AFTERGLOW!\"\n2162\t  - LOU: \"Looks like a tumbleweed tripped over the power cable, Chet.\"\n2163\t  - FUMBLES: [guilty tumbleweed noises]\n2164\t  - COACH: \"Glow paint! Everybody rub on the glow paint!\"\n2165\t  - [LIGHTS OUT for 3 plays]\n2166\t- **Win:**\n2167\t  - DJ HOOT: \"Respect, Tumbleweed. That comeback was a banger.\"\n2168\t  - ZAP: \"...Can I get your rookie's autograph? For my cousin. Not for me.\"\n2169\t  - [cards: ROCKET CLEATS and GLUE GLOVES]\n2170\t- **Loss:** COACH: \"Somebody turn the lights back on in your heads! Again!\"\n2171\t\n2172\t**CH4 FROSTBITE.**\n2173\t- **Intro** [Frostbite Field, snow, the northern lights]:\n2174\t  - CHET: \"THE SEMIFINAL! IT'S MINUS TWELVE AND THE HOT DOGS ARE FROZEN SOLID!\"\n2175\t  - ICEBERG: \"The glacier does not hurry. Yet it carves the valley.\"\n2176\t  - COACH BLUSTER: \"...Is that a threat or a fortune cookie?\"\n2177\t  - AVALANCHE: [a growl that shakes the snow off the roof]\n2178\t  - LOU: \"That's Avalanche. Seven feet tall. Speaks only in growls and sacks.\"\n2179\t  - [card: 4TH QUARTER, 1:30 LEFT. YETIS 20, FIASCOS 17. YOUR BALL ON YOUR 20]\n2180\t  - COACH: \"Ninety seconds, eighty yards. Get out of bounds to stop the clock!\"\n2181\t- **Win:**\n2182\t  - AVALANCHE: [a soft growl; he hands Hap a hand-knitted scarf]\n2183\t  - LOU: \"He knits, Chet. The big fella knits.\"\n2184\t  - [card: MASCOT MAYHEM]\n2185\t- **Loss:** COACH: \"Frozen solid. Thaw out and run it back!\"\n2186\t\n2187\t**CH5 THE FIASCO BOWL.**\n2188\t- **Intro** [the Mega Dome press conference, camera flashes]:\n2189\t  - CHET: \"THE FIASCO BOWL! SEVENTY THOUSAND FANS AND ONE BULLDOZER!\"\n2190\t  - BROCK: \"I've got a golden arm, a golden helmet, and a golden future.\"\n2191\t  - BROCK: \"You've got... pickles.\"\n2192\t  - HAP: \"And you've never been hit by a guy who hauls pickle barrels for a living.\"\n2193\t  - THE MOUNTAIN: \"I will fall on you. Like a mountain. Because I am THE MOUNTAIN.\"\n2194\t  - STERLING: \"Win and keep your little field, Pearl. Lose, and the bulldozer's warming up.\"\n2195\t  - MAMA PEARL: \"Warm it up all you like, Montgomery. It's gonna be a long, cold night.\"\n2196\t- **Halftime** [the visitors' locker room]:\n2197\t  - MAMA PEARL: \"Ninety-nine losses taught us one thing: how to get back up.\"\n2198\t  - COACH: \"So get back up! What's the plan?\" [the same 4 choices as CH2]\n2199\t- **Win** [the field, confetti, the trophy stage]:\n2200\t  - CHET: \"THE TUMBLEWEED FIASCOS ARE FIASCO CUP CHAMPIONS! I NEED TO SIT DOWN!\"\n2201\t  - LOU: \"You ARE sitting down, Chet.\"\n2202\t  - [the team dumps the sports-drink bucket on Coach Bluster]\n2203\t  - COACH: \"AAAAH! IT'S ORANGE! WHY IS IT ALWAYS ORANGE?!\"\n2204\t  - STERLING: \"This is a... a FIASCO!\" [he steps back off the stage into the victory cake]\n2205\t  - MAMA PEARL: \"Keep your bulldozer, Montgomery. We're keeping our field.\"\n2206\t  - BROCK: \"...Hey. Rookie. Nice arm.\"\n2207\t  - HAP: \"Nice cake, Brock.\"\n2208\t  - [EPILOGUE card: TUMBLEWEED FIELD, ONE YEAR LATER. ATTENDANCE: SOLD OUT. The full bleachers chant \"FI-AS-CO!\",\n2209\t    then the credits roll over a montage of the season's highlight clips.]\n2210\t- **Loss:**\n2211\t  - STERLING: \"Start the engines!\"\n2212\t  - COACH: \"Not today! Run it back!\"\n2213\t\n2214\t**The credits roll** (`credits` scene): the FIASCO FOREVER ballad. The About pages scroll as credits (§14.10), over\n2215\treplays of the player's best story highlight clips (or the attract segments when there are none). Any button speeds\n2216\tit up 4×, and ○ held for 1 s skips it.\n2217\t\n2218\t---\n2219\t\n2220\t## 19. Build order and milestones\n2221\tBuild in this order. Each milestone ends with the one test command passing (§21) and its exit check. Systems before\n2222\tcontent, and the riskiest systems first. Placeholders are fine *between* milestones; none may remain at the end.\n2223\tDon't commit to git unless you're asked to (the folder is inside a shared repository).\n2224\t\n2225\t| M | Milestone | Build | Exit check |\n2226\t|---|---|---|---|\n2227\t| M0 | Setup | the dev folder; sparse fetches; the engine copy; E1 and E2; the mocap set and the store props cut; `build.mjs`; `test/run.mjs` and `test/lib/context.mjs`; `index.html`; `package.json` with Playwright | `npm test` prints a count line; `node build.mjs` writes the deliverable and it boots from `file://` |\n2228\t| M1 | Field and athletes | the stadium builder with Tumbleweed Field (floor paint, stands, crowd v1, goalposts, pylons, sideline props, backdrop, lights); the views; E3 and E4 gear; 14 athletes in formation with team uniforms; the ball drawn; movement, turbo and collisions; one human athlete; the camera following | tests: yard ↔ world, formation spots, collision separation, speed caps. Screenshots of the formation at 1920×1080 and 1280×720 read clearly at TV distance |\n2229\t| M2 | Football core | the match state machine, rules and clock; `02-tuning.js` and the first Dev sliders (E7); all formations and plays as data; actions (hike, handoff, throw, catch, tackle, dive); AI v1 (blocking, routes, coverage, rush, pursuit, QB reads, carrier steering); kicks (the meter, the Kick Cam, the FG test, kickoffs, punts, returns, touchbacks); INTs and fumbles v1; PATs; HUD v1; the play-call UI v1; the CPU coach; the Play Lab | a whole exhibition (Fiascos vs Mudhogs at Tumbleweed) plays start to finish against the CPU with keyboard, pad, and mouse for passing and menus; the Play Lab bands pass; no stuck plays |\n2230\t| M3 | Netcode spike | `80-net.js`: the adapter, roles, snapshots, prediction, the action log, play-call and kick sync, leave, time-up, end, finish; the hub card scene (functional); the fake hub and the loopback test; the browser harness runner | the net suite passes; all 4 harness configurations give `__hubCheck.pass === true` on the bundle. If not, §20 risk 2's decision is made now |\n2231\t| M4 | The over-the-top layer | every action in §7.4; Big and Mega Hits with FX, punch-ins and slow motion; fumbles and pile-ups; Hot Streak; the Fiasco Meter and the 8 cards; boss specials; celebrations; mascots; refs; divots, footprints, breath; replays and the highlight reel; commentary text and pops; crowd excitement, the Wave, signs | each feature's tests (§21.2 `actions`, `ots`, `replay`); a filmstrip of each new animation is clean |\n2232\t| M5 | Front end and UX | the title, main menu, exhibition setup, play-call final, HUD final, kick meter, results, Hall of Fiasco, About/Credits (wired to `FF_ABOUT`), settings with E2 and E9, glyph chips and device prompts everywhere, mouse hover and click everywhere, the touch-only gate, the pause items, Help; the attract mode with all 16 segments | the `ui`, `control` and `attract` suites; screenshots of every screen at both sizes |\n2233\t| M6 | Audio | all songs, layers and stings; every sfx; the crowd bed and chants; E5 and E6; the babble synth and every profile; the dialog voice hook; the commentary voice; the Voices, Crowd and Commentary settings | the `audio` suite (no unknown-sound warnings); a listening pass through every scene |\n2234\t| M7 | Content and story | all 6 teams (rosters, looks, logos, mascots, cast); all 5 stadiums (dressing, weather, light, backdrops, music); story mode (the board, the loadout, the prologue, chapters 1–5, the cutscene sets and scripts, halftime choices, rewards, stars, loss and retry, the ending, the credits); drills D1–D9 with bots; Practice; saves and Continue | the `data` and `story` suites (the scripted whole-game playthrough reaches the credits) |\n2235\t| M8 | Multiplayer complete | local 1–4 polish (prompts and colors per player, the co-op rules, keyboard halves); hub polish (card art, seat colors and names, the session overlay, Create + Options, stats and awards, results) | the `net` and `control` suites; the harness passes on the new bundle; a manual 2-player local game |\n2236\t| M9 | Dev, balance, polish, ship | every Dev page; balance against §22.2 with the sliders, the Play Lab and `test/balance.mjs`; the look pass (check.mjs notes, filmstrips, screenshots); the final `about.json`; the final bundle | the full `npm test -- --browser` passes; the §23 checklist is all ticked |\n2237\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49428dbe-779b-4248-8ac3-c582018d3c3d","uuid":"e0bf6424-2ee6-4657-9b8f-2403313b7767","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:06:30.421Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-070556__xb697dc/work/PLAN.md","content":"| DE | 5 | 5 | 6 | 3 | 6 | 1 | 1 | 5 | 1 |\n| NT | 2 | 3 | 8 | 2 | 6 | 1 | 1 | 5 | 1 |\n| LB | 5 | 5 | 6 | 4 | 7 | 1 | 1 | 6 | 1 |\n| CB | 8 | 7 | 3 | 5 | 4 | 1 | 1 | 5 | 1 |\n| S | 7 | 6 | 4 | 5 | 6 | 1 | 1 | 6 | 1 |\n| K | 3 | 3 | 2 | 3 | 1 | 4 | 3 | 5 | 7 |\n\nEach team has an offense of QB, C, LG, RG, RB, WR1, WR2; a defense of DE1, NT, DE2, LB1, LB2, CB, S; and a K, who\nalso punts and replaces the QB slot on kick plays (the QB holds for FGs). Skin tones are indexes into the §12.2 list\n(1 lightest to 6 darkest). The AI tendencies are `{ run, pass, trick }` play weights, `blitz`, `lateHit`.\n\n**1. TUMBLEWEED JUNCTION FIASCOS** (TUM; the player's team in story mode)\n- **Colors:** jersey burnt orange `#e8742a`, purple `#4a2a6a`, cream trim `#f4e8c8`. The helmet is orange with a\n  purple stripe, the pants cream, the cleats black.\n- **Logo:** a flaming tumbleweed. **Home:** Tumbleweed Field. **Chant:** \"FI-AS-CO!\"\n- **Team modifier:** −1 to every rating except those of the stars below. They're bad, and the player's skill and\n  cards carry them. **AI tendencies:** {.45, .45, .10}, blitz .25, late hits .10.\n- **Offense:**\n  - QB #7 HAP HAZARD: skin 2, short brown hair, a big grin. ARM +2, AWR +1. The rookie: a pickle-barrel hauler with\n    a cannon arm.\n  - RB #22 \"DOC\" DOBSON: skin 4, bald, a mustache. ACC +1. A dentist on weekdays.\n  - WR #88 WHEELS WASHINGTON: skin 5, spiky hair, a gold chain. SPD +2. Fast, vain.\n  - WR #81 PETEY PICKENS: skin 1, red hair, freckles. HND −1. The owner's nephew: brave, butterfingered.\n  - C #50 TANK TANKERSLEY: skin 3. STR +2. A gentle giant who cries at sad movies and in big moments.\n  - G #63 SPUD MURPHY: skin 1, a ginger beard. He always has a potato.\n  - G #66 LUGNUT LOPEZ: skin 3, a ponytail. A mechanic.\n- **Defense:**\n  - DE #91 GRIZZ GRIZZWOLD: skin 2, a huge beard. STR +1.\n  - NT #95 MOOSE MALONEY: skin 4.\n  - DE #97 \"RATTLESNAKE\" RITA RUIZ: skin 3, a ponytail. ACC +2, SPD +1. The team's best player, and she knows it.\n  - LB #52 BUCK BOONE: skin 1, a buzz cut.\n  - LB #54 SAGEBRUSH SAM: skin 5, a mustache.\n  - CB #24 DUST DEVIL DIAZ: skin 3, spiky hair. SPD +1.\n  - S #31 PREACHER PRUITT: skin 6. AWR +2. He quotes scripture about tackling.\n- **K** #3 TOE-JAM TOMMY: skin 1, long hair, size 1.0.\n- **Cast:** Coach GUS BLUSTER (bulky, a red face, a too-small polo, a cap, a whistle, a megaphone in the drills).\n  Owner MAMA PEARL PICKENS (heroic 1.15, grey ponytail, an apron with a pickle on it; she runs Pickens' Pickle Barn).\n  Mascot FUMBLES THE FLAMING TUMBLEWEED.\n\n**2. BAYOU MUDHOGS** (BAY)\n- **Colors:** swamp green `#4a6a2a`, mud brown `#6a4a2a`, gold trim `#e8c040`. The helmet is green with a gold\n  stripe, the pants brown.\n- **Logo:** a hog head with tusks. **Home:** The Hog Wallow. **Chant:** \"HOGS! HOGS! HOGS!\"\n- **Team modifier:** STR +2 on OL, DL and LB; SPD −1 on everyone. **AI tendencies:** {.70, .25, .05}, blitz .30,\n  late hits .35.\n- **Offense:**\n  - QB #10 CLETUS THIBODEAUX: ARM −2, AIM −1, SPD +2. A scrambler.\n  - RB #44 BIG BERTHA BOUDREAUX: the boss; bulky 1.6; STR 10, SPD 6, ACC 4. Special MUDSLIDE.\n  - WR #80 CRAWDAD COMEAUX.\n  - WR #84 SKEETER LANDRY.\n  - C #60 GUMBO GUIDRY JR.\n  - G #71 BOUDIN BROUSSARD.\n  - G #75 TOOTIE TRAHAN.\n- **Defense:**\n  - DE #90 BAYOU BILLY BREAUX.\n  - NT #98 HOG JAW HEBERT.\n  - DE #92 CATFISH CORMIER.\n  - LB #51 MOSSY MOUTON.\n  - LB #57 RUSTY ROBICHAUX.\n  - CB #21 PIROGUE PREJEAN.\n  - S #33 GATOR BAIT GUILLORY.\n- **K** #8 BOOTS BOUDREAUX (Bertha's cousin).\n- **Cast:** Coach \"GATOR\" GUIDRY (an alligator-hide cap in green, a toothpick). Mascot HAMBONE (hog head).\n\n**3. NEON NITE OWLS** (NEO)\n- **Colors:** black `#1a1a2a`, neon cyan `#3af0f0` (glowing), magenta trim `#f03ab0`. The helmet is black with a\n  cyan glow stripe, the pants black.\n- **Logo:** neon owl eyes. **Home:** Afterglow Arena. **Chant:** \"HOOT-HOOT!\"\n- **Team modifier:** SPD +2 and HND +1 on QB, RB, WR, CB and S; STR −1 on OL and DL. **AI tendencies:**\n  {.25, .65, .10}, blitz .15, late hits .10.\n- **Offense:**\n  - QB #1 LUMEN LOPEZ: ARM 9, AIM 9. Special NIGHT VISION.\n  - RB #26 STROBE STEVENS.\n  - WR #11 ZAP ZAPATA: SPD 10, ACC 9. Special AFTERBURNER.\n  - WR #17 PIXEL PARK.\n  - C #55 BASS DROP BAKER.\n  - G #64 SUBWOOFER SMITH.\n  - G #68 REVERB REYES.\n- **Defense:**\n  - DE #93 NEON NIKKI NAKAMURA.\n  - NT #96 BLACKLIGHT BRUNO.\n  - DE #99 GLOWSTICK GUS.\n  - LB #50 LASER LARUE.\n  - LB #58 DISCO DAN.\n  - CB #2 SPARKLE SPARKS.\n  - S #20 MIDNIGHT MOSS.\n- **K** #4 RAVE RAVENSWOOD.\n- **Cast:** Coach DJ HOOT (headphones, sunglasses at night). Mascot HOOTY (owl head with glowing eyes).\n\n**4. GLACIER BAY YETIS** (GLB)\n- **Colors:** ice blue `#8ac8f0`, white `#f0f4f8`, navy trim `#2a3a6a`. The helmet is white with an ice-blue stripe,\n  the pants navy.\n- **Logo:** a yeti footprint. **Home:** Frostbite Field. **Chant:** \"BRRR! BRRR!\"\n- **Team modifier:** STR +2 and TCK +2 on DL and LB; HND +1 on everyone (ball security); SPD −1 on everyone.\n  **AI tendencies:** {.50, .45, .05}, blitz .45, late hits .15.\n- **Offense:**\n  - QB #9 SLEET SORENSEN.\n  - RB #30 PLOW PETERSON.\n  - WR #82 FLURRY FINN.\n  - WR #87 ICICLE IVERSEN.\n  - C #61 TUNDRA THORSON.\n  - G #70 PERMAFROST PAULSEN.\n  - G #77 GLACIER GUNDERSON.\n- **Defense:**\n  - DE #99 AVALANCHE: the boss; bulky 1.8, a beard; STR 10, SPD 6, TCK 9. Special SNOWPLOW. He speaks only in\n    growls.\n  - NT #94 BERG BJORKLUND.\n  - DE #91 HAILSTORM HANSEN.\n  - LB #53 FROSTY FJELD.\n  - LB #59 SNOWBALL SVENSSON.\n  - CB #23 POWDER PEDERSEN.\n  - S #36 WHITEOUT WALLIN.\n- **K** #5 SNOWSHOE SAMUELSSON.\n- **Cast:** Coach BJORN ICEBERG (fur coat, speaks in proverbs). Mascot ABOMINABLE AL.\n\n**5. GOLD COAST DYNASTY** (GCD; the final boss team)\n- **Colors:** gold `#f0c040`, black `#18161e`, white trim `#f4f4f0`. The helmet is gold with a black stripe, the\n  pants black.\n- **Logo:** a crown on a football. **Home:** The Mega Dome. **Chant:** \"DY-NAS-TY!\"\n- **Team modifier:** +1 to everything. **AI tendencies:** {.45, .50, .05}, blitz .30, late hits .20 (sneaky).\n- **Offense:**\n  - QB #12 BROCK STERLING III: the boss; ARM 10, AIM 9, AWR 8. Special GOLDEN SPIRAL. The owner's son: smug, never\n    been hit.\n  - RB #28 CHASE MONEY.\n  - WR #13 TREY GOLD: SPD +1.\n  - WR #19 PRESTON PLATINUM.\n  - C #52 BLUE CHIP BIXBY.\n  - G #67 TRUST FUND TUCKER.\n  - G #74 OFFSHORE OSGOOD.\n- **Defense:**\n  - DE #90 GOLDEN GATE GRAYSON.\n  - NT #97 VAULT VANCE.\n  - DE #94 DIAMOND DUKE.\n  - LB #55 \"THE MOUNTAIN\" MALU FALEOLO: the boss; bulky 1.7; STR 9, TCK 10, SPD 6. Special SEISMIC SACK.\n  - LB #50 ROYCE ROLLINS.\n  - CB #22 SILVER SPOON SINCLAIR.\n  - S #29 HEDGE FUND HARRINGTON.\n- **K** #1 PENNY PINCHER PERKINS: KCK 9.\n- **Cast:** Coach PRESCOTT PRIMROSE (a cashmere sweater over the shoulders). Owner MONTGOMERY STERLING II (a gold\n  suit, a cane; he wants Tumbleweed Field for a parking lot). Mascot GOLDIE (a gold lion head).\n\n**6. THE SCRUBS** (PRC; the practice squad: drills and the chapter 1 scrimmage only, hidden in exhibition)\n- **Colors:** grey practice jerseys `#8a8a90`, red trim `#c83a3a`. **Logo:** a whistle with a \"P\".\n- **Team modifier:** −2 to everything. **AI tendencies:** {.60, .40, 0}, blitz .10, late hits 0.\n- **Players:** BACKUP BOB, SCOUT TEAM SCOTT, PRACTICE PAT, CLIPBOARD CARL, WATERBOY WALT, DUMMY DAN, FILLER FRANK,\n  BENCH BRENDA, TRYOUT TROY, SPARE SPENCER, UNDERSTUDY URSULA, DEPTH CHART DEV, SUB SUSIE, PINNIE PETE, and the\n  kicker LONG SHOT LARRY. Numbers 60–99.\n\n**Other cast:** the announcers CHET THUNDERBUNS (play-by-play) and LOU \"THE TOE\" DIGGS (color). Head ref ZEBRA ZEKE\nand two more refs. A cheer squad of 4 per team in team colors with pom-poms. The Mega Dome's marching band of 8\n(bass drums and horns drawn by the gear hook). Photographers, a chain gang of 2, TV camera operators.\n\n### 18.2 Stadiums (`12-data-stadiums.js`)\n| | TUMBLEWEED FIELD | THE HOG WALLOW | AFTERGLOW ARENA | FROSTBITE FIELD | THE MEGA DOME |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Home | Fiascos | Mudhogs | Nite Owls | Yetis | Dynasty |\n| Light | dusk, ambient .62, warm sun from the west; a night variant for the prologue (.3, one flickering light) | overcast .55 | night .35, 4 towers, neon colors | cold day .5, towers | indoor .55, cool white, 6 sweeping spots |\n| Weather | clear | rain .6, wind .2, lightning .1 | clear | snow .7, wind .3 | none |\n| Field | worn grass, dirt patches | mud blotches between the hashes and at midfield (`mud`), shiny puddle decals | dark synthetic turf, glowing yard lines | snow-dusted grass, ice strips by the sidelines (`ice`), footprints | pristine turf, gold end zones, a giant crown at midfield |\n| Backdrop | a sunset sky, mesas, desert hills, cactus silhouettes | a grey sky, bald cypress with moss, fog | a city skyline at night with lit windows, neon billboards | snowy mountains and animated northern lights (green and purple bands) | the dome's dark ceiling truss with lights, banners |\n| Stands | 3 tiers of wooden bleachers (`plank`), 35% full (100% in the ending) | 5 tin-roof tiers (`metal`), 80%, ponchos | 7 concrete tiers with neon trims, 90%, glow sticks | 6 tiers, 75%, parkas and fur hats | 8 concrete tiers, 100%, gold and black sections |\n| Props | a water tower, a pickup truck, string lights, the hand-flipped scoreboard, hay bales, cacti, an old bench | an airboat, crab traps (crates), a smoking grill, lanterns, a HOG WALLOW sign | neon signs (HOOT, AFTERGLOW), laser emitters (sweeping emissive lines), a DJ booth (speakers, a table), towers | snow-capped pines, a plow (the bulldozer shape in blue), heaters (fire drums), a yeti ice sculpture (crystal) | 4 pyro cannons, the inflatable helmet tunnel, the indoor blimp, the jumbotron, TV cameras, confetti cannons, the trophy stage (the ending) |\n| Music | DUST DEVIL STOMP | SWAMP STOMP | NEON NIGHTDRIVE | FROSTBITE FANFARE | MEGA DOME ANTHEM |\n| Special | crickets at night | lightning, puddle splashes | LIGHTS OUT (ch3, and a Dev toggle), lasers on TDs | breath puffs, slippery edges | pyro on scores, the halftime band, the blimp's message board |\n\n### 18.3 Plays (`11-data-plays.js`; coordinates in yards from the ball spot, x downfield, y + to the offense's right)\n**Offensive formations** (C, LG and RG are always at `[-0.6, 0]`, `[-0.8, -1.4]`, `[-0.8, 1.4]`):\n\n| Formation | QB | RB | WR1 | WR2 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| PRO | [-1.4, 0] | [-6, 0] | [-0.8, -13] | [-0.8, 12] |\n| SHOTGUN | [-5, 0] | [-5, 1.8] | [-0.8, -13] | [-0.8, 12] |\n| TIGHT | [-1.4, 0] | [-5, 0] | [-0.8, -6] | [-0.8, 3.4] |\n| SPREAD | [-5, 0] | [-0.8, 7] | [-0.8, -15] | [-0.8, 15] |\n\n| Kick formation | Slots |\n|---|---|\n| PUNT | the K replaces the QB at [-12, 0]; RB up-back [-5, 1.5]; WR1 and WR2 gunners at [-0.8, ∓20] |\n| FIELD GOAL | QB holder [-7, 0]; K [-9.5, -1.2]; RB wing [-1, -2.6]; WR2 wing [-1, 2.6]; WR1 sits out |\n| KICKOFF | the defense unit with the K for the NT; the K at [-6, 0] behind the spot; the others on the line at y −20, −12, −5, 5, 12, 20 |\n\n**Offensive plays** (QB reads in order; `readT` is when reading starts):\n\n| Tab | Play | Formation | Assignments |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| RUN | HB DIVE | PRO | QB hands off at 0.45 s, then fakes a drop to [-5, 1]. RB carries [-2.5, 0.6] → [2, 0.8] → [8, 0.8]. C drives the NT. LG seals DE1 (drive [0.3, -1]). RG climbs to LB2. WR1 blocks the CB, WR2 the S. |\n| RUN | HB SWEEP | PRO | QB pitches at 0.3 s. RB carries [-5, 4] → [-1, 11] → [6, 13]. LG pulls [-1.8, 1.5] → [0.5, 9], then leads. C reaches the NT. RG seals DE2 inside. WR2 crack-blocks LB2. WR1 blocks the CB. |\n| RUN | HB DRAW | SHOTGUN | QB drops to [-6.5, 0] and hands off at 0.9 s. RB waits, then carries [-4.5, 0.5] → [3, 0] → [9, 0]. The OL pass-sets for 0.9 s, then run-blocks the nearest man. WR1 and WR2 run go routes to clear out. |\n| RUN | QB SNEAK | TIGHT | QB keeps: [0.5, 0.3] → [4, 0.3]. RB leads into his back. The OL drives straight ahead. WRs block. |\n| RUN | COUNTER | PRO | QB hands off at 0.55 s. RB steps [-6, -1.5], then cuts: [-4, 0.5] → [1, 2.6] → [8, 3.5]. LG pulls [-2, 0] → [0, 3] and kicks out DE2. C blocks the NT. RG blocks LB1. WRs block the CB and S. |\n| RUN | TOSS | SHOTGUN | QB tosses at 0.2 s. RB carries [-5, -4] → [0, -11] → [6, -13]. WR1 crack-blocks LB1. C and LG reach left. RG cuts off the NT. WR2 blocks the S. |\n| PASS | SLANTS | SHOTGUN | Drop [-6, 0]; reads WR2, WR1, RB; readT 0.6. WR1 [2.5, -13] → [9, -6]. WR2 [2.5, 12] → [9, 5]. RB flat [-2, 5] → [1, 10]. |\n| PASS | CURLS | SHOTGUN | Drop [-6.5, 0]; reads WR1, WR2, RB. WR1 [11, -13] → [9, -12]. WR2 [11, 12] → [9, 11]. RB swing [-3, -6] → [1, -11]. |\n| PASS | DEEP POST | PRO | Drop [-7, 0]; reads WR2, WR1, RB; readT 1.0. WR1 post [12, -13] → [28, -3]. WR2 go [35, 12]. RB blocks 1.2 s, then [2, 3] → [5, 6]. |\n| PASS | MESH | SHOTGUN | Reads WR1, WR2, RB. WR1 crosses [5, -13] → [5, 10]. WR2 crosses [7, 12] → [7, -10]. RB wheel [-3, 5] → [2, 10] → [18, 12]. |\n| PASS | OUT & UP | SHOTGUN | Reads WR2, WR1, RB; readT 0.9. WR2 [8, 12] → [8, 16] → [30, 17]. WR1 dig [12, -13] → [12, -2]. RB flat [-1, -4] → [2, -9]. |\n| PASS | QUICK OUTS | SHOTGUN | Drop [-5.5, 0]; reads WR2, WR1, RB; readT 0.5. WR1 [5, -13] → [5, -18]. WR2 [5, 12] → [5, 17]. RB seam [-1, 0.5] → [6, 0.5]. |\n| TRICK | HB SCREEN | SHOTGUN | Drop [-7.5, 0]; reads RB only; readT 1.4. RB to [-3, 5] and waits. The OL pass-sets 0.8 s, then releases to [1, 5], [0, 7], [2, 8] and leads. WR1 go [25, -13]. WR2 blocks. |\n| TRICK | FLEA FLICKER | PRO | QB hands off at 0.5 s. RB to [-2, 0.5] and pitches back to the QB at 1.3 s (automatic). QB at [-5, 0] reads WR1, WR2 from 1.8 s. WR1 [30, -8]. WR2 [25, 10]. The OL pass-blocks. |\n| TRICK | HOOK & LATERAL | SHOTGUN | Reads WR1 only; readT 0.9. WR1 hook [10, -12] → [9, -12]. WR2 [6, 12] → [9, -7], trailing behind WR1. After the catch, the lateral to WR2 (lb/rb; the CPU laterals by itself when WR2 is within 4 yd behind). RB blocks. |\n| TRICK | FUMBLEROOSKI | PRO | QB sets the ball down behind the C at 0.2 s. The C scoops it at 0.6 s and carries [1, -2] → [6, -4] → [12, -5]. QB and RB fake a sweep right ([-4, 6] → [0, 11]). Defenders are fooled for 0.8 s (they chase the RB). LG and RG block. |\n| TRICK | HAIL MARY | SPREAD | Drop [-9, 0]; reads WR1, WR2, RB; readT 2.2. WR1 [40, -2]. WR2 [42, 2]. RB [38, 0]. Maximum protection. |\n| SPECIAL | PUNT | PUNT | A long snap, the meter, the shield protects 1.5 s, then everyone covers. The gunners sprint. |\n| SPECIAL | FIELD GOAL | FIELD GOAL | The snap to the holder, the plant, the kick, the Kick Cam. |\n| SPECIAL | FAKE PUNT | PUNT | The punter rolls right and throws to WR1 at [8, -10], or runs when open. |\n| SPECIAL | KNEEL | PRO | The QB kneels at once; the clock runs `T.runoff`. |\nKickoff choices: DEEP KICK, SQUIB KICK, ONSIDE KICK. PAT choices: KICK XP, GO FOR 2.\n\n**Defensive formations** (x = yards off the ball on the defense's side; y in the offense's frame):\n\n| Formation | DE1 | NT | DE2 | LB1 | LB2 | CB | S |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| BASE 3-2-2 | [1.2, -2.8] | [1.0, 0] | [1.2, 2.8] | [4.5, -3.5] | [4.5, 3.5] | [6, over WR1] | [12, 0] |\n| PRESSURE | as BASE | as BASE | as BASE | [3, -2.5] | [3, 2.5] | [5, over WR1] | [10, over WR2] |\n| PREVENT | [1.2, -2.8] | [3, 0] | [1.2, 2.8] | [10, -8] | [10, 8] | [20, -8] | [20, 8] |\n| GOAL LINE | [0.9, -2.6] | [0.8, 0] | [0.9, 2.6] | [2.2, -1.5] | [2.2, 1.5] | [1.5, over WR1] | [3, over WR2] |\n\n**Defensive plays:**\n\n| Tab | Play | Formation | Assignments |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| BASE | COVER 2 | BASE | DE1 and DE2 contain, NT rushes the A gap. LB1 zone [6, -7] r5, LB2 zone [6, 7] r5. CB zone [16, -9] r10, S zone [16, 9] r10. |\n| BASE | MAN-TO-MAN | BASE | The DL rushes. CB on WR1, S on WR2, LB2 on the RB. LB1 robber zone [8, 0] r6. |\n| BASE | QB SPY | BASE | The DL rushes. LB1 spies the QB. CB on WR1, S on WR2, LB2 on the RB. |\n| PRESSURE | LB BLITZ | PRESSURE | The DL rushes; LB1 rushes the A gap, LB2 the B gap. CB on WR1, S on WR2. The RB is free. |\n| PRESSURE | ZONE BLITZ | PRESSURE | The NT drops to zone [5, 0] r6. LB1, DE1 and DE2 rush. LB2 zone [6, 6] r5. CB zone [15, -9] r10, S zone [15, 9] r10. |\n| PRESSURE | FIASCO BLITZ | PRESSURE | Six rush (everyone but the S). S zone [18, 0] r14. All or nothing. |\n| SPECIAL | PREVENT | PREVENT | DE1 and DE2 rush, the NT spies the QB. LB1 zone [10, -8] r7, LB2 zone [10, 8] r7, CB zone [22, -8] r12, S zone [22, 8] r12. |\n| SPECIAL | GOAL LINE | GOAL LINE | The DL and LBs fill the A, B and C gaps. CB on WR1, S on WR2. |\n| SPECIAL | FG BLOCK | GOAL LINE | Everyone rushes; the NT and LB1 jump at the kick. |\nReturn choices: RETURN MIDDLE, RETURN LEFT, RETURN RIGHT (the wedge's lane), HANDS TEAM (against an onside kick).\nPunt returns: RETURN, BLOCK THE PUNT.\n\n### 18.4 Fiasco Cards\nThe 8 cards and their rules are in §10.2. Each card needs its art (§12.8), its commentary line (§18.5) and its CPU\ntrigger.\n\n### 18.5 Commentary line banks (`16-data-lines.js`)\nWrite at least 8 lines for each of the main events (kickoff, bigRun, td, bigHit, megaHit, sack, int, fumble, drop,\nlateHit, hotOn, final) and at least 3 for the rest, in this voice: short (at most 48 characters a line, so they fit\ntwo caption lines at 10 feet), CHET in ALL CAPS and LOU in sentence case, puns and broadcast clichés, never cruel, no\nreal teams, players or leagues, no real broadcasters' catchphrases, and no profanity (\"DAG NABBIT!\" is as far as it\ngoes). The samples set the tone:\n\n| Event | Samples |\n|---|---|\n| kickoff | CHET: \"HERE WE GO! THE BALL IS IN THE AIR!\" · LOU: \"I used to kick those. Then my leg retired.\" |\n| bigRun | \"{player} FINDS DAYLIGHT!\" · \"THE 40! THE 30! SOMEBODY TACKLE HIM!\" · \"LOOK AT THOSE WHEELS!\" |\n| td | \"TOUCH! DOWN! {team}!\" · \"HE IS GONE! LIKE MY HAIRLINE!\" · \"SIX POINTS AND A SIDE OF FRIES!\" · LOU: \"Somebody call the mayor.\" |\n| bigHit | \"OH! THAT HIT HAD A ZIP CODE!\" · \"HE JUST GOT DELIVERED!\" · \"SOMEBODY CALL HIS MAMA!\" |\n| megaHit | \"OH, THE HUMANITY OF IT ALL!\" · \"HE'S IN ORBIT! NASA, ARE YOU SEEING THIS?\" · \"HIS HELMET IS IN A DIFFERENT AREA CODE!\" |\n| sack | \"SACKED! {player} PUTS HIM IN A BAG!\" · \"BROUGHT DOWN LIKE THE GROCERIES!\" |\n| int | \"PICKED OFF! {player} HAS IT!\" · \"THAT'S A GIFT WITH A BOW ON IT!\" · \"INTERCEPTED! HE'S TAKING IT TO THE HOUSE!\" |\n| fumble | \"FUMBLE! THE BALL IS LOOSE!\" · \"THAT'S A FIASCO, FOLKS!\" · \"BUTTERFINGERS!\" |\n| pile | \"WHO'S GOT IT?! THERE'S A PILE OF HUMANITY!\" · LOU: \"I see a shoe. I see an elbow. I see a sandwich?\" |\n| drop | \"DROPPED! RIGHT IN THE BREADBASKET!\" · LOU: \"Hands of stone, Chet. Granite.\" |\n| lateHit | \"THE WHISTLE BLEW, FOLKS! HE DID NOT CARE!\" · \"LATE HIT! AND THE REF JUST SHRUGS!\" |\n| hotOn | \"{player} IS BLAZING!\" · \"IS IT HOT IN HERE OR IS IT JUST {player}?\" · \"SOMEBODY GET A FIRE EXTINGUISHER!\" |\n| hotOff | \"AND THE FIRE IS OUT. RESET THE SMOKE ALARMS.\" |\n| card | ROCKET CLEATS \"THOSE SHOES ARE ILLEGAL IN FOUR STATES!\" · GLUE GLOVES \"NOTHING'S GETTING LOOSE NOW!\" · BRICK WALL \"WHERE'D THEY GET THE BRICKS?!\" · HOT SAUCE \"HE DRANK THE WHOLE BOTTLE!\" · MEGA HIT \"SOMEBODY'S GOING TO ORBIT!\" · BUTTERFINGERS \"THAT BALL IS SLICK AS A GREASED PIG!\" · MASCOT MAYHEM \"IS THAT {mascot} ON THE FIELD?! IT IS!\" · SUPER FOOT \"THAT LEG IS INSURED FOR A MILLION BUCKS!\" |\n| fiascoBreak | \"FIASCO BREAK! EVERY DISASTER IS AN OPPORTUNITY!\" |\n| fgGood / fgMiss | \"IT'S GOOD! RIGHT DOWN THE PIPE!\" · \"DOINK... AND IN! LUCKY, LUCKY!\" / \"NO GOOD! WIDE LEFT! WIDE EVERYTHING!\" |\n| punt | \"BOOMING PUNT!\" · LOU: \"Beautiful spiral. I'd know. I never had one.\" |\n| safety | \"SAFETY! TWO POINTS AND A LOT OF SHAME!\" |\n| firstDown / thirdLong / fourthDown / redZone | \"MOVE THE CHAINS!\" / \"THIRD AND A COUNTY MILE!\" / \"FOURTH DOWN! DECISION TIME!\" / \"RED ZONE! THE CROWD IS ON ITS FEET!\" |\n| halftime / final | \"THAT'S THE HALF! {team} LEADS {score}!\" / \"THAT'S THE BALL GAME! {team} WINS IT {score}!\" · close: \"WHAT A FINISH! I NEED A NAP!\" · blowout, LOU: \"That wasn't a game, Chet. That was a crime scene.\" |\n| specials | MUDSLIDE \"BERTHA IS BULLDOZING THROUGH!\" · AFTERBURNER \"ZAP JUST BROKE THE SOUND BARRIER!\" · SNOWPLOW \"AVALANCHE IS CLEARING THE ROAD!\" · GOLDEN SPIRAL \"THE GOLDEN SPIRAL! YOU CAN'T TOUCH IT!\" · SEISMIC SACK \"THAT ONE REGISTERED ON THE RICHTER SCALE!\" |\n| mascot, refDown, lightsOut | \"IS THAT A TUMBLEWEED ON THE FIELD?! AND IT'S ON FIRE!\" · \"AND THE REF GOES DOWN! HE'S FINE! HE'S... MOSTLY FINE!\" · \"THE LIGHTS ARE OUT AT THE AFTERGLOW!\" |\n| weather, idle | LOU: \"It's raining sideways, Chet.\" · LOU: \"I can't feel my microphone.\" · LOU: \"Football's a lot like life, Chet. Mostly running into things.\" |\n| incomplete, brokenTackle, pancake | \"INCOMPLETE. THE BALL HAD OTHER PLANS.\" · \"HE SHRUGGED HIM OFF LIKE A BAD HABIT!\" · \"PANCAKE! WITH SYRUP!\" |\n- **Refs** (babble plus a tiny speech bubble): \"FIRST DOWN!\", \"TOUCHDOWN!\", \"INCOMPLETE!\", \"BALL'S HERE!\", \"...SURE,\n  WHY NOT.\"\n- **QB cadences** (a small bubble over the QB): Hap \"PICKLE 7! PICKLE 7! HUT!\"; Brock \"GOLD! GOLD! HUT HUT!\"; Lumen\n  \"LIGHTS! CAMERA! HUT!\"; Cletus \"MUD 44! MUD 44! HUT!\"; Sleet \"COLD! COLDER! HUT!\"; others \"BLUE 42! SET... HUT!\"\n\n### 18.6 The story scripts (`14-data-story.js`; [stage directions] become E.Story `event` steps)\n**PROLOGUE: TUMBLEWEED FIELD, 11:58 PM.** [night, one flickering light, crickets; the team mopes at midfield]\n- CHET (radio): \"LIVE FROM TUMBLEWEED JUNCTION... WHERE FOOTBALL COMES TO DIE!\"\n- LOU (radio): \"Ninety-nine losses in a row, Chet. You have to admire the consistency.\"\n- MAMA PEARL: \"Ninety-nine losses, one leaky roof, and zero quit. That's my Fiascos.\"\n- [a gold golf cart rolls in; a bulldozer rumbles behind it, headlights on]\n- STERLING: \"Pearl! Sign the papers. This dirt patch would make a lovely parking lot.\"\n- MAMA PEARL: \"Over my pickled body, Montgomery.\"\n- BROCK: \"Dad, it smells like a pickle barrel exploded out here.\"\n- STERLING: \"Fine. The Fiasco Cup. Win it, keep your field. Lose it... and I pave it.\"\n- COACH BLUSTER: \"You got yourself a bet! ...Wait. What's the Fiasco Cup?\"\n- LOU (radio): \"Only the most over-the-top football tournament on Earth, Gus.\"\n- CHET (radio): \"FOUR GAMES! NO RULES! ONE TROPHY! IT'S THE FIASCO CUP!\"\n- MAMA PEARL: \"Then we need a quarterback. A real one.\"\n- [a spotlight finds HAP, who is carrying two pickle barrels]\n- HAP: \"I can throw a pickle barrel sixty yards. Does that count?\"\n- COACH BLUSTER: \"Kid... tryouts are at dawn.\" [title card: THE FIASCO CUP]\n\n**CH1 TRYOUTS.**\n- **Intro** [dawn, cones and dummies]:\n  - COACH: \"Listen up, Hazard! This is tryouts. You fail, you go back to pickles.\"\n  - COACH: \"First drill: run the cones. Then hit the turbo like it owes you money!\"\n- **Between drills,** one line each:\n  - D2: \"Hike it! The ball goes to the man in the backfield, not the man in the stands!\"\n  - D3: \"Spin, stiff arm, hurdle! Like a ballerina with anger issues!\"\n  - D4: \"See the button over his head? Press it! Football is easy!\"\n  - D5: \"Jump at the top! The ball's shadow tells you where!\"\n  - D6: \"Defense wins championships! Offense wins... also championships. Hit somebody!\"\n  - D7: \"Three taps, son. Power, then aim. Don't kick the holder. AGAIN.\"\n  - D8: \"Pick a play. Flip it. And Pearl's hot sauce? That's for emergencies.\"\n  - D9: \"One drive. Score, and you're my quarterback.\"\n- **Outro:**\n  - COACH: \"Hazard, you might be the worst thing to happen to this franchise...\"\n  - COACH: \"...which makes you the best thing to happen to this franchise.\"\n  - MAMA PEARL: \"Here, sugar. Pearl's Five-Alarm Hot Sauce. For emergencies only.\"\n  - [cards: HOT SAUCE and SUPER FOOT]\n\n**CH2 THE MUD BOWL.**\n- **Intro** [the press room at the Hog Wallow, rain drumming on the tin roof]:\n  - CHET: \"ROUND ONE! THE FIASCOS VISIT THE BAYOU MUDHOGS IN THE HOG WALLOW!\"\n  - GATOR: \"Y'all ever play in mud this deep? We got crawdads livin' in the end zone.\"\n  - BIG BERTHA: \"I'm gonna run through y'all like hot butter through grits.\"\n  - COACH: \"Grits don't tackle, ma'am. ...Do they?\"\n  - HAP: \"Coach, why are we wearing snorkels?\"\n  - COACH: \"Mud management, son. Tackle low, hold the ball tight, watch for the MUDSLIDE.\"\n  - LOU: \"Rain's coming in sideways, Chet. Fumbles are gonna fly like bats.\"\n- **Halftime** [the visitors' locker room]:\n  - COACH: \"We're {score} at the half! Somebody tell me what we do about it!\" [choice]\n  - The choices (each effect lasts the second half): **GROUND AND POUND** (+10% run blocking, carriers break\n    tackles +0.05), **AIR IT OUT** (catch +0.06, aim error ×0.9), **HIT 'EM HARDER** (tackle +0.05, Big Hit fumble\n    +5%), **TRICKERY** (draw a Fiasco Card).\n- **Win:**\n  - BIG BERTHA: \"Well I'll be. Y'all hit like a family reunion. Respect.\"\n  - GATOR: \"Come on back for the crawfish boil. Bring that rookie.\"\n  - CHET: \"THE FIASCOS WIN A FOOTBALL GAME! I REPEAT! THE FIASCOS WIN A FOOTBALL GAME!\"\n  - [card: MEGA HIT]\n- **Loss:** COACH: \"We got mud in places mud shouldn't go. Again!\"\n\n**CH3 LIGHTS OUT.**\n- **Intro** [the Afterglow tunnel, neon, bass thumping]:\n  - CHET: \"THE QUARTERFINAL! THE NEON NITE OWLS AT THE AFTERGLOW!\"\n  - DJ HOOT: \"Welcome to the Afterglow, small town. Hope your eyes can keep up.\"\n  - LUMEN: \"I see the open man in the dark. I AM the open man in the dark.\"\n  - ZAP: \"You blinked. I'm already in the end zone.\"\n  - [card: 3RD QUARTER. OWLS 21, FIASCOS 7]\n  - COACH: \"We're down fourteen because SOMEBODY slept through the first half!\"\n  - WHEELS: \"...I needed my beauty rest, Coach.\"\n- **In-game, at the 4th play of Q3** (radio, non-modal):\n  - CHET: \"WAIT, THE LIGHTS! THE LIGHTS ARE OUT AT THE AFTERGLOW!\"\n  - LOU: \"Looks like a tumbleweed tripped over the power cable, Chet.\"\n  - FUMBLES: [guilty tumbleweed noises]\n  - COACH: \"Glow paint! Everybody rub on the glow paint!\"\n  - [LIGHTS OUT for 3 plays]\n- **Win:**\n  - DJ HOOT: \"Respect, Tumbleweed. That comeback was a banger.\"\n  - ZAP: \"...Can I get your rookie's autograph? For my cousin. Not for me.\"\n  - [cards: ROCKET CLEATS and GLUE GLOVES]\n- **Loss:** COACH: \"Somebody turn the lights back on in your heads! Again!\"\n\n**CH4 FROSTBITE.**\n- **Intro** [Frostbite Field, snow, the northern lights]:\n  - CHET: \"THE SEMIFINAL! IT'S MINUS TWELVE AND THE HOT DOGS ARE FROZEN SOLID!\"\n  - ICEBERG: \"The glacier does not hurry. Yet it carves the valley.\"\n  - COACH BLUSTER: \"...Is that a threat or a fortune cookie?\"\n  - AVALANCHE: [a growl that shakes the snow off the roof]\n  - LOU: \"That's Avalanche. Seven feet tall. Speaks only in growls and sacks.\"\n  - [card: 4TH QUARTER, 1:30 LEFT. YETIS 20, FIASCOS 17. YOUR BALL ON YOUR 20]\n  - COACH: \"Ninety seconds, eighty yards. Get out of bounds to stop the clock!\"\n- **Win:**\n  - AVALANCHE: [a soft growl; he hands Hap a hand-knitted scarf]\n  - LOU: \"He knits, Chet. The big fella knits.\"\n  - [card: MASCOT MAYHEM]\n- **Loss:** COACH: \"Frozen solid. Thaw out and run it back!\"\n\n**CH5 THE FIASCO BOWL.**\n- **Intro** [the Mega Dome press conference, camera flashes]:\n  - CHET: \"THE FIASCO BOWL! SEVENTY THOUSAND FANS AND ONE BULLDOZER!\"\n  - BROCK: \"I've got a golden arm, a golden helmet, and a golden future.\"\n  - BROCK: \"You've got... pickles.\"\n  - HAP: \"And you've never been hit by a guy who hauls pickle barrels for a living.\"\n  - THE MOUNTAIN: \"I will fall on you. Like a mountain. Because I am THE MOUNTAIN.\"\n  - STERLING: \"Win and keep your little field, Pearl. Lose, and the bulldozer's warming up.\"\n  - MAMA PEARL: \"Warm it up all you like, Montgomery. It's gonna be a long, cold night.\"\n- **Halftime** [the visitors' locker room]:\n  - MAMA PEARL: \"Ninety-nine losses taught us one thing: how to get back up.\"\n  - COACH: \"So get back up! What's the plan?\" [the same 4 choices as CH2]\n- **Win** [the field, confetti, the trophy stage]:\n  - CHET: \"THE TUMBLEWEED FIASCOS ARE FIASCO CUP CHAMPIONS! I NEED TO SIT DOWN!\"\n  - LOU: \"You ARE sitting down, Chet.\"\n  - [the team dumps the sports-drink bucket on Coach Bluster]\n  - COACH: \"AAAAH! IT'S ORANGE! WHY IS IT ALWAYS ORANGE?!\"\n  - STERLING: \"This is a... a FIASCO!\" [he steps back off the stage into the victory cake]\n  - MAMA PEARL: \"Keep your bulldozer, Montgomery. We're keeping our field.\"\n  - BROCK: \"...Hey. Rookie. Nice arm.\"\n  - HAP: \"Nice cake, Brock.\"\n  - [EPILOGUE card: TUMBLEWEED FIELD, ONE YEAR LATER. ATTENDANCE: SOLD OUT. The full bleachers chant \"FI-AS-CO!\",\n    then the credits roll over a montage of the season's highlight clips.]\n- **Loss:**\n  - STERLING: \"Start the engines!\"\n  - COACH: \"Not today! Run it back!\"\n\n**The credits roll** (`credits` scene): the FIASCO FOREVER ballad. The About pages scroll as credits (§14.10), over\nreplays of the player's best story highlight clips (or the attract segments when there are none). Any button speeds\nit up 4×, and ○ held for 1 s skips it.\n\n---\n\n## 19. Build order and milestones\nBuild in this order. Each milestone ends with the one test command passing (§21) and its exit check. Systems before\ncontent, and the riskiest systems first. Placeholders are fine *between* milestones; none may remain at the end.\nDon't commit to git unless you're asked to (the folder is inside a shared repository).\n\n| M | Milestone | Build | Exit check |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| M0 | Setup | the dev folder; sparse fetches; the engine copy; E1 and E2; the mocap set and the store props cut; `build.mjs`; `test/run.mjs` and `test/lib/context.mjs`; `index.html`; `package.json` with Playwright | `npm test` prints a count line; `node build.mjs` writes the deliverable and it boots from `file://` |\n| M1 | Field and athletes | the stadium builder with Tumbleweed Field (floor paint, stands, crowd v1, goalposts, pylons, sideline props, backdrop, lights); the views; E3 and E4 gear; 14 athletes in formation with team uniforms; the ball drawn; movement, turbo and collisions; one human athlete; the camera following | tests: yard ↔ world, formation spots, collision separation, speed caps. Screenshots of the formation at 1920×1080 and 1280×720 read clearly at TV distance |\n| M2 | Football core | the match state machine, rules and clock; `02-tuning.js` and the first Dev sliders (E7); all formations and plays as data; actions (hike, handoff, throw, catch, tackle, dive); AI v1 (blocking, routes, coverage, rush, pursuit, QB reads, carrier steering); kicks (the meter, the Kick Cam, the FG test, kickoffs, punts, returns, touchbacks); INTs and fumbles v1; PATs; HUD v1; the play-call UI v1; the CPU coach; the Play Lab | a whole exhibition (Fiascos vs Mudhogs at Tumbleweed) plays start to finish against the CPU with keyboard, pad, and mouse for passing and menus; the Play Lab bands pass; no stuck plays |\n| M3 | Netcode spike | `80-net.js`: the adapter, roles, snapshots, prediction, the action log, play-call and kick sync, leave, time-up, end, finish; the hub card scene (functional); the fake hub and the loopback test; the browser harness runner | the net suite passes; all 4 harness configurations give `__hubCheck.pass === true` on the bundle. If not, §20 risk 2's decision is made now |\n| M4 | The over-the-top layer | every action in §7.4; Big and Mega Hits with FX, punch-ins and slow motion; fumbles and pile-ups; Hot Streak; the Fiasco Meter and the 8 cards; boss specials; celebrations; mascots; refs; divots, footprints, breath; replays and the highlight reel; commentary text and pops; crowd excitement, the Wave, signs | each feature's tests (§21.2 `actions`, `ots`, `replay`); a filmstrip of each new animation is clean |\n| M5 | Front end and UX | the title, main menu, exhibition setup, play-call final, HUD final, kick meter, results, Hall of Fiasco, About/Credits (wired to `FF_ABOUT`), settings with E2 and E9, glyph chips and device prompts everywhere, mouse hover and click everywhere, the touch-only gate, the pause items, Help; the attract mode with all 16 segments | the `ui`, `control` and `attract` suites; screenshots of every screen at both sizes |\n| M6 | Audio | all songs, layers and stings; every sfx; the crowd bed and chants; E5 and E6; the babble synth and every profile; the dialog voice hook; the commentary voice; the Voices, Crowd and Commentary settings | the `audio` suite (no unknown-sound warnings); a listening pass through every scene |\n| M7 | Content and story | all 6 teams (rosters, looks, logos, mascots, cast); all 5 stadiums (dressing, weather, light, backdrops, music); story mode (the board, the loadout, the prologue, chapters 1–5, the cutscene sets and scripts, halftime choices, rewards, stars, loss and retry, the ending, the credits); drills D1–D9 with bots; Practice; saves and Continue | the `data` and `story` suites (the scripted whole-game playthrough reaches the credits) |\n| M8 | Multiplayer complete | local 1–4 polish (prompts and colors per player, the co-op rules, keyboard halves); hub polish (card art, seat colors and names, the session overlay, Create + Options, stats and awards, results) | the `net` and `control` suites; the harness passes on the new bundle; a manual 2-player local game |\n| M9 | Dev, balance, polish, ship | every Dev page; balance against §22.2 with the sliders, the Play Lab and `test/balance.mjs`; the look pass (check.mjs notes, filmstrips, screenshots); the final `about.json`; the final bundle | the full `npm test -- --browser` passes; the §23 checklist is all ticked |\n","numLines":420,"startLine":1818,"totalLines":2515}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014f2GTgwTwvHr1tXMrSgYRL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
