{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi1wFZruVxByjL6kHNGv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HZAC3zJYimUHjEm4Nu6TBg","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-070556__xb697dc/work/PLAN.md","offset":2237,"limit":280},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19342,"cache_read_input_tokens":94292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19342},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49428dbe-779b-4248-8ac3-c582018d3c3d","uuid":"08e1f138-40cb-4d78-8e04-153f4b79d036","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:06:36.171Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi1wF9YvbD9NwjacXU92","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01HZAC3zJYimUHjEm4Nu6TBg":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-070556__xb697dc/work/PLAN.md","offset":2237,"limit":280}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HZAC3zJYimUHjEm4Nu6TBg","type":"tool_result","content":"2237\t\n2238\t---\n2239\t\n2240\t## 20. Risks and how to de-risk them\n2241\t| # | Risk | Why it's risky | De-risk | Fallback |\n2242\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n2243\t| 1 | The football AI feels broken: stuck plays, clumps, no blocking | many interacting agents, the heart of the game | build it first (M2) in the Play Lab with overlays; keep behaviors small and data-driven; delay perception for realism; the Monte Carlo bands are tests; tune with sliders | simplify a behavior (zone-only coverage, timed sheds) before shipping a stuck play; never ship a play that can stall |\n2244\t| 2 | Shared-world netcode under latency and loss | real-time physics across devices | spike it at M3, before content; the arena example's prediction model; action logs that survive loss; a snapshot size budget; the Node loopback with a simulated network; the harness | if prediction can't be made stable by M3's end, ship host-authoritative rendering without prediction (it passes the harness; it feels laggier). Only if the shared world can't pass the harness at all: a parallel-mode \"TWO-MINUTE DRILL\" round (each player scores what they can against the CPU in 2:00). Decide at M3, write the decision in ENGINE-CHANGES.md's notes and on the About screen. |\n2245\t| 3 | Animation quality: retargeted clips on bulky rigs, PoseFX pops | new animation | a filmstrip of every clip on every build at M1 and M4; ease all weights; Dev deep links that loop a pose | replace any clip that looks wrong with the engine's procedural poses and E.MOVES |\n2246\t| 4 | Readability at 10 feet: small characters on a busy field | the TV distance | screenshots at 1080p and 720p from M1; text-size rules (§14.1); panels behind text; E1 and E9 | zoom the default camera in (`camera.start` 1.15) and simplify the field paint |\n2247\t| 5 | The babble voices sound harsh or annoying | synthesis | a voice test page (a Dev page: say any line with any profile) early in M6; soft envelopes, a bus lowpass, short syllables; the Voices slider; subtitles always on | turn the rate down and use Animalese blips only (letter blips through formants) |\n2248\t| 6 | Content volume: 6 teams, 5 stadiums, 5 chapters, 35 shapes, 13 songs, 400+ lines | time | content as data with validation; base ratings plus modifiers; content passes after the systems are done (M7); reuse sets (the locker room recolored) | cut variety, never features: fewer props per stadium, 6 lines per event instead of 8 |\n2249\t| 7 | Engine changes break the engine | a shared base | small isolated changes; after each, `node tools/check.mjs kits/sports.html` and `node kits/test.mjs sports` | revert the change and do it in game code |\n2250\t| 8 | The single-file bundle | `</script>`, the size, `session.js` integrity, `file://` | the build escapes and checks session.js's hash; check.mjs on the bundle from `file://`; no fetches at runtime | — |\n2251\t| 9 | Slow headless tests | 14 rigs at 120 Hz | fast mode (presentation off); short quarters through scenario overrides; cheats to finish chapters | split the playthrough into one suite per chapter |\n2252\t| 10 | Replays mutate or desync the sim | shared state | presentation-only playback from recorded frames; the hash test | — |\n2253\t| 11 | View switches stall (floor rebakes) | the Kick Cam and replays | measure the rebake in a test; if over 100 ms, pre-bake the Kick Cam views in a boot step | a dissolve hides it |\n2254\t| 12 | 10-foot scaling breaks the Shell's layout | CSS | `clamp()`; screenshots of pause, settings, controls and Dev at both sizes | lower the scale to 1.4 |\n2255\t| 13 | Touch-only false positives (touch laptops) | detection | require no fine pointer and no key or pad; any key or pad unlocks | — |\n2256\t| 14 | The hub card's ready timing | protocol | `ready()` only after the boot steps and the match build; the harness checks it | — |\n2257\t| 15 | The violence reads as mean | tone | slapstick only: stars, flying helmets, pancakes, no blood, no injuries beyond \"Dinged\"; the comfort settings respected | — |\n2258\t\n2259\t---\n2260\t\n2261\t## 21. Testing\n2262\t\n2263\t### 21.1 The one command\n2264\t`npm test` (that is, `node test/run.mjs`) prints **only failures** (`FAIL suite › test: detail`) and one final line:\n2265\t`N passed, M failed (12.3 s)`. The exit code is 1 on any failure.\n2266\t- `node test/run.mjs rules ai` runs only those suites. Rerun only the suites covering code you changed. Run the full\n2267\t  set at the end of each milestone.\n2268\t- `--browser` adds the Playwright suites. `--seed n` reseeds.\n2269\t- `test/lib/context.mjs` builds a vm context with stand-ins: `window`, `addEventListener` (records listeners),\n2270\t  `location { hash }`, `matchMedia` (configurable, for the touch-only tests), `navigator { getGamepads: () => [],\n2271\t  maxTouchPoints }`, `performance`, and a `console` whose warnings are collected (an engine warning fails the test\n2272\t  unless it is listed as expected).\n2273\t- It loads `vendor/` and `src/` in `index.html`'s order (parse the script tags, as `kits/test.mjs` does) and returns\n2274\t  `{ game, FF, E, I, step(s), tap(a), hold(a, on), feed(...), snap() }`.\n2275\t\n2276\t### 21.2 The suites\n2277\t| Suite | What it asserts |\n2278\t|---|---|\n2279\t| `boot` | boots headless; the boot steps run; every scene enters and exits with `game.go(..., { fade: 0 })`; deep links parse; no errors |\n2280\t| `data` | every team (15 unique numbers, ratings 1–10, hex colors, a valid logo), play (every slot assigned, coordinates in range, reads pointing at eligible slots, 3 linemen on the line), stadium (props exist, songs exist), card, chapter (nodes, cast and scenarios exist), drill, line (≤ 48 characters, known variables) and attract segment is valid |\n2281\t| `rules` | downs and distance, first downs, a turnover on downs, TDs (run and catch), PAT kick and 2-point, FG good, no good and doink, safety, touchback, out of bounds, the incomplete spot, INT and fumble possession, the clock (live, runoff, stops, the last-30 s rule), quarters, halftime ends switching, OT sudden death, the final. All through scenarios with forced outcomes |\n2282\t| `physics` | speeds by rating and turbo, turbo drain and regen, collision separation after 1 s of pushing, a pass with no aim error landing within 1 unit of its target, bounces, kick distances by power, FG geometry |\n2283\t| `actions` | every action's pose code and timing; a spin evades a frontal tackle in its window and not outside it; the stiff-arm bonus; a hurdle evades low dives; a Big Hit launches and its fumble roll is ×3 (seeded Monte Carlo within ±0.05); strip; the jump-catch window; laterals; the late-hit window; pile-up resolution; the 3-press meter |\n2284\t| `ai` | the Play Lab bands (§8.6) for every offense × defense pair (n = 30, seeded, fast mode); the coach's choice in 20 canonical situations (4th & 15 at your 30: punt; 4th & 1 at their 40, late and trailing: go; down 2 after a late TD: go for 2) |\n2285\t| `ots` | Hot Streak starts at 3 big plays and ends on its reset events; the Fiasco Meter fills and draws a card; each card's effect is measurable (ROCKET CLEATS gives +20% speed, and so on); boss specials fire under their conditions and keep to once per drive or half; Dinged; cosmetics (the flying helmet, divots, breath) don't change the sim hash |\n2286\t| `replay` | the sim hash is equal before and after a replay; the frame count; the highlight reel keeps the top 5 |\n2287\t| `control` | switching (auto, b2, a mouse click through `FF.control.pickAt`); the co-op assignment; control after turnovers; keyboard halves get b1–b4, turbo and lb; prompt labels per device and glyph setting (PlayStation by default gives `✕`, Xbox gives `A`, the keyboard gives Space or K, r1–r4 on a full keyboard) |\n2288\t| `ui` | every menu navigable by keyboard taps, pad taps, and the mouse (`input.feed('move' / 'down' / 'up', x, y)`: hover focuses, a click picks); the title's 10 s idle starts the attract mode and any input leaves it; touch-only mode shows the message and the Settings button; the settings specs hold the game's settings, and `glyphs` defaults to PlayStation with Xbox as the other option (`game.settings.spec('glyphs')`; headless the Shell keeps only screen names, so the Settings screen's look is checked by screenshot, §21.6); `game.menu('settings')` opens the screen named `settings` (`game.shell.screen`); the pause items (`menu.items()`) include Dev Mode outside sessions and not in them |\n2289\t| `audio` | every sfx and song named in data exists (no unknown-sound warnings during a full attract cycle); the voice planner's plans are deterministic for every profile; Commentary Off plans nothing; a hub `end` leaves the audio muted and the music stopped |\n2290\t| `dev` | every Dev action runs; each slider changes `FF.T` live (`game.settings.set('dev.speedBase', v)` changes the sim's top speed); Reset all restores the defaults; the Play Lab returns stats; the cheats work |\n2291\t| `attract` | the whole loop runs headless and each segment's key event fires (TD, fumble, pile-up, doink FG, INT, late hit, ref down, mascot sack, lights out, Snowplow, the story line, the halftime show, Seismic Sack, the trophy, the records); nothing is saved; any input leaves within one step |\n2292\t| `story` (**the scripted whole-game playthrough**) | title → menu → STORY → NEW GAME → the prologue (confirm taps) → the ch1 drills by their bots → chapters 2–5 with the human side on autopilot (the CPU brains drive its athletes through intents, the play calls are COACH SAYS) with `godMode` and `forceCatch` for that side and `quarterLength: 20` → halftime choices → outros → the ending → the credits → the menu. It checks the chapter flags, the rewards, stars ≥ 1, `game.saves.latest()` with chapter 5 done, Big Heads unlocked, the records, no errors, and no NaN positions (snapshots every 120 steps). Also a loss in one chapter (the CPU forced to win) → THAT'S A FIASCO → RETRY works. Also a 2-player local exhibition (`game.addPlayer({ keys: 'right' })`) to the results and REMATCH. |\n2293\t| `net` | 2–4 vm contexts with a fake `AIHub` (`test/lib/fakehub.mjs`: `active`, `connect` → info, `ready`, `answer`, `on`, `send(data, { to, reliable })`, `time`, `finish`, `rng(label)`, `server`) over a bus with 150 ± 50 ms latency, 5% loss for unreliable messages, reliable ordering, the 20/s burst-40 limiter, 16 KB maximum, and the card → start → time-up → end flow. Cases: 2 players; 4 players with latency and loss; the host leaving; a server host; a player leaving mid-match (his athletes go CPU); time-up (finish within grace). It checks traffic both ways, ≤ 18 msgs/s per copy, snapshots ≤ 1,100 bytes, the predicted athlete within 2 yd of the host's 95% of the time when not locked, that play calls and kicks arrive, `finish` called once with valid standings (every player once) and scores, every copy ended, nothing sent after `end`, and no errors |\n2294\t| `browser` (with `--browser`) | (1) `node tools/check.mjs <deliverable> --size 1920x1080` and `--size 1280x720`: exit 0, no errors, look notes saved. (2) The deep links `#match`, `#drill/passing`, `#attract`, `#story/ch5` play 4 s without errors. (3) The hub harness: copy `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` and the deliverable into `test/hub/serve/`. Start `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` there (read the port from its output, keep its PID), and confirm that `GET /<deliverable>` contains `AMERICAN FOOTBALL FIASCO`. Open `harness.html?game=<deliverable>&players=2&auto=1`, then `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, the same with `&scenario=host-leave`, and `&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1` (add `&limit=90` to keep rounds short). Wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`. Assert `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`, printing the failed checks otherwise. Stop the server by its PID. |\n2295\t\n2296\t### 21.3 Devices in tests\n2297\t- Keyboard and pad go through `input.tap` / `input.hold`. Set `input.lastDevice` to check prompts.\n2298\t- The mouse goes through `input.feed('move' | 'down' | 'up', x, y, { button })`.\n2299\t- Headless there is no last frame for `r.pick`, so the game has its own `FF.control.pickAt(sx, sy)`: it projects\n2300\t  athletes through the current view and hit-tests their bounds. Use it in both the browser and tests, with `r.pick`\n2301\t  as a cross-check in the browser.\n2302\t\n2303\t### 21.4 Determinism\n2304\tTests seed `FF.rng` through the scenario's `seed` and never read the wall clock. The kits' `proof()` pattern\n2305\t(`kits/sports.js`) shows that the same seed gives the same match hash twice. Keep a `FF.sim.hash()`.\n2306\t\n2307\t### 21.5 Filmstrips (animation review; not in the one command)\n2308\t`node tools/filmstrip.mjs <page>#drill/moves --steps \"wait:800 rec:16:2 ...\" --seed 1` for the spin, stiff arm,\n2309\thurdle and dive, and a Dev deep link `#dev/pose/<CODE>` that loops one pose code on every build, to review each\n2310\t§12.3 row.\n2311\t\n2312\t### 21.6 Screenshots (only for what a script can't judge)\n2313\t`npm run shots` (`test/browser/shots.mjs`) saves to `shots/`, at 1920×1080 and 1280×720:\n2314\t- the title, the main menu, the exhibition setup, team select;\n2315\t- the play call (offense, defense, split);\n2316\t- live play at each of the 5 stadiums, a Big Hit, a TD celebration, a replay, the Kick Cam, a pile-up, a Blazing\n2317\t  player, LIGHTS OUT;\n2318\t- each cutscene set, the results, Hall of Fiasco, the About pages;\n2319\t- the pause menu, Settings (with Button symbols), the Dev screens;\n2320\t- the touch-only title (`--size 390x844@3`), the hub card.\n2321\tReview them against §12.1, and fix what reads badly.\n2322\t\n2323\t---\n2324\t\n2325\t## 22. Tuning defaults (the Dev sliders; `02-tuning.js`)\n2326\t| Group | Key: default (min–max) |\n2327\t|---|---|\n2328\t| Movement | `speedBase` 92 (60–140), `speedPerSpd` 7 (3–12), `accelBase` 520 (200–1200), `turboMult` 1.25 (1–1.6), `turboDrain` 0.45 (0.1–1.5), `turboRegen` 0.22 (0.05–1), `turboDeadRefill` 0.35 (0–1), `carrySpeedMult` 0.96 (0.8–1), `backpedalMult` 0.65 (0.4–1) |\n2329\t| Passing | `lobSpeed` 240 (150–350), `bulletSpeed` 400 (250–550), `passGravity` 300 (150–700), `aimError` 0.035 (0–0.12), `maxPass` 55 yd (30–80), `pressureMult` 1.6 (1–3) |\n2330\t| Catching | `catchBase` 0.66 (0.3–0.95), `catchRadius` 14 (6–24), `contestPenalty` 0.22 (0–0.5), `intBase` 0.10 (0–0.4), `deflectChance` 0.35 (0–0.8) |\n2331\t| Tackling | `tackleBase` 0.62 (0.3–0.9), `bigHitBonus` 0.12 (0–0.3), `bigHitLaunch` 180 (60–320), `fumbleBase` 0.03 (0–0.2), `stripChance` 0.12 (0–0.4), `stiffBonus` 0.35 (0–0.6), `spinWindow` 0.22 s (0.05–0.4), `gangBonus` 0.18 (0–0.4), `pileRadius` 5 yd (2–10) |\n2332\t| Blocking | `blockPush` 18 (5–40), `shedBase` 1.9 s (0.5–4) |\n2333\t| Kicking | `meterSpeed` 1.4 (0.6–3), `accBand` 0.12 (0.04–0.3), `kickGravity` 260 (120–600), `kickApex` punt 260 / kickoff 220 / FG 150 (40–500), `blockChance` 0.6 (0–1), `cpuFgRange` 45 yd (30–60) |\n2334\t| AI | `aiOpen` 3 yd (1–6), `cushion` 2 yd (0.5–5), `reactionMult` 1 (0.5–2), `aiThinkHz` 20 (5–60), `rubberBand` (by difficulty; a toggle) |\n2335\t| Rules | `yardsToGo` 20 (10–30), `quarterLength` 120 s (30–300), `runoff` 10 s (0–25), `playcallTime` 12 s (5–30), `autoHike` 8 s (3–20), `lateHitWindow` 1.2 s (0–3), `hotPlays` 6 (1–12), `fiascoMeterMult` 1 (0.25–3) |\n2336\t| Presentation | `camLead` 0.35 s (0–1), `camSmooth` 0.18 (0–0.6), `crowdDecay` 0.15 (0.02–0.5), `replayRate` 0.5 (0.2–1), `commentaryGap` 2.5 s (1–6), `safeMargin` 8 px (0–24) |\n2337\t\n2338\t### 22.2 Balance targets\n2339\tAt Pro difficulty, measured over CPU-vs-CPU games and the Play Lab, with 2:00 quarters:\n2340\t\n2341\t| Measure | Target |\n2342\t|---|---|\n2343\t| Points per team per game | 14–28 |\n2344\t| Completion rate | 55–70% |\n2345\t| Yards per carry | 4–6 |\n2346\t| Sacks per team per game | 1–3 |\n2347\t| Turnovers per game | 1–2.5 |\n2348\t| FG% from 40–49 yd | 60–75% |\n2349\t| Average live time per play | 5–8 s |\n2350\t| Hot Streaks per game | about 1 |\n2351\t| Fiasco Meter fills per team per game | 1–2 |\n2352\t\n2353\t`node test/balance.mjs` (not in the one command) runs 20 such games headless and prints these against the targets.\n2354\t\n2355\t---\n2356\t\n2357\t## 23. Definition of done and the hand-off\n2358\t- [ ] Every system and every piece of content in this plan works in the bundle, opened from `file://`. There are no\n2359\t  TODOs, placeholders, stub features, console errors, engine warnings or debug leftovers. The Dev mode is a feature,\n2360\t  behind the pause menu.\n2361\t- [ ] `npm test` and `npm test -- --browser` pass. The hub harness passes all 4 configurations on the final file. The\n2362\t  scripted playthrough reaches the credits.\n2363\t- [ ] `tools/check.mjs` has no errors and its look notes are addressed. The screenshots (§21.6) have been reviewed.\n2364\t- [ ] `src/about.json` is filled in for real. `build.mjs` writes it into the game (`window.FF_ABOUT`, the About and\n2365\t  Credits pages) and as `exit-interview.json` beside the deliverable, in exactly TASK.md's shape. Check that it parses\n2366\t  (`node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`). Write \"unknown\" for what you\n2367\t  can't confirm. Suggested values:\n2368\t  - `sourceInformation`:\n2369\t    - date: \"2026-11-03 17:48:31\"\n2370\t    - source: \"American football (over the top arcade style)\"\n2371\t    - plan: \"PLAN.md\"\n2372\t    - genre: \"Arcade sports (American football) with beat-'em-up hits and a story campaign\"\n2373\t    - perspective: \"Sideline broadcast camera (a custom 50° view), a Kick Cam behind the kicker, replay angles\"\n2374\t    - tech: \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff (modified, see the Engine Changes page), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, my-3D2dge\n2375\t      mocap runtime with a FIASCO clip set, Canvas 2D, Web Audio; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 for tests\". Confirm\n2376\t      the versions.\n2377\t    - artDirection: \"my-3D2dge native: HD Humanoid rigs drawn as pixel art, lit stadiums, weather, particles; new\n2378\t      football gear, field painting, 35 shapes, logos\"\n2379\t    - animation: \"my-3D2dge procedural rigs, E.MOVES and attack specs, joint post-processing (PoseFX), and 18\n2380\t      motion-capture clips (Quaternius, Mesh2Motion, CMU)\"\n2381\t    - audio: \"The engine's chip synth: original songs and sound effects, a crowd bed, and a formant babble synth for\n2382\t      Animalese and Simlish voices\"\n2383\t    - online: \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1–4 players; local 1–4 on one machine\"\n2384\t    - testing: what TASK.md allowed and what you used\n2385\t    - research: what you researched, or \"none\"\n2386\t    - environment: \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\", or yours\n2387\t    - model: your model and reasoning effort\n2388\t    - usage: the estimate, or \"unknown\"\n2389\t  - `testingFeedback` (4 answers), `engineFeedback` (6 answers), `promptFeedback` (4 answers): your real answers.\n2390\t  - `aiHub`:\n2391\t    - name: \"American Football Fiasco\"\n2392\t    - tagline: \"Over-the-top arcade football\"\n2393\t    - description: \"Lead the hopeless Tumbleweed Junction Fiascos through the Fiasco Cup: 7-on-7 arcade football with\n2394\t      turbo, Big Hits, Hot Streaks, trick plays and mascots, for 1–4 players.\"\n2395\t    - type: \"Game\"\n2396\t    - genre: \"Sports\"\n2397\t    - source: \"American football\"\n2398\t    - series: \"\"\n2399\t    - players: \"1–4\"\n2400\t    - controls: \"Stick/WASD run · ✕/Space hike, dive, tackle · ✕○□△ or 1–4/click throw · R2/Shift turbo\"\n2401\t    - tags: [\"arcade\", \"comedy\", \"versus\", \"co-op\", \"story\", \"retro\"]\n2402\t- [ ] **The final chat reply:** a short summary of the game, plus the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine\n2403\t  Feedback and Prompt Feedback, the same as the About screen.\n2404\t- [ ] **Clean up:** stop every server you started (by its PID). `.cache/` may be deleted. Leave the dev folder, the\n2405\t  deliverable and `exit-interview.json`.\n2406\t\n2407\t---\n2408\t\n2409\t## Appendix A. Data schemas\n2410\t```js\n2411\t// A.1 team\n2412\t{ id: 'fiascos', name: 'TUMBLEWEED JUNCTION FIASCOS', short: 'FIASCOS', abbr: 'TUM',\n2413\t  colors: { primary: '#e8742a', secondary: '#4a2a6a', trim: '#f4e8c8', helmet: '#e8742a', stripe: '#4a2a6a', pants: '#f4e8c8', cleats: '#1e1a22' },\n2414\t  logo: { rows: [/* 16 strings of 16 */], pal: { o: '#e8742a', y: '#ffd84a', b: '#6a4a2a' } }, stadium: 'tumbleweed', chant: ['FI', 'AS', 'CO'],\n2415\t  mod: { all: { '*': -1 } },                  // or { OL: { STR: 2 }, DL: { STR: 2 }, all: { SPD: -1 } }\n2416\t  ai: { run: .45, pass: .45, trick: .10, blitz: .25, lateHit: .10 },\n2417\t  coach: { name: 'GUS BLUSTER', rig: { build: 'bulky', size: 1.2, hat: 'cap', colors: { cloth: '#e8742a', skin: '#f0a080' } }, voice: 'bluster' },\n2418\t  mascot: { name: 'FUMBLES', head: 'tumbleweed' }, cheer: { count: 4 },\n2419\t  roster: [{ slot: 'QB', num: 7, name: 'HAP HAZARD', skin: 2, hair: { style: 'short', color: '#6a4a2a' }, delta: { ARM: 2, AWR: 1 }, special: null, bio: 'Rookie. Hauls pickle barrels.' }, /* ... 15 */] }\n2420\t\n2421\t// A.2 play (offense; defense uses rush / man / zone / spy)\n2422\t{ id: 'slants', name: 'SLANTS', side: 'off', tab: 'PASS', formation: 'shotgun', type: 'pass', tags: ['quick'],\n2423\t  qb: { drop: [-6, 0], reads: ['WR2', 'WR1', 'RB'], readT: .6 },\n2424\t  assign: { C: { block: 'pass', zone: 'mid' }, LG: { block: 'pass', zone: 'left' }, RG: { block: 'pass', zone: 'right' },\n2425\t            RB: { route: [[-2, 5], [1, 10]], after: 'settle' }, WR1: { route: [[2.5, -13], [9, -6]], after: 'settle' },\n2426\t            WR2: { route: [[2.5, 12], [9, 5]], after: 'settle' } } }\n2427\t// a run: QB: { handoff: 'RB', at: .45, then: { fake: [-5, 1] } }, RB: { carry: [[-2.5, .6], [2, .8], [8, .8]] }\n2428\t// a defense: { id: 'cover2', side: 'def', tab: 'BASE', formation: 'base', assign: { DE1: { rush: 'contain' }, NT: { rush: 'A' },\n2429\t//   DE2: { rush: 'contain' }, LB1: { zone: { at: [6, -7], r: 5 } }, LB2: { zone: { at: [6, 7], r: 5 } }, CB: { zone: { at: [16, -9], r: 10 } }, S: { zone: { at: [16, 9], r: 10 } } } }\n2430\t\n2431\t// A.3 stadium\n2432\t{ id: 'hogwallow', name: 'THE HOG WALLOW', home: 'mudhogs', music: 'SWAMP_STOMP',\n2433\t  light: { ambient: .55, tint: '#9aa4b0', towers: false, sun: null }, weather: { kind: 'rain', amount: .6, wind: .2, lightning: .1 },\n2434\t  surface: { stripes: ['#3e6a2e', '#4a7a36'], mud: { blotches: 9, seed: 4 }, ice: null, glowLines: false },\n2435\t  backdrop: { sky: ['#5a6470', '#7a848e', '#9aa2a8'], layers: [{ kind: 'forest', color: '#2a3a2a', y: .62, height: .25, parallax: .2 }, { kind: 'fog', color: '#8a9490', y: .8, height: .15, parallax: .1, drift: 6 }] },\n2436\t  stands: { tiers: 5, face: 'metal', roof: 'slab', density: .8, sections: { home: ['#4a6a2a', '#6a4a2a'], away: 'byEndzone' }, signs: ['HOGS!', 'MUD!', 'OINK'] },\n2437\t  props: [['airboat', -6, -4, { facing: 0 }], ['grill', 20, 58, {}] /* [shape or prop id, x yd from the left goal line, y yd from the far sideline, opts] */],\n2438\t  specials: ['lightning', 'puddleSplash'] }\n2439\t\n2440\t// A.4 card\n2441\t{ id: 'ROCKET_CLEATS', name: 'ROCKET CLEATS', side: 'off', art: 'cleats', text: 'Carrier and receivers +20% speed this play',\n2442\t  cpu: ctx => (ctx.down >= 3 && ctx.toGo >= 10) || (ctx.trailing && ctx.timeLeft < 120),\n2443\t  apply: ctx => ctx.mod('speed', a => a.team === ctx.team && (a.carrier || a.role === 'WR' || a.role === 'RB') ? 1.2 : 1, { plays: 1 }) }\n2444\t\n2445\t// A.5 scenario\n2446\t{ id: 'ch3', seed: 7, stadium: 'afterglow', weather: null, home: 'owls', away: 'fiascos', humans: { away: [0] }, difficulty: 'pro-',\n2447\t  quarterLength: 90, quarter: 3, clock: 90, score: { home: 21, away: 7 }, kicking: 'home', start: 'kickoff', // or { possession: 'away', los: 20, down: 1, toGo: 20 }\n2448\t  cards: { away: 'loadout', home: ['MEGA_HIT'] }, events: [{ when: { quarter: 3, play: 4 }, do: 'lightsOut', plays: 3 }],\n2449\t  win: { type: 'outscore' }, bonus: { type: 'margin', value: 7 }, cheats: {},\n2450\t  script: [/* attract and tests: { call: { off: 'deep_post', def: 'cover2', card: 'HOT_SAUCE' }, force: { catch: true, td: true } } */] }\n2451\t\n2452\t// A.6 intent (one per athlete per step)\n2453\t{ mx: 0, my: 0, turbo: false, press: 0 /* bits: b1 1, b2 2, b3 4, b4 8, lb 16, rb 32 */, held: 0, recv: -1 /* receiver 0..3 */, click: -1 /* athlete id */ }\n2454\t\n2455\t// A.7 drill\n2456\t{ id: 'moves', title: 'MOVES', scenario: { /* A.5 */ }, coach: 'Spin, stiff arm, hurdle! Like a ballerina with anger issues!',\n2457\t  steps: [{ text: 'Spin past the first tackler', chips: ['b3'], goal: 'evade:spin' }, { text: 'Stiff-arm the second', chips: ['b2'], goal: 'evade:stiff' },\n2458\t          { text: 'Hurdle the diver', chips: ['b4'], goal: 'evade:hurdle' }, { text: 'Dive into the end zone', chips: ['b1'], goal: 'td:dive' }],\n2459\t  bot: ctx => { /* intents that complete it */ } }\n2460\t\n2461\t// A.8 chapter\n2462\t{ id: 'ch3', n: 3, title: 'LIGHTS OUT', stadium: 'afterglow', opponent: 'owls', scenario: 'ch3', intro: 'ch3_intro', halftime: null,\n2463\t  win: 'ch3_win', loss: 'ch3_loss', rewards: ['ROCKET_CLEATS', 'GLUE_GLOVES'], bonus: { type: 'margin', value: 7, text: 'Win by 7 or more' } }\n2464\t```\n2465\t\n2466\t## Appendix B. Network messages (compact JSON: integers, keys of 1–2 letters)\n2467\t```js\n2468\t// client → host, unreliable, 15 Hz\n2469\t{ t: 'i', at: 41234 /* AIHub.time() ms */, q: 812 /* seq */, a: 3 /* athlete */, p: [10234, 6120] /* x, y × 10 */, v: [1450, -220],\n2470\t  f: 314 /* facing × 100 */, b: 5 /* held bits */, log: [[57, 1, 0], [58, 4, 2]] /* last 8 actions: [seq, code, arg] */ }\n2471\t// client → host, reliable\n2472\t{ t: 'call', ph: 23 /* the play-call id */, play: 'slants', flip: 0, card: null, rcv: 'WR1' }\n2473\t{ t: 'kick', ph: 24, power: 870, acc: -40, aim: 120 }   // ×1000\n2474\t// host → all, unreliable, 14 Hz, ≤ 1,100 bytes\n2475\t{ t: 's', at: 41250, n: 619, ph: 5 /* phase code */, c: 873 /* clock × 10 */, q: 2, sc: [14, 7], d: [3, 120, 10420] /* down, toGo × 10, los x × 10 */,\n2476\t  ball: [10234, 6120, 140, 1 /* state */, 3 /* holder */], A: [[0, 10234, 6120, 0, 314, 1, 128, 1], /* id, x, y, z (×10), facing, pose, u (0–255), flags */],\n2477\t  ack: { 1: 58 }, corr: [] }\n2478\t// host → all, reliable, ≤ 4/s\n2479\t{ t: 'e', k: 'phase', ph: 24, phase: 'PRESNAP', off: { play: 'slants', flip: 0, card: null }, def: { play: 'cover2', flip: 0, card: 'MEGA_HIT' }, ctl: { 0: 4, 1: 13 } }\n2480\t{ t: 'e', k: 'ctl', seat: 1, a: 12 }    { t: 'e', k: 'score', sc: [21, 7], by: 5, how: 'td' }\n2481\t{ t: 'e', k: 'card', team: 1, card: 'HOT_SAUCE' }    { t: 'e', k: 'over', sc: [21, 14], stats: { /* per seat */ } }\n2482\t```\n2483\tFlags: 1 carrying, 2 hot, 4 dinged, 8 helmet off, 16 locked, 32 CPU (seat left), 64 special ready. Test the JSON length\n2484\tof the biggest snapshot (every athlete plus the mascot on the field).\n2485\t\n2486\t## Appendix C. Pose codes\n2487\t0 IDLE, 1 RUN, 2 STANCE3, 3 STANCE2, 4 QB_UC, 5 QB_SG, 6 SNAP, 7 DROPBACK, 8 THROW, 9 HANDOFF_GIVE, 10 HANDOFF_TAKE,\n2488\t11 CARRY, 12 CATCH_READY, 13 CATCH, 14 JUMP, 15 DIVE, 16 TACKLE_DIVE, 17 SPIN, 18 STIFFARM, 19 HURDLE, 20 BLOCK,\n2489\t21 SHED, 22 BIGHIT, 23 TACKLED, 24 FLY, 25 DOWN, 26 GETUP, 27 PILE, 28 KICK, 29 HOLD, 30 CELEBRATE (u selects the\n2490\tdance), 31 CHEER, 32 DEJECTED, 33 REF_TD, 34 REF_FD, 35 REF_INC, 36 REF_SHRUG, 37 CHEERLEADER, 38 COACH_YELL, 39 KNEEL,\n2491\t40 STRIP, 41 LATERAL, 42 DIVE_CATCH, 43 SEISMIC, 44 MUDSLIDE. `poseU` is the action's progress 0–1 (0–255 on the\n2492\tnetwork).\n2493\t\n2494\t## Appendix D. Bus events and modifiers\n2495\tEvents, with their commentary priority:\n2496\t- 10: `td` (scorer, team, how, yards)\n2497\t- 9: `int` (defender), `fumble` (carrier, forcer), `megaHit`\n2498\t- 8: `bigHit`, `sack` (defender, qb), `special` (who, kind)\n2499\t- 7: `catch` (receiver, yards) when 20+ yd, `tackle` (tackler, carrier, bigHit, yards) when the play went 15+ yd,\n2500\t  `hotOn`, `mascotOn`, `fg` (good, yards, doink)\n2501\t- 6: `lateHit`, `cardUsed` (team, card)\n2502\t- 5: `drop` (receiver)\n2503\t- 4: `firstDown`\n2504\t- 3: `incomplete`\n2505\t- 2: weather\n2506\t- 1: idle chatter\n2507\t- No commentary priority: `snap`, `handoff`, `pass` (thrower, target, type), `deflect`, `brokenTackle`, `recover`\n2508\t  (athlete, team), `pile`, `pat` (good, type), `safety`, `touchback`, `turnoverOnDowns`, `punt`, `kickoff`, `return`\n2509\t  (yards), `outOfBounds`, `hotOff`, `fiascoFill`, `fiascoBreak` (team, card), `refDown`, `lightsOut`, `lightsOn`,\n2510\t  `quarterEnd`, `halftime`, `twoMinute`, `overtime`, `final` (winner, score), `phase` (from, to).\n2511\t\n2512\tModifiers, through `FF.bus.mod(name, value, ctx)` (listeners multiply or add): `tackle.p`, `catch.p`, `int.p`,\n2513\t`fumble.p`, `speed`, `accel`, `aim.err`, `shed.t`, `kick.acc`, `kick.power`, `turbo.drain`. Cards, Hot Streak,\n2514\tDinged, halftime choices, boss specials, difficulty and cheats are all modifiers, so they never edit the core code.\n2515\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49428dbe-779b-4248-8ac3-c582018d3c3d","uuid":"522e4c1d-871d-44f8-95a4-ae91015a8e2d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:06:36.324Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-070556__xb697dc/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n---\n\n## 20. Risks and how to de-risk them\n| # | Risk | Why it's risky | De-risk | Fallback |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | The football AI feels broken: stuck plays, clumps, no blocking | many interacting agents, the heart of the game | build it first (M2) in the Play Lab with overlays; keep behaviors small and data-driven; delay perception for realism; the Monte Carlo bands are tests; tune with sliders | simplify a behavior (zone-only coverage, timed sheds) before shipping a stuck play; never ship a play that can stall |\n| 2 | Shared-world netcode under latency and loss | real-time physics across devices | spike it at M3, before content; the arena example's prediction model; action logs that survive loss; a snapshot size budget; the Node loopback with a simulated network; the harness | if prediction can't be made stable by M3's end, ship host-authoritative rendering without prediction (it passes the harness; it feels laggier). Only if the shared world can't pass the harness at all: a parallel-mode \"TWO-MINUTE DRILL\" round (each player scores what they can against the CPU in 2:00). Decide at M3, write the decision in ENGINE-CHANGES.md's notes and on the About screen. |\n| 3 | Animation quality: retargeted clips on bulky rigs, PoseFX pops | new animation | a filmstrip of every clip on every build at M1 and M4; ease all weights; Dev deep links that loop a pose | replace any clip that looks wrong with the engine's procedural poses and E.MOVES |\n| 4 | Readability at 10 feet: small characters on a busy field | the TV distance | screenshots at 1080p and 720p from M1; text-size rules (§14.1); panels behind text; E1 and E9 | zoom the default camera in (`camera.start` 1.15) and simplify the field paint |\n| 5 | The babble voices sound harsh or annoying | synthesis | a voice test page (a Dev page: say any line with any profile) early in M6; soft envelopes, a bus lowpass, short syllables; the Voices slider; subtitles always on | turn the rate down and use Animalese blips only (letter blips through formants) |\n| 6 | Content volume: 6 teams, 5 stadiums, 5 chapters, 35 shapes, 13 songs, 400+ lines | time | content as data with validation; base ratings plus modifiers; content passes after the systems are done (M7); reuse sets (the locker room recolored) | cut variety, never features: fewer props per stadium, 6 lines per event instead of 8 |\n| 7 | Engine changes break the engine | a shared base | small isolated changes; after each, `node tools/check.mjs kits/sports.html` and `node kits/test.mjs sports` | revert the change and do it in game code |\n| 8 | The single-file bundle | `</script>`, the size, `session.js` integrity, `file://` | the build escapes and checks session.js's hash; check.mjs on the bundle from `file://`; no fetches at runtime | — |\n| 9 | Slow headless tests | 14 rigs at 120 Hz | fast mode (presentation off); short quarters through scenario overrides; cheats to finish chapters | split the playthrough into one suite per chapter |\n| 10 | Replays mutate or desync the sim | shared state | presentation-only playback from recorded frames; the hash test | — |\n| 11 | View switches stall (floor rebakes) | the Kick Cam and replays | measure the rebake in a test; if over 100 ms, pre-bake the Kick Cam views in a boot step | a dissolve hides it |\n| 12 | 10-foot scaling breaks the Shell's layout | CSS | `clamp()`; screenshots of pause, settings, controls and Dev at both sizes | lower the scale to 1.4 |\n| 13 | Touch-only false positives (touch laptops) | detection | require no fine pointer and no key or pad; any key or pad unlocks | — |\n| 14 | The hub card's ready timing | protocol | `ready()` only after the boot steps and the match build; the harness checks it | — |\n| 15 | The violence reads as mean | tone | slapstick only: stars, flying helmets, pancakes, no blood, no injuries beyond \"Dinged\"; the comfort settings respected | — |\n\n---\n\n## 21. Testing\n\n### 21.1 The one command\n`npm test` (that is, `node test/run.mjs`) prints **only failures** (`FAIL suite › test: detail`) and one final line:\n`N passed, M failed (12.3 s)`. The exit code is 1 on any failure.\n- `node test/run.mjs rules ai` runs only those suites. Rerun only the suites covering code you changed. Run the full\n  set at the end of each milestone.\n- `--browser` adds the Playwright suites. `--seed n` reseeds.\n- `test/lib/context.mjs` builds a vm context with stand-ins: `window`, `addEventListener` (records listeners),\n  `location { hash }`, `matchMedia` (configurable, for the touch-only tests), `navigator { getGamepads: () => [],\n  maxTouchPoints }`, `performance`, and a `console` whose warnings are collected (an engine warning fails the test\n  unless it is listed as expected).\n- It loads `vendor/` and `src/` in `index.html`'s order (parse the script tags, as `kits/test.mjs` does) and returns\n  `{ game, FF, E, I, step(s), tap(a), hold(a, on), feed(...), snap() }`.\n\n### 21.2 The suites\n| Suite | What it asserts |\n|---|---|\n| `boot` | boots headless; the boot steps run; every scene enters and exits with `game.go(..., { fade: 0 })`; deep links parse; no errors |\n| `data` | every team (15 unique numbers, ratings 1–10, hex colors, a valid logo), play (every slot assigned, coordinates in range, reads pointing at eligible slots, 3 linemen on the line), stadium (props exist, songs exist), card, chapter (nodes, cast and scenarios exist), drill, line (≤ 48 characters, known variables) and attract segment is valid |\n| `rules` | downs and distance, first downs, a turnover on downs, TDs (run and catch), PAT kick and 2-point, FG good, no good and doink, safety, touchback, out of bounds, the incomplete spot, INT and fumble possession, the clock (live, runoff, stops, the last-30 s rule), quarters, halftime ends switching, OT sudden death, the final. All through scenarios with forced outcomes |\n| `physics` | speeds by rating and turbo, turbo drain and regen, collision separation after 1 s of pushing, a pass with no aim error landing within 1 unit of its target, bounces, kick distances by power, FG geometry |\n| `actions` | every action's pose code and timing; a spin evades a frontal tackle in its window and not outside it; the stiff-arm bonus; a hurdle evades low dives; a Big Hit launches and its fumble roll is ×3 (seeded Monte Carlo within ±0.05); strip; the jump-catch window; laterals; the late-hit window; pile-up resolution; the 3-press meter |\n| `ai` | the Play Lab bands (§8.6) for every offense × defense pair (n = 30, seeded, fast mode); the coach's choice in 20 canonical situations (4th & 15 at your 30: punt; 4th & 1 at their 40, late and trailing: go; down 2 after a late TD: go for 2) |\n| `ots` | Hot Streak starts at 3 big plays and ends on its reset events; the Fiasco Meter fills and draws a card; each card's effect is measurable (ROCKET CLEATS gives +20% speed, and so on); boss specials fire under their conditions and keep to once per drive or half; Dinged; cosmetics (the flying helmet, divots, breath) don't change the sim hash |\n| `replay` | the sim hash is equal before and after a replay; the frame count; the highlight reel keeps the top 5 |\n| `control` | switching (auto, b2, a mouse click through `FF.control.pickAt`); the co-op assignment; control after turnovers; keyboard halves get b1–b4, turbo and lb; prompt labels per device and glyph setting (PlayStation by default gives `✕`, Xbox gives `A`, the keyboard gives Space or K, r1–r4 on a full keyboard) |\n| `ui` | every menu navigable by keyboard taps, pad taps, and the mouse (`input.feed('move' / 'down' / 'up', x, y)`: hover focuses, a click picks); the title's 10 s idle starts the attract mode and any input leaves it; touch-only mode shows the message and the Settings button; the settings specs hold the game's settings, and `glyphs` defaults to PlayStation with Xbox as the other option (`game.settings.spec('glyphs')`; headless the Shell keeps only screen names, so the Settings screen's look is checked by screenshot, §21.6); `game.menu('settings')` opens the screen named `settings` (`game.shell.screen`); the pause items (`menu.items()`) include Dev Mode outside sessions and not in them |\n| `audio` | every sfx and song named in data exists (no unknown-sound warnings during a full attract cycle); the voice planner's plans are deterministic for every profile; Commentary Off plans nothing; a hub `end` leaves the audio muted and the music stopped |\n| `dev` | every Dev action runs; each slider changes `FF.T` live (`game.settings.set('dev.speedBase', v)` changes the sim's top speed); Reset all restores the defaults; the Play Lab returns stats; the cheats work |\n| `attract` | the whole loop runs headless and each segment's key event fires (TD, fumble, pile-up, doink FG, INT, late hit, ref down, mascot sack, lights out, Snowplow, the story line, the halftime show, Seismic Sack, the trophy, the records); nothing is saved; any input leaves within one step |\n| `story` (**the scripted whole-game playthrough**) | title → menu → STORY → NEW GAME → the prologue (confirm taps) → the ch1 drills by their bots → chapters 2–5 with the human side on autopilot (the CPU brains drive its athletes through intents, the play calls are COACH SAYS) with `godMode` and `forceCatch` for that side and `quarterLength: 20` → halftime choices → outros → the ending → the credits → the menu. It checks the chapter flags, the rewards, stars ≥ 1, `game.saves.latest()` with chapter 5 done, Big Heads unlocked, the records, no errors, and no NaN positions (snapshots every 120 steps). Also a loss in one chapter (the CPU forced to win) → THAT'S A FIASCO → RETRY works. Also a 2-player local exhibition (`game.addPlayer({ keys: 'right' })`) to the results and REMATCH. |\n| `net` | 2–4 vm contexts with a fake `AIHub` (`test/lib/fakehub.mjs`: `active`, `connect` → info, `ready`, `answer`, `on`, `send(data, { to, reliable })`, `time`, `finish`, `rng(label)`, `server`) over a bus with 150 ± 50 ms latency, 5% loss for unreliable messages, reliable ordering, the 20/s burst-40 limiter, 16 KB maximum, and the card → start → time-up → end flow. Cases: 2 players; 4 players with latency and loss; the host leaving; a server host; a player leaving mid-match (his athletes go CPU); time-up (finish within grace). It checks traffic both ways, ≤ 18 msgs/s per copy, snapshots ≤ 1,100 bytes, the predicted athlete within 2 yd of the host's 95% of the time when not locked, that play calls and kicks arrive, `finish` called once with valid standings (every player once) and scores, every copy ended, nothing sent after `end`, and no errors |\n| `browser` (with `--browser`) | (1) `node tools/check.mjs <deliverable> --size 1920x1080` and `--size 1280x720`: exit 0, no errors, look notes saved. (2) The deep links `#match`, `#drill/passing`, `#attract`, `#story/ch5` play 4 s without errors. (3) The hub harness: copy `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` and the deliverable into `test/hub/serve/`. Start `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` there (read the port from its output, keep its PID), and confirm that `GET /<deliverable>` contains `AMERICAN FOOTBALL FIASCO`. Open `harness.html?game=<deliverable>&players=2&auto=1`, then `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, the same with `&scenario=host-leave`, and `&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1` (add `&limit=90` to keep rounds short). Wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`. Assert `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`, printing the failed checks otherwise. Stop the server by its PID. |\n\n### 21.3 Devices in tests\n- Keyboard and pad go through `input.tap` / `input.hold`. Set `input.lastDevice` to check prompts.\n- The mouse goes through `input.feed('move' | 'down' | 'up', x, y, { button })`.\n- Headless there is no last frame for `r.pick`, so the game has its own `FF.control.pickAt(sx, sy)`: it projects\n  athletes through the current view and hit-tests their bounds. Use it in both the browser and tests, with `r.pick`\n  as a cross-check in the browser.\n\n### 21.4 Determinism\nTests seed `FF.rng` through the scenario's `seed` and never read the wall clock. The kits' `proof()` pattern\n(`kits/sports.js`) shows that the same seed gives the same match hash twice. Keep a `FF.sim.hash()`.\n\n### 21.5 Filmstrips (animation review; not in the one command)\n`node tools/filmstrip.mjs <page>#drill/moves --steps \"wait:800 rec:16:2 ...\" --seed 1` for the spin, stiff arm,\nhurdle and dive, and a Dev deep link `#dev/pose/<CODE>` that loops one pose code on every build, to review each\n§12.3 row.\n\n### 21.6 Screenshots (only for what a script can't judge)\n`npm run shots` (`test/browser/shots.mjs`) saves to `shots/`, at 1920×1080 and 1280×720:\n- the title, the main menu, the exhibition setup, team select;\n- the play call (offense, defense, split);\n- live play at each of the 5 stadiums, a Big Hit, a TD celebration, a replay, the Kick Cam, a pile-up, a Blazing\n  player, LIGHTS OUT;\n- each cutscene set, the results, Hall of Fiasco, the About pages;\n- the pause menu, Settings (with Button symbols), the Dev screens;\n- the touch-only title (`--size 390x844@3`), the hub card.\nReview them against §12.1, and fix what reads badly.\n\n---\n\n## 22. Tuning defaults (the Dev sliders; `02-tuning.js`)\n| Group | Key: default (min–max) |\n|---|---|\n| Movement | `speedBase` 92 (60–140), `speedPerSpd` 7 (3–12), `accelBase` 520 (200–1200), `turboMult` 1.25 (1–1.6), `turboDrain` 0.45 (0.1–1.5), `turboRegen` 0.22 (0.05–1), `turboDeadRefill` 0.35 (0–1), `carrySpeedMult` 0.96 (0.8–1), `backpedalMult` 0.65 (0.4–1) |\n| Passing | `lobSpeed` 240 (150–350), `bulletSpeed` 400 (250–550), `passGravity` 300 (150–700), `aimError` 0.035 (0–0.12), `maxPass` 55 yd (30–80), `pressureMult` 1.6 (1–3) |\n| Catching | `catchBase` 0.66 (0.3–0.95), `catchRadius` 14 (6–24), `contestPenalty` 0.22 (0–0.5), `intBase` 0.10 (0–0.4), `deflectChance` 0.35 (0–0.8) |\n| Tackling | `tackleBase` 0.62 (0.3–0.9), `bigHitBonus` 0.12 (0–0.3), `bigHitLaunch` 180 (60–320), `fumbleBase` 0.03 (0–0.2), `stripChance` 0.12 (0–0.4), `stiffBonus` 0.35 (0–0.6), `spinWindow` 0.22 s (0.05–0.4), `gangBonus` 0.18 (0–0.4), `pileRadius` 5 yd (2–10) |\n| Blocking | `blockPush` 18 (5–40), `shedBase` 1.9 s (0.5–4) |\n| Kicking | `meterSpeed` 1.4 (0.6–3), `accBand` 0.12 (0.04–0.3), `kickGravity` 260 (120–600), `kickApex` punt 260 / kickoff 220 / FG 150 (40–500), `blockChance` 0.6 (0–1), `cpuFgRange` 45 yd (30–60) |\n| AI | `aiOpen` 3 yd (1–6), `cushion` 2 yd (0.5–5), `reactionMult` 1 (0.5–2), `aiThinkHz` 20 (5–60), `rubberBand` (by difficulty; a toggle) |\n| Rules | `yardsToGo` 20 (10–30), `quarterLength` 120 s (30–300), `runoff` 10 s (0–25), `playcallTime` 12 s (5–30), `autoHike` 8 s (3–20), `lateHitWindow` 1.2 s (0–3), `hotPlays` 6 (1–12), `fiascoMeterMult` 1 (0.25–3) |\n| Presentation | `camLead` 0.35 s (0–1), `camSmooth` 0.18 (0–0.6), `crowdDecay` 0.15 (0.02–0.5), `replayRate` 0.5 (0.2–1), `commentaryGap` 2.5 s (1–6), `safeMargin` 8 px (0–24) |\n\n### 22.2 Balance targets\nAt Pro difficulty, measured over CPU-vs-CPU games and the Play Lab, with 2:00 quarters:\n\n| Measure | Target |\n|---|---|\n| Points per team per game | 14–28 |\n| Completion rate | 55–70% |\n| Yards per carry | 4–6 |\n| Sacks per team per game | 1–3 |\n| Turnovers per game | 1–2.5 |\n| FG% from 40–49 yd | 60–75% |\n| Average live time per play | 5–8 s |\n| Hot Streaks per game | about 1 |\n| Fiasco Meter fills per team per game | 1–2 |\n\n`node test/balance.mjs` (not in the one command) runs 20 such games headless and prints these against the targets.\n\n---\n\n## 23. Definition of done and the hand-off\n- [ ] Every system and every piece of content in this plan works in the bundle, opened from `file://`. There are no\n  TODOs, placeholders, stub features, console errors, engine warnings or debug leftovers. The Dev mode is a feature,\n  behind the pause menu.\n- [ ] `npm test` and `npm test -- --browser` pass. The hub harness passes all 4 configurations on the final file. The\n  scripted playthrough reaches the credits.\n- [ ] `tools/check.mjs` has no errors and its look notes are addressed. The screenshots (§21.6) have been reviewed.\n- [ ] `src/about.json` is filled in for real. `build.mjs` writes it into the game (`window.FF_ABOUT`, the About and\n  Credits pages) and as `exit-interview.json` beside the deliverable, in exactly TASK.md's shape. Check that it parses\n  (`node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`). Write \"unknown\" for what you\n  can't confirm. Suggested values:\n  - `sourceInformation`:\n    - date: \"2026-11-03 17:48:31\"\n    - source: \"American football (over the top arcade style)\"\n    - plan: \"PLAN.md\"\n    - genre: \"Arcade sports (American football) with beat-'em-up hits and a story campaign\"\n    - perspective: \"Sideline broadcast camera (a custom 50° view), a Kick Cam behind the kicker, replay angles\"\n    - tech: \"my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff (modified, see the Engine Changes page), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, my-3D2dge\n      mocap runtime with a FIASCO clip set, Canvas 2D, Web Audio; Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 for tests\". Confirm\n      the versions.\n    - artDirection: \"my-3D2dge native: HD Humanoid rigs drawn as pixel art, lit stadiums, weather, particles; new\n      football gear, field painting, 35 shapes, logos\"\n    - animation: \"my-3D2dge procedural rigs, E.MOVES and attack specs, joint post-processing (PoseFX), and 18\n      motion-capture clips (Quaternius, Mesh2Motion, CMU)\"\n    - audio: \"The engine's chip synth: original songs and sound effects, a crowd bed, and a formant babble synth for\n      Animalese and Simlish voices\"\n    - online: \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1–4 players; local 1–4 on one machine\"\n    - testing: what TASK.md allowed and what you used\n    - research: what you researched, or \"none\"\n    - environment: \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\", or yours\n    - model: your model and reasoning effort\n    - usage: the estimate, or \"unknown\"\n  - `testingFeedback` (4 answers), `engineFeedback` (6 answers), `promptFeedback` (4 answers): your real answers.\n  - `aiHub`:\n    - name: \"American Football Fiasco\"\n    - tagline: \"Over-the-top arcade football\"\n    - description: \"Lead the hopeless Tumbleweed Junction Fiascos through the Fiasco Cup: 7-on-7 arcade football with\n      turbo, Big Hits, Hot Streaks, trick plays and mascots, for 1–4 players.\"\n    - type: \"Game\"\n    - genre: \"Sports\"\n    - source: \"American football\"\n    - series: \"\"\n    - players: \"1–4\"\n    - controls: \"Stick/WASD run · ✕/Space hike, dive, tackle · ✕○□△ or 1–4/click throw · R2/Shift turbo\"\n    - tags: [\"arcade\", \"comedy\", \"versus\", \"co-op\", \"story\", \"retro\"]\n- [ ] **The final chat reply:** a short summary of the game, plus the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine\n  Feedback and Prompt Feedback, the same as the About screen.\n- [ ] **Clean up:** stop every server you started (by its PID). `.cache/` may be deleted. Leave the dev folder, the\n  deliverable and `exit-interview.json`.\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A. Data schemas\n```js\n// A.1 team\n{ id: 'fiascos', name: 'TUMBLEWEED JUNCTION FIASCOS', short: 'FIASCOS', abbr: 'TUM',\n  colors: { primary: '#e8742a', secondary: '#4a2a6a', trim: '#f4e8c8', helmet: '#e8742a', stripe: '#4a2a6a', pants: '#f4e8c8', cleats: '#1e1a22' },\n  logo: { rows: [/* 16 strings of 16 */], pal: { o: '#e8742a', y: '#ffd84a', b: '#6a4a2a' } }, stadium: 'tumbleweed', chant: ['FI', 'AS', 'CO'],\n  mod: { all: { '*': -1 } },                  // or { OL: { STR: 2 }, DL: { STR: 2 }, all: { SPD: -1 } }\n  ai: { run: .45, pass: .45, trick: .10, blitz: .25, lateHit: .10 },\n  coach: { name: 'GUS BLUSTER', rig: { build: 'bulky', size: 1.2, hat: 'cap', colors: { cloth: '#e8742a', skin: '#f0a080' } }, voice: 'bluster' },\n  mascot: { name: 'FUMBLES', head: 'tumbleweed' }, cheer: { count: 4 },\n  roster: [{ slot: 'QB', num: 7, name: 'HAP HAZARD', skin: 2, hair: { style: 'short', color: '#6a4a2a' }, delta: { ARM: 2, AWR: 1 }, special: null, bio: 'Rookie. Hauls pickle barrels.' }, /* ... 15 */] }\n\n// A.2 play (offense; defense uses rush / man / zone / spy)\n{ id: 'slants', name: 'SLANTS', side: 'off', tab: 'PASS', formation: 'shotgun', type: 'pass', tags: ['quick'],\n  qb: { drop: [-6, 0], reads: ['WR2', 'WR1', 'RB'], readT: .6 },\n  assign: { C: { block: 'pass', zone: 'mid' }, LG: { block: 'pass', zone: 'left' }, RG: { block: 'pass', zone: 'right' },\n            RB: { route: [[-2, 5], [1, 10]], after: 'settle' }, WR1: { route: [[2.5, -13], [9, -6]], after: 'settle' },\n            WR2: { route: [[2.5, 12], [9, 5]], after: 'settle' } } }\n// a run: QB: { handoff: 'RB', at: .45, then: { fake: [-5, 1] } }, RB: { carry: [[-2.5, .6], [2, .8], [8, .8]] }\n// a defense: { id: 'cover2', side: 'def', tab: 'BASE', formation: 'base', assign: { DE1: { rush: 'contain' }, NT: { rush: 'A' },\n//   DE2: { rush: 'contain' }, LB1: { zone: { at: [6, -7], r: 5 } }, LB2: { zone: { at: [6, 7], r: 5 } }, CB: { zone: { at: [16, -9], r: 10 } }, S: { zone: { at: [16, 9], r: 10 } } } }\n\n// A.3 stadium\n{ id: 'hogwallow', name: 'THE HOG WALLOW', home: 'mudhogs', music: 'SWAMP_STOMP',\n  light: { ambient: .55, tint: '#9aa4b0', towers: false, sun: null }, weather: { kind: 'rain', amount: .6, wind: .2, lightning: .1 },\n  surface: { stripes: ['#3e6a2e', '#4a7a36'], mud: { blotches: 9, seed: 4 }, ice: null, glowLines: false },\n  backdrop: { sky: ['#5a6470', '#7a848e', '#9aa2a8'], layers: [{ kind: 'forest', color: '#2a3a2a', y: .62, height: .25, parallax: .2 }, { kind: 'fog', color: '#8a9490', y: .8, height: .15, parallax: .1, drift: 6 }] },\n  stands: { tiers: 5, face: 'metal', roof: 'slab', density: .8, sections: { home: ['#4a6a2a', '#6a4a2a'], away: 'byEndzone' }, signs: ['HOGS!', 'MUD!', 'OINK'] },\n  props: [['airboat', -6, -4, { facing: 0 }], ['grill', 20, 58, {}] /* [shape or prop id, x yd from the left goal line, y yd from the far sideline, opts] */],\n  specials: ['lightning', 'puddleSplash'] }\n\n// A.4 card\n{ id: 'ROCKET_CLEATS', name: 'ROCKET CLEATS', side: 'off', art: 'cleats', text: 'Carrier and receivers +20% speed this play',\n  cpu: ctx => (ctx.down >= 3 && ctx.toGo >= 10) || (ctx.trailing && ctx.timeLeft < 120),\n  apply: ctx => ctx.mod('speed', a => a.team === ctx.team && (a.carrier || a.role === 'WR' || a.role === 'RB') ? 1.2 : 1, { plays: 1 }) }\n\n// A.5 scenario\n{ id: 'ch3', seed: 7, stadium: 'afterglow', weather: null, home: 'owls', away: 'fiascos', humans: { away: [0] }, difficulty: 'pro-',\n  quarterLength: 90, quarter: 3, clock: 90, score: { home: 21, away: 7 }, kicking: 'home', start: 'kickoff', // or { possession: 'away', los: 20, down: 1, toGo: 20 }\n  cards: { away: 'loadout', home: ['MEGA_HIT'] }, events: [{ when: { quarter: 3, play: 4 }, do: 'lightsOut', plays: 3 }],\n  win: { type: 'outscore' }, bonus: { type: 'margin', value: 7 }, cheats: {},\n  script: [/* attract and tests: { call: { off: 'deep_post', def: 'cover2', card: 'HOT_SAUCE' }, force: { catch: true, td: true } } */] }\n\n// A.6 intent (one per athlete per step)\n{ mx: 0, my: 0, turbo: false, press: 0 /* bits: b1 1, b2 2, b3 4, b4 8, lb 16, rb 32 */, held: 0, recv: -1 /* receiver 0..3 */, click: -1 /* athlete id */ }\n\n// A.7 drill\n{ id: 'moves', title: 'MOVES', scenario: { /* A.5 */ }, coach: 'Spin, stiff arm, hurdle! Like a ballerina with anger issues!',\n  steps: [{ text: 'Spin past the first tackler', chips: ['b3'], goal: 'evade:spin' }, { text: 'Stiff-arm the second', chips: ['b2'], goal: 'evade:stiff' },\n          { text: 'Hurdle the diver', chips: ['b4'], goal: 'evade:hurdle' }, { text: 'Dive into the end zone', chips: ['b1'], goal: 'td:dive' }],\n  bot: ctx => { /* intents that complete it */ } }\n\n// A.8 chapter\n{ id: 'ch3', n: 3, title: 'LIGHTS OUT', stadium: 'afterglow', opponent: 'owls', scenario: 'ch3', intro: 'ch3_intro', halftime: null,\n  win: 'ch3_win', loss: 'ch3_loss', rewards: ['ROCKET_CLEATS', 'GLUE_GLOVES'], bonus: { type: 'margin', value: 7, text: 'Win by 7 or more' } }\n```\n\n## Appendix B. Network messages (compact JSON: integers, keys of 1–2 letters)\n```js\n// client → host, unreliable, 15 Hz\n{ t: 'i', at: 41234 /* AIHub.time() ms */, q: 812 /* seq */, a: 3 /* athlete */, p: [10234, 6120] /* x, y × 10 */, v: [1450, -220],\n  f: 314 /* facing × 100 */, b: 5 /* held bits */, log: [[57, 1, 0], [58, 4, 2]] /* last 8 actions: [seq, code, arg] */ }\n// client → host, reliable\n{ t: 'call', ph: 23 /* the play-call id */, play: 'slants', flip: 0, card: null, rcv: 'WR1' }\n{ t: 'kick', ph: 24, power: 870, acc: -40, aim: 120 }   // ×1000\n// host → all, unreliable, 14 Hz, ≤ 1,100 bytes\n{ t: 's', at: 41250, n: 619, ph: 5 /* phase code */, c: 873 /* clock × 10 */, q: 2, sc: [14, 7], d: [3, 120, 10420] /* down, toGo × 10, los x × 10 */,\n  ball: [10234, 6120, 140, 1 /* state */, 3 /* holder */], A: [[0, 10234, 6120, 0, 314, 1, 128, 1], /* id, x, y, z (×10), facing, pose, u (0–255), flags */],\n  ack: { 1: 58 }, corr: [] }\n// host → all, reliable, ≤ 4/s\n{ t: 'e', k: 'phase', ph: 24, phase: 'PRESNAP', off: { play: 'slants', flip: 0, card: null }, def: { play: 'cover2', flip: 0, card: 'MEGA_HIT' }, ctl: { 0: 4, 1: 13 } }\n{ t: 'e', k: 'ctl', seat: 1, a: 12 }    { t: 'e', k: 'score', sc: [21, 7], by: 5, how: 'td' }\n{ t: 'e', k: 'card', team: 1, card: 'HOT_SAUCE' }    { t: 'e', k: 'over', sc: [21, 14], stats: { /* per seat */ } }\n```\nFlags: 1 carrying, 2 hot, 4 dinged, 8 helmet off, 16 locked, 32 CPU (seat left), 64 special ready. Test the JSON length\nof the biggest snapshot (every athlete plus the mascot on the field).\n\n## Appendix C. Pose codes\n0 IDLE, 1 RUN, 2 STANCE3, 3 STANCE2, 4 QB_UC, 5 QB_SG, 6 SNAP, 7 DROPBACK, 8 THROW, 9 HANDOFF_GIVE, 10 HANDOFF_TAKE,\n11 CARRY, 12 CATCH_READY, 13 CATCH, 14 JUMP, 15 DIVE, 16 TACKLE_DIVE, 17 SPIN, 18 STIFFARM, 19 HURDLE, 20 BLOCK,\n21 SHED, 22 BIGHIT, 23 TACKLED, 24 FLY, 25 DOWN, 26 GETUP, 27 PILE, 28 KICK, 29 HOLD, 30 CELEBRATE (u selects the\ndance), 31 CHEER, 32 DEJECTED, 33 REF_TD, 34 REF_FD, 35 REF_INC, 36 REF_SHRUG, 37 CHEERLEADER, 38 COACH_YELL, 39 KNEEL,\n40 STRIP, 41 LATERAL, 42 DIVE_CATCH, 43 SEISMIC, 44 MUDSLIDE. `poseU` is the action's progress 0–1 (0–255 on the\nnetwork).\n\n## Appendix D. Bus events and modifiers\nEvents, with their commentary priority:\n- 10: `td` (scorer, team, how, yards)\n- 9: `int` (defender), `fumble` (carrier, forcer), `megaHit`\n- 8: `bigHit`, `sack` (defender, qb), `special` (who, kind)\n- 7: `catch` (receiver, yards) when 20+ yd, `tackle` (tackler, carrier, bigHit, yards) when the play went 15+ yd,\n  `hotOn`, `mascotOn`, `fg` (good, yards, doink)\n- 6: `lateHit`, `cardUsed` (team, card)\n- 5: `drop` (receiver)\n- 4: `firstDown`\n- 3: `incomplete`\n- 2: weather\n- 1: idle chatter\n- No commentary priority: `snap`, `handoff`, `pass` (thrower, target, type), `deflect`, `brokenTackle`, `recover`\n  (athlete, team), `pile`, `pat` (good, type), `safety`, `touchback`, `turnoverOnDowns`, `punt`, `kickoff`, `return`\n  (yards), `outOfBounds`, `hotOff`, `fiascoFill`, `fiascoBreak` (team, card), `refDown`, `lightsOut`, `lightsOn`,\n  `quarterEnd`, `halftime`, `twoMinute`, `overtime`, `final` (winner, score), `phase` (from, to).\n\nModifiers, through `FF.bus.mod(name, value, ctx)` (listeners multiply or add): `tackle.p`, `catch.p`, `int.p`,\n`fumble.p`, `speed`, `accel`, `aim.err`, `shed.t`, `kick.acc`, `kick.power`, `turbo.drain`. Cards, Hot Streak,\nDinged, halftime choices, boss specials, difficulty and cheats are all modifiers, so they never edit the core code.\n","numLines":279,"startLine":2237,"totalLines":2515}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HZAC3zJYimUHjEm4Nu6TBg","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
