{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QZ2b4LFMDM7yN8Hqo2ZqzW","type":"tool_result","content":"183:- `E.store`: saved data that survives reloads (localStorage, JSON). Never throws.\n184:- `E.store.get(key, fallback = null)`: the value saved under key (any JSON), or fallback\n185:- `E.store.remove(key)`: forget key\n186:- `E.store.set(key, value)`: save value (any JSON) under key; false when storage is blocked\n223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n244:- `E.charView(view)`: the view a rig in `view` is drawn from (the sprite-like angle above; the view itself outside pitch 40-89)\n275:- `E.Input.halfKeys(preset, side)` †: a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SHMUP, 'right') -> fire on . and Numpad 1, bomb on /)\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })\n430:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (x-ray silhouettes show through it: by default when it stands at least E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22, high), footprint, light (add its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true), charView (default true: steep views draw it from the characters' lower angle), flash, alpha, xray, pick (r.pick finds it) }\n468:- `game.addPlayer(o = {})` †: a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the left). Returns its input (null when four play already)\n471:- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's)\n473:- `game.cornerArea()` †: where the corner's buttons (menu and full screen, top right; the touch START) cover the screen, in screen pixels { x0, y0, x1, y1 } (r.W and r.H's space), or null while none show: keep a HUD clear of it\n483:- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage, color, sound: 'hit', rumble: true })\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (menu: false, or the agent edition) it pauses a scene in play. Returns true when a menu opened\n490:- `game.players` †: the players: [game.input (player 1), ...the ones who joined (game.allowJoin, game.addPlayer: section 10j)]; each an input with player (1..4), name ('P1'), color (E.PLAYER_COLORS) and device. A game of one: [game.input]\n544:- `game.settings`: the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved and applied (section 10b)\n559:- `E.PLAYER_COLORS: #4a8aff, #ff4a4a, #4ad860, #ffd040` †: the players' colors: player 1 blue, 2 red, 3 green, 4 yellow (game.players)\n568:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n569:- `settings.spec(key)`: the spec a setting was defined with (its label, type, range, options), or undefined\n618:- `saves.any` †: is there any save to load (a title's Continue)?\n619:- `saves.autosave(o)` †: save to the autosave (what write() gives)\n620:- `saves.copy(from, to)` †: copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty\n621:- `saves.erase(slot)` †: erase a slot\n622:- `saves.get(slot)` †: a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer: true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, place, level, time, at (the date saved), version }\n623:- `saves.latest()` †: the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it)\n624:- `saves.list()` †: every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows)\n625:- `saves.load(slot)` †: load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot is empty, damaged or from a newer version\n626:- `saves.save(slot, o)` †: save to a slot (0.., or 'auto'): o ({ data, place, level }) or what write() gives. Returns true when it is kept (in storage, or for the visit when storage is blocked: blocked tells), false when there was nothing to save\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n628:- `saves.blocked = false` †: storage refused a save (they last for the visit)\n629:- `saves.canSave = true` †: the pause menu offers Save (a JRPG turns it off away from save points)\n630:- `saves.game` †: its game\n631:- `saves.migrate` †: an older version's data brought up to this one (or null: kept as it is)\n632:- `saves.played = 0` †: seconds played in the game's scenes (paused time and titles left out), saved with each save and set by a load\n633:- `saves.read` †: what a load does with { data, place, level, time, slot }\n634:- `saves.slots` †: how many slots besides the autosave (3)\n635:- `saves.version` †: the game's version of its data (1), saved with each save\n636:- `saves.write` †: what a save holds ({ data, place, level })\n1081:- `new E.Backdrop(o = {}) → backdrop`: new E.Backdrop('castle-night') (a preset: E.Backdrop.presets) or new E.Backdrop({ sky: [colors top to bottom], sun, moon, stars, layers: [{ kind: 'mountains' | 'hills' | 'forest' | 'city' | 'castle' | 'clouds' | 'sea' | 'fog' | 'stalactites', color, y, height, parallax, seed }] }): a parallax sky and scenery drawn behind a level. sun, moon: { x, y (0..1 of the screen), r, color }\n1102:- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or a View, as given (r.shape draws steep views from the characters' angle: E.charView(view) gives that); a bag icon is the item's shape seen at an angle. r.sprite stands it on its feet (foot: [x, y] in the sprite) unless an anchor is given\n1163:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n1164:- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font, titleFont)\n1165:- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n1167:- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n1168:- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\n1181:- `shell.show(name, spec = {})` †: open a screen: 'title' | 'pause' | 'settings' | 'help' | 'results' | 'map' or a name of your own, from spec over o.screens[name]. A spec: { kicker, title, text (strings or functions), actions: [[label, fn] or { label, fn, act, primary, disabled }], back (fn for cancel) }. From another screen it stacks (back() returns); shown again, it updates (the new spec over the old). 'settings' takes its items\n1182:- `shell.show('title')` †: { name, subtitle, meta: [...], footer }\n1183:- `shell.show('help')` †: { keys: [[key, what]], sections: [[heading, text]] }\n1184:- `shell.show('results')` †: { emblem, stats: [[value, label]], medals: [[label, earned]] }\n1185:- `shell.show('map')` †: { map, at, markers (a list or a function), labels: [[text, x, y]], onPick(x, y) }\n// A headless test of the template game: the engine and game.js run in Node with no screen (new E.Game is headless where\n// there is no DOM), driven by fixed steps (game.advance) and scripted input (input.tap, input.hold), and read through\n// game.debug.snapshot(). Run it: node game/test.mjs (exit code 1 on a failure). Write one like it for your game.\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n\nconst ctx = { console };\nvm.createContext(ctx);\nfor (const f of ['../my-3d2dge.js', './game.js']) vm.runInContext(readFileSync(new URL(f, import.meta.url), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: f });\nconst E = ctx.My3D2dge, game = E.current, I = game.input, snap = () => game.debug.snapshot();\nlet failed = 0;\nconst check = (what, ok, detail = '') => { console.log((ok ? 'ok   ' : 'FAIL ') + what + (ok ? '' : ': ' + detail)); if (!ok) failed++; };\n\ngame.advance(.5);\ncheck('the title waits for start', snap().scene === 'title', JSON.stringify(snap()));\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\ncheck('start begins play', snap().scene === 'play', JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// climb: stand facing the roof's west wall (cells 7-9 of rows 4-6: x 112-160, y 64-112), press jump to take hold, then\n// climb with up (up the screen is up the wall) until it pulls up onto the top\ngame.debug.teleport(100, 88, 0, 0);\nI.tap('jump'); game.advance(.1);\ncheck('jump next to a wall takes hold of it', snap().climbing, JSON.stringify(snap()));\nI.hold('up'); game.advance(.6); I.hold('up', false); game.advance(1);\ncheck('climbing up pulls up onto the roof', !snap().climbing && snap().hero[2] === 32, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// take the gem (on the roof's middle cell), then hop down into the street with it\ngame.debug.teleport(136, 88, 32, 0); game.advance(.1);\ncheck('walking onto the gem takes it', snap().got, JSON.stringify(snap()));\ngame.debug.teleport(156, 120, 32, Math.PI / 2); I.hold('down'); game.advance(1.5); I.hold('down', false); game.advance(.5);\ncheck('back in the street with the gem wins', snap().scene === 'end' && snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// get seen: stand in front of the guard, in the open, until its alert fills\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\nconst [gx, gy, gf] = snap().guard;\ngame.debug.teleport(gx + Math.cos(gf) * 40, gy + Math.sin(gf) * 40, 0, gf + Math.PI);\ngame.advance(2.5);\ncheck('the guard catches a hero it sees', snap().scene === 'end' && !snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\ncheck('no errors', !game.errors.length, game.errors.map(e => e.message).join(' | '));\n\nconsole.log(failed ? `${failed} check(s) failed` : 'all checks passed');\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49428dbe-779b-4248-8ac3-c582018d3c3d","uuid":"7c26acc9-5ede-4f5b-94c2-a1c0cb803677","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:07:43.286Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"183:- `E.store`: saved data that survives reloads (localStorage, JSON). Never throws.\n184:- `E.store.get(key, fallback = null)`: the value saved under key (any JSON), or fallback\n185:- `E.store.remove(key)`: forget key\n186:- `E.store.set(key, value)`: save value (any JSON) under key; false when storage is blocked\n223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\n244:- `E.charView(view)`: the view a rig in `view` is drawn from (the sprite-like angle above; the view itself outside pitch 40-89)\n275:- `E.Input.halfKeys(preset, side)` †: a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SHMUP, 'right') -> fire on . and Numpad 1, bomb on /)\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })\n430:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x before facing), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (x-ray silhouettes show through it: by default when it stands at least E.HEIGHTS.chest, 22, high), footprint, light (add its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true), charView (default true: steep views draw it from the characters' lower angle), flash, alpha, xray, pick (r.pick finds it) }\n468:- `game.addPlayer(o = {})` †: a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the left). Returns its input (null when four play already)\n471:- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's)\n473:- `game.cornerArea()` †: where the corner's buttons (menu and full screen, top right; the touch START) cover the screen, in screen pixels { x0, y0, x1, y1 } (r.W and r.H's space), or null while none show: keep a HUD clear of it\n483:- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage, color, sound: 'hit', rumble: true })\n484:- `game.menu(name)`: open the menu (the corner's menu button and the touch START do it): a pausable scene (or a game started without scenes) pauses on its pause screen; any other scene, a title, waits under the settings. menu('settings') or menu('controls') opens that screen. Without a menu (menu: false, or the agent edition) it pauses a scene in play. Returns true when a menu opened\n490:- `game.players` †: the players: [game.input (player 1), ...the ones who joined (game.allowJoin, game.addPlayer: section 10j)]; each an input with player (1..4), name ('P1'), color (E.PLAYER_COLORS) and device. A game of one: [game.input]\n544:- `game.settings`: the player's choices (game.settings.volume, game.settings.set('volume', .5), your own from menu.settings), saved and applied (section 10b)\n559:- `E.PLAYER_COLORS: #4a8aff, #ff4a4a, #4ad860, #ffd040` †: the players' colors: player 1 blue, 2 red, 3 green, 4 yellow (game.players)\n568:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n569:- `settings.spec(key)`: the spec a setting was defined with (its label, type, range, options), or undefined\n618:- `saves.any` †: is there any save to load (a title's Continue)?\n619:- `saves.autosave(o)` †: save to the autosave (what write() gives)\n620:- `saves.copy(from, to)` †: copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty\n621:- `saves.erase(slot)` †: erase a slot\n622:- `saves.get(slot)` †: a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer: true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, place, level, time, at (the date saved), version }\n623:- `saves.latest()` †: the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it)\n624:- `saves.list()` †: every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows)\n625:- `saves.load(slot)` †: load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot is empty, damaged or from a newer version\n626:- `saves.save(slot, o)` †: save to a slot (0.., or 'auto'): o ({ data, place, level }) or what write() gives. Returns true when it is kept (in storage, or for the visit when storage is blocked: blocked tells), false when there was nothing to save\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n628:- `saves.blocked = false` †: storage refused a save (they last for the visit)\n629:- `saves.canSave = true` †: the pause menu offers Save (a JRPG turns it off away from save points)\n630:- `saves.game` †: its game\n631:- `saves.migrate` †: an older version's data brought up to this one (or null: kept as it is)\n632:- `saves.played = 0` †: seconds played in the game's scenes (paused time and titles left out), saved with each save and set by a load\n633:- `saves.read` †: what a load does with { data, place, level, time, slot }\n634:- `saves.slots` †: how many slots besides the autosave (3)\n635:- `saves.version` †: the game's version of its data (1), saved with each save\n636:- `saves.write` †: what a save holds ({ data, place, level })\n1081:- `new E.Backdrop(o = {}) → backdrop`: new E.Backdrop('castle-night') (a preset: E.Backdrop.presets) or new E.Backdrop({ sky: [colors top to bottom], sun, moon, stars, layers: [{ kind: 'mountains' | 'hills' | 'forest' | 'city' | 'castle' | 'clouds' | 'sea' | 'fog' | 'stalactites', color, y, height, parallax, seed }] }): a parallax sky and scenery drawn behind a level. sun, moon: { x, y (0..1 of the screen), r, color }\n1102:- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or a View, as given (r.shape draws steep views from the characters' angle: E.charView(view) gives that); a bag icon is the item's shape seen at an angle. r.sprite stands it on its feet (foot: [x, y] in the sprite) unless an anchor is given\n1163:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n1164:- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font, titleFont)\n1165:- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n1167:- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n1168:- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\n1181:- `shell.show(name, spec = {})` †: open a screen: 'title' | 'pause' | 'settings' | 'help' | 'results' | 'map' or a name of your own, from spec over o.screens[name]. A spec: { kicker, title, text (strings or functions), actions: [[label, fn] or { label, fn, act, primary, disabled }], back (fn for cancel) }. From another screen it stacks (back() returns); shown again, it updates (the new spec over the old). 'settings' takes its items\n1182:- `shell.show('title')` †: { name, subtitle, meta: [...], footer }\n1183:- `shell.show('help')` †: { keys: [[key, what]], sections: [[heading, text]] }\n1184:- `shell.show('results')` †: { emblem, stats: [[value, label]], medals: [[label, earned]] }\n1185:- `shell.show('map')` †: { map, at, markers (a list or a function), labels: [[text, x, y]], onPick(x, y) }\n// A headless test of the template game: the engine and game.js run in Node with no screen (new E.Game is headless where\n// there is no DOM), driven by fixed steps (game.advance) and scripted input (input.tap, input.hold), and read through\n// game.debug.snapshot(). Run it: node game/test.mjs (exit code 1 on a failure). Write one like it for your game.\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n\nconst ctx = { console };\nvm.createContext(ctx);\nfor (const f of ['../my-3d2dge.js', './game.js']) vm.runInContext(readFileSync(new URL(f, import.meta.url), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: f });\nconst E = ctx.My3D2dge, game = E.current, I = game.input, snap = () => game.debug.snapshot();\nlet failed = 0;\nconst check = (what, ok, detail = '') => { console.log((ok ? 'ok   ' : 'FAIL ') + what + (ok ? '' : ': ' + detail)); if (!ok) failed++; };\n\ngame.advance(.5);\ncheck('the title waits for start', snap().scene === 'title', JSON.stringify(snap()));\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\ncheck('start begins play', snap().scene === 'play', JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// climb: stand facing the roof's west wall (cells 7-9 of rows 4-6: x 112-160, y 64-112), press jump to take hold, then\n// climb with up (up the screen is up the wall) until it pulls up onto the top\ngame.debug.teleport(100, 88, 0, 0);\nI.tap('jump'); game.advance(.1);\ncheck('jump next to a wall takes hold of it', snap().climbing, JSON.stringify(snap()));\nI.hold('up'); game.advance(.6); I.hold('up', false); game.advance(1);\ncheck('climbing up pulls up onto the roof', !snap().climbing && snap().hero[2] === 32, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// take the gem (on the roof's middle cell), then hop down into the street with it\ngame.debug.teleport(136, 88, 32, 0); game.advance(.1);\ncheck('walking onto the gem takes it', snap().got, JSON.stringify(snap()));\ngame.debug.teleport(156, 120, 32, Math.PI / 2); I.hold('down'); game.advance(1.5); I.hold('down', false); game.advance(.5);\ncheck('back in the street with the gem wins', snap().scene === 'end' && snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// get seen: stand in front of the guard, in the open, until its alert fills\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\nconst [gx, gy, gf] = snap().guard;\ngame.debug.teleport(gx + Math.cos(gf) * 40, gy + Math.sin(gf) * 40, 0, gf + Math.PI);\ngame.advance(2.5);\ncheck('the guard catches a hero it sees', snap().scene === 'end' && !snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\ncheck('no errors', !game.errors.length, game.errors.map(e => e.message).join(' | '));\n\nconsole.log(failed ? `${failed} check(s) failed` : 'all checks passed');\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QZ2b4LFMDM7yN8Hqo2ZqzW","permission_decision":{"de