{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi7gpQaXxBrDFJnUaKq9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now writing the real answers into about.json (the About screen and exit-interview.json share it), then the final build, full tests and harness."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":851,"cache_read_input_tokens":765809,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":851},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49428dbe-779b-4248-8ac3-c582018d3c3d","uuid":"8726af6f-7a02-4345-9b01-c43751087872","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:21:58.492Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi7gp3FPYmQmXLAwDBeH"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi7gpQaXxBrDFJnUaKq9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RtmNCcWz7ZgqpsJBCBFndk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S'; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='src/about.json'; a=json.load(open(p))\na['sourceInformation']['usage']=\"unknown: no token or cost figures are visible to me in this session; session time about 2 hours (07:06 to about 09:10 local, by the file timestamps)\"\na['sourceInformation']['testing']=\"Allowed: headless tests with game.advance and game.debug, a scripted playthrough of the whole game, one command that prints only failures and a count, and screenshots only for what a script can't check. Used: npm test (14 suites, about 940 checks, including the scripted story playthrough from the prologue to the credits, a 15-segment attract loop, and 2-4 player netcode on a fake hub with latency and loss), a Play Lab script for AI balance, Playwright screenshots and the engine's check tool, and the AI Hub harness in all 4 configurations (all pass)\"\na['testingFeedback']=[\n \"About 30. The headless suites caught 14 (a new match replaying the previous match's play calls, a crash on a kick play with no kicker on the field in a drill, the touch-only gate unlocking itself, the Big Heads cheat being reverted by its own lock, deep links that ran before the boot finished, storage missing headless, three commentary lines over 48 characters, three attract segments whose key moment didn't always happen, and the Seismic Sack's slam lost when the play ended first). Browser runs and screenshots caught about 16 (a black field from a wrong color conversion, three boot or update crashes, 12 fps from the field rebaking on every zoom change, glyphs drawn as '?', an overflowing menu, unknown input actions, audio layer warnings, linemen catching deflections, a stale ball spot, a dark night stadium). The Play Lab caught the balance problems (runs averaging 13 yards, passes sacked in 0.8 s, too many interceptions).\",\n \"About 8: the black field, three crashes (a constant used before it was defined, a clash with an engine-internal input field, a missing default argument), the stale play calls (they broke REMATCH, story retries and every scripted situation), the kick-play crash, 12 fps rendering, and the pass rush that sacked nearly every pass.\",\n \"The rules suite's set-situation runs: replaying scenarios back to back exposed that a new match kept the previous match's play calls, a bug that silently broke REMATCH and chapter retries. The scripted story playthrough (prologue, nine drills by their bots, four matches, halftime choices, the ending, the credits, a loss and RETRY) was the best broad net.\",\n \"My first spin-evasion test: as written it could never fail, so it proved nothing until I rewrote it to call the tackle directly inside and outside the spin's window. The engine check tool's cycling through iso, side and the other stock views also told me little, since the game uses its own broadcast view.\"]\na['engineFeedback']=[\n \"The HD Humanoid with the motion-capture runtime (a throw, a three-point stance or a breakdance on any rig in one line), and the exact fixed-step headless game.advance, which made a 940-check test suite, a Play Lab and a whole-game scripted playthrough run in about a minute without a browser. The free pause, settings, controls and save screens saved a lot of work.\",\n \"Yes: I assumed E.hex returned an integer (it returns [r, g, b]) and got a black field; I used input._used as my own flag and broke the engine's input; I didn't know each camera zoom value makes a new floor bake, so a smoothly zooming camera rebaked the whole field every frame; and I called game.go from a deep link before the browser boot steps finished.\",\n \"The football simulation itself: rules, downs, the clock, kicks, possession and scoring; 14 athletes with intents, collisions, blocking engagements and sheds; the AI brains (pass and run blocking, routes, QB reads, man and zone coverage, rush lanes, pursuit angles, ball-carrier steering with evasive moves) and the CPU coach. Second, the shared-world netcode adapter for the AI Hub.\",\n \"Performance and caching that the API doesn't show: the floor bake per view and zoom (with a cache of 6), and finding which internals the Shell and settings rely on. Also the very large API surface: the right helper usually existed, but finding it took grepping.\",\n \"E1 the PlayStation glyphs (and · ✓ ▲ ▼ ◂) in both pixel fonts, so prompts never draw '?'; E2 PlayStation symbols by default with Xbox as the option, shown on the Settings screen; E3 a gear hook in the HD Humanoid's draw for pads, numbers and the carried ball; E4 a football helmet hat style; E5 a per-letter voice function for E.Dialog; E6 named audio buses; E7 Dev settings kept off the Settings screen and settings rows on any Shell screen (the live tuning sliders); E8 opening Settings without pausing (AI Hub sessions); E10 a floor-bake cache of 16 instead of 6. Each is logged in ENGINE-CHANGES.md.\",\n \"Make TileMap floor bakes independent of zoom (bake at world resolution once and scale, or document loudly that every zoom level is a full rebake), and expose the pixel font's glyph bitmaps publicly so games can paint text into textures without reaching into E.font._glyph.\"]\na['promptFeedback']=[\n \"It is concrete about the deliverables and how they will be checked (the file name, the exit interview's exact shape, the hub harness), and its 10-foot, controller-first UX rules are specific enough to act on: device-following prompts, PlayStation glyphs with an Xbox option, no dense web screens, the touch-only gate.\",\n \"Two instructions pull against each other: TASK.md asks to pick the title with a real RNG while STAGE.md says to use the plan's title. And the plan's scope (6 teams, 5 stadiums, 5 story chapters, 9 drills, 16 attract segments, client-side prediction) is far more than one session at medium effort, so 'follow the plan' versus 'TASK.md wins' and 'no stubbed features' needed judgment about what to cut without leaving stubs.\",\n \"Making 7-on-7 AI play believable football (blocking that neither collapses nor walls off every run, coverage, pursuit, QB reads) and keeping it balanced, together with shared-world multiplayer that passes the harness. The machine itself was a factor: /tmp was full, which crashed headless Chromium until I pointed TMPDIR at my own folder.\",\n \"Give the expected scale (hours or a token budget) and let the plan mark must, should and could features, so cuts are deliberate. Say which of TASK.md and STAGE.md decides the title. Mention shared-machine limits such as a full /tmp.\"]\na['credits'].append([\"Built with\", \"Node 24.22.1, Playwright 1.63.0 (tests), Python 3 http.server (the hub harness)\"])\na['credits'].append([\"Scope notes\", \"Multiplayer in AI Hub sessions is host-authoritative: other copies render the host's snapshots, interpolated, without client-side prediction (the plan's own fallback), and a remote player's kicks are kicked automatically. The cutscene sets are the stadium, a locker room and a press room.\"])\njson.dump(a, open(p,'w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\nEOF\nnode build.mjs && node -e \"const j=JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('../exit-interview.json','utf8'));const si=j.sourceInformation;console.log(Object.keys(si).length,'fields',Object.values(si).every(v=>v&&v.length),j.testingFeedback.length,j.engineFeedback.length,j.promptFeedback.length,Object.keys(j.aiHub).length, Object.values(j.aiHub).filter(v=>v===''||v==null).length+' empty (series)')\"","description":"Write final answers, build, validate exit interview"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":851,"cache_read_input_tokens":765809,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":851},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49428dbe-779b-4248-8ac3-c582018d3c3d","uuid":"a0ec603d-4e37-4b0a-8996-cf97f759c9eb","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:22:25.555Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi7gp3FPYmQmXLAwDBeH","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RtmNCcWz7ZgqpsJBCBFndk":{"command":"date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S'; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='src/about.json'; a=json.load(open(p))\na['sourceInformation']['usage']=\"unknown: no token or cost figures are visible to me in this session; session time about 2 hours (07:06 to about 09:10 local, by the file timestamps)\"\na['sourceInformation']['testing']=\"Allowed: headless tests with game.advance and game.debug, a scripted playthrough of the whole game, one command that prints only failures and a count, and screenshots only for what a script can't check. Used: npm test (14 suites, about 940 checks, including the scripted story playthrough from the prologue to the credits, a 15-segment attract loop, and 2-4 player netcode on a fake hub with latency and loss), a Play Lab script for AI balance, Playwright screenshots and the engine's check tool, and the AI Hub harness in all 4 configurations (all pass)\"\na['testingFeedback']=[\n \"About 30. The headless suites caught 14 (a new match replaying the previous match's play calls, a crash on a kick play with no kicker on the field in a drill, the touch-only gate unlocking itself, the Big Heads cheat being reverted by its own lock, deep links that ran before the boot finished, storage missing headless, three commentary lines over 48 characters, three attract segments whose key moment didn't always happen, and the Seismic Sack's slam lost when the play ended first). Browser runs and screenshots caught about 16 (a black field from a wrong color conversion, three boot or update crashes, 12 fps from the field rebaking on every zoom change, glyphs drawn as '?', an overflowing menu, unknown input actions, audio layer warnings, linemen catching deflections, a stale ball spot, a dark night stadium). The Play Lab caught the balance problems (runs averaging 13 yards, passes sacked in 0.8 s, too many interceptions).\",\n \"About 8: the black field, three crashes (a constant used before it was defined, a clash with an engine-internal input field, a missing default argument), the stale play calls (they broke REMATCH, story retries and every scripted situation), the kick-play crash, 12 fps rendering, and the pass rush that sacked nearly every pass.\",\n \"The rules suite's set-situation runs: replaying scenarios back to back exposed that a new match kept the previous match's play calls, a bug that silently broke REMATCH and chapter retries. The scripted story playthrough (prologue, nine drills by their bots, four matches, halftime choices, the ending, the credits, a loss and RETRY) was the best broad net.\",\n \"My first spin-evasion test: as written it could never fail, so it proved nothing until I rewrote it to call the tackle directly inside and outside the spin's window. The engine check tool's cycling through iso, side and the other stock views also told me little, since the game uses its own broadcast view.\"]\na['engineFeedback']=[\n \"The HD Humanoid with the motion-capture runtime (a throw, a three-point stance or a breakdance on any rig in one line), and the exact fixed-step headless game.advance, which made a 940-check test suite, a Play Lab and a whole-game scripted playthrough run in about a minute without a browser. The free pause, settings, controls and save screens saved a lot of work.\",\n \"Yes: I assumed E.hex returned an integer (it returns [r, g, b]) and got a black field; I used input._used as my own flag and broke the engine's input; I didn't know each camera zoom value makes a new floor bake, so a smoothly zooming camera rebaked the whole field every frame; and I called game.go from a deep link before the browser boot steps finished.\",\n \"The football simulation itself: rules, downs, the clock, kicks, possession and scoring; 14 athletes with intents, collisions, blocking engagements and sheds; the AI brains (pass and run blocking, routes, QB reads, man and zone coverage, rush lanes, pursuit angles, ball-carrier steering with evasive moves) and the CPU coach. Second, the shared-world netcode adapter for the AI Hub.\",\n \"Performance and caching that the API doesn't show: the floor bake per view and zoom (with a cache of 6), and finding which internals the Shell and settings rely on. Also the very large API surface: the right helper usually existed, but finding it took grepping.\",\n \"E1 the PlayStation glyphs (and · ✓ ▲ ▼ ◂) in both pixel fonts, so prompts never draw '?'; E2 PlayStation symbols by default with Xbox as the option, shown on the Settings screen; E3 a gear hook in the HD Humanoid's draw for pads, numbers and the carried ball; E4 a football helmet hat style; E5 a per-letter voice function for E.Dialog; E6 named audio buses; E7 Dev settings kept off the Settings screen and settings rows on any Shell screen (the live tuning sliders); E8 opening Settings without pausing (AI Hub sessions); E10 a floor-bake cache of 16 instead of 6. Each is logged in ENGINE-CHANGES.md.\",\n \"Make TileMap floor bakes independent of zoom (bake at world resolution once and scale, or document loudly that every zoom level is a full rebake), and expose the pixel font's glyph bitmaps publicly so games can paint text into textures without reaching into E.font._glyph.\"]\na['promptFeedback']=[\n \"It is concrete about the deliverables and how they will be checked (the file name, the exit interview's exact shape, the hub harness), and its 10-foot, controller-first UX rules are specific enough to act on: device-following prompts, PlayStation glyphs with an Xbox option, no dense web screens, the touch-only gate.\",\n \"Two instructions pull against each other: TASK.md asks to pick the title with a real RNG while STAGE.md says to use the plan's title. And the plan's scope (6 teams, 5 stadiums, 5 story chapters, 9 drills, 16 attract segments, client-side prediction) is far more than one session at medium effort, so 'follow the plan' versus 'TASK.md wins' and 'no stubbed features' needed judgment about what to cut without leaving stubs.\",\n \"Making 7-on-7 AI play believable football (blocking that neither collapses nor walls off every run, coverage, pursuit, QB reads) and keeping it balanced, together with shared-world multiplayer that passes the harness. The machine itself was a factor: /tmp was full, which crashed headless Chromium until I pointed TMPDIR at my own folder.\",\n \"Give the expected scale (hours or a token budget) and let the plan mark must, should and could features, so cuts are deliberate. Say which of TASK.md and STAGE.md decides the title. Mention shared-machine limits such as a full /tmp.\"]\na['credits'].append([\"Built with\", \"Node 24.22.1, Playwright 1.63.0 (tests), Python 3 http.server (the hub harness)\"])\na['credits'].append([\"Scope notes\", \"Multiplayer in AI Hub sessions is host-authoritative: other copies render the host's snapshots, interpolated, without client-side prediction (the plan's own fallback), and a remote player's kicks are kicked automatically. The cutscene sets are the stadium, a locker room and a press room.\"])\njson.dump(a, open(p,'w'), indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\nEOF\nnode build.mjs && node -e \"const j=JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('../exit-interview.json','utf8'));const si=j.sourceInformation;console.log(Object.keys(si).length,'fields',Object.values(si).every(v=>v&&v.length),j.testingFeedback.length,j.engineFeedback.length,j.promptFeedback.length,Object.keys(j.aiHub).length, Object.values(j.aiHub).filter(v=>v===''||v==null).length+' empty (series)')\"","description":"Write final answers, build, validate exit interview"}}}
