{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi9pmYeE4EoYzQCdXkzj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I took the remaining points from the stop hook, and **HAMERICAN FOOTBALL** is done. All 942 tests pass and the AI Hub harness passes 4 of 4 on the final file, `HamericanFootball-AmericanFootball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-070556.html`. `exit-interview.json` parses and answers every field.\n\nWhat I changed this round:\n- **Office cutscene set:** Mama Pearl's Pickle Barn (pickle barrels, the 1974 team photo, a PICKLES sign, a desk and a lamp) now hosts the chapter 1 outro. Checked in a browser screenshot.\n- **Marching band:** eight bandsmen in the home colors, with drums and horns, march across midfield during the halftime show. Checked in a browser screenshot.\n- **Balance re-measured on the final code:** all 17 offensive plays against 8 defenses at the plan's own sample size (n = 30) are inside the plan's bands. The log is in `shots/bands-n30.txt`.\n- **Exact issue counts:** I replaced my earlier estimates with an itemized list of the 40 game issues fixed this session. The full list is in Testing Feedback below and on the About screen.\n- **Not optimized: 1080p frame rate.** It's 22–30 fps measured in headless Chromium on this heavily shared machine (45–60 at 720p). TASK.md puts frame-rate targets out of scope (\"handled later\"), so I left it.\n- **Earlier this session:** the chain gang, client-side prediction and the online kick meter went in during the previous round. All three are in this build and have tests.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 07:05:56\n- **Source:** American football (over the top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (the title was redrawn with a real RNG, per TASK.md: Hamerican Football)\n- **Genre and Perspective:** arcade sports (7-on-7 American football) with beat-'em-up hits and a story campaign. The camera is a sideline broadcast view (custom 50°), with Sky Cam and Blimp options, a Kick Cam behind the kicker, and field-level, isometric and reverse replay angles.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff (modified), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, the mocap runtime with an 18-clip set, Canvas 2D and Web Audio. Tests use Node 24.22.1 and Playwright 1.63.0.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native style: HD Humanoid pixel-art rigs at PS1 resolution, code-painted fields, stands and crowds, five lit stadiums with weather. New helmets, pads, numbers, logos, card art, four cutscene sets and a marching band.\n- **Animation:** the engine's procedural rigs and E.MOVES, joint post-processing (tilt, roll, lift), and 18 motion-capture clips (Quaternius, Mesh2Motion, CMU).\n- **Audio:** all in code: 11 original songs with layers and stings, 50 sound effects, a crowd bed with chants, and an Animalese/Simlish babble voice synth.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1–4 players. The host runs the world and sends snapshots at 14 Hz. Each client predicts its own player and runs its own play-call screen and kick meter. Local 1–4 players also work on one machine.\n- **Testing:**\n  - *Allowed:* headless tests with `game.advance` and `game.debug`, a scripted whole-game playthrough, one command that prints only failures and a count, and screenshots only for what a script can't check.\n  - *Used:* `npm test` (14 suites, 942 checks, including the story playthrough from the prologue to the credits, the attract loop, and 2–4 player netcode with latency and loss).\n  - *Also used:* the plan's Play Lab bands at n = 30 (all 17 plays inside), Playwright screenshots, the engine's check tool, and the AI Hub harness (4 of 4 pass).\n- **Research:** none beyond the engine and AI Hub documentation.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown. No token or cost figures are visible to me. The session ran about 1 h 45 min (07:06 to about 08:50).\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** 40, each fixed:\n   - **Headless suites (15):**\n     - a new match replayed the previous match's play calls;\n     - a kick play with no kicker on the field crashed;\n     - the touch-only gate unlocked itself;\n     - the Big Heads cheat was reverted by its own lock;\n     - deep links ran before the boot finished;\n     - storage was missing in Node;\n     - 3 commentary lines ran over 48 characters;\n     - 5 attract segments missed their key moment;\n     - the Seismic Sack's slam was lost when the play ended first.\n   - **Browser runs and screenshots (16):**\n     - 3 crashes and a syntax error that stopped the page loading;\n     - the field drew black;\n     - 12 fps, because the field rebaked on every zoom change;\n     - the input map wasn't applied at start;\n     - audio layer warnings;\n     - scene changes before the boot finished;\n     - glyphs drawn as \"?\";\n     - an overflowing menu;\n     - a wrong device label in setup;\n     - a stale ball spot before the snap;\n     - linemen catching deflections;\n     - a night stadium too dark to read;\n     - an overlapping PRESS START.\n   - **Play Lab and the plan's bands (9):**\n     - blocked defenders couldn't tackle, so runs averaged 13 yards;\n     - a pass rush that sacked in 0.8 s;\n     - too many interceptions;\n     - 77 late hits a game;\n     - blocks that never broke off;\n     - defenders diving at where the runner was;\n     - receivers blocking as well as linemen;\n     - the QB sneak's path was never wired;\n     - the pitch plays sat outside the run band.\n2. **How many were critical or game-breaking?** 9: the boot crash, the input crash, the update crash, the syntax error, the black field, the stale play calls, the kick-play crash, 12 fps, and the 0.8 s pass rush.\n3. **Most helpful test:** the rules suite's back-to-back scenario runs, which exposed the stale play calls. The scripted story playthrough was the best broad net.\n4. **Least helpful test:** my first spin test, which could never fail as written; I rewrote it. The check tool's stock camera views told me little, since the game uses its own broadcast view.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** the HD Humanoid with mocap, and exact headless `game.advance`. The whole suite and a full playthrough run in about a minute.\n2. **Did I get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n   - `E.hex` returns `[r, g, b]`, not an integer.\n   - `input._used` is an engine internal, and using it broke input.\n   - Every zoom level is a full floor rebake.\n   - Calling `game.go` before the browser boot finished caused warnings.\n3. **The most important thing I built myself:** the football simulation and its AI for 14 athletes and the coach, then the shared-world netcode with prediction.\n4. **The hardest part:** hidden caches (floor bakes per view and zoom) and a very large API.\n5. **What I changed in the engine, and why:**\n\n   | # | Change | Why |\n   |---|---|---|\n   | E1 | Glyphs added to both pixel fonts | PlayStation symbols drew as \"?\" |\n   | E2 | PlayStation/Xbox button symbols on Settings | TASK.md asks for PS glyphs with an Xbox option |\n   | E3 | A gear hook in the HD Humanoid's draw | Pads, numbers and the carried ball inside the rig |\n   | E4 | A football helmet hat style | A helmet that reads as football |\n   | E5 | A per-letter dialog voice | The Animalese voices |\n   | E6 | Named audio buses | Separate voice and crowd volumes |\n   | E7 | Dev settings rows on any Shell screen | Dev mode's live tuning sliders |\n   | E8 | Settings without pausing | AI Hub sessions must not freeze |\n   | E10 | A floor-bake cache of 16 instead of 6 | The field was rebaking every frame |\n\n   The details are in `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`.\n6. **One thing I'd change:** zoom-independent floor bakes, and public access to the pixel font's glyph bitmaps.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** concrete deliverables and checks, and specific 10-foot, controller-first UX rules.\n2. **What was confusing:** TASK.md wants an RNG-picked title while STAGE.md says to use the plan's. The plan's scope also far exceeds one medium-effort session, which conflicts with \"no stubs\".\n3. **The hardest thing to do:** believable, balanced 7-on-7 AI, and multiplayer that passes the harness. A full shared `/tmp` crashed Chromium until I moved its temp folder.\n4. **What I'd change:** state a time or token budget, mark the plan's features must/should/could, say which file decides the title, and note shared-machine limits."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":212,"cache_read_input_tokens":839951,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":212},"output_tokens":779,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49428dbe-779b-4248-8ac3-c582018d3c3d","uuid":"0719ef7d-2bf3-4ccd-ab37-7e1508fb5447","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:50:21.032Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi9pm966f4GGfEwk185V"}
