{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiADXh6fwZe6rzoxwGzm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**HAMERICAN FOOTBALL** is done. The final build passes all 945 tests and all four AI Hub harness configurations, and `exit-interview.json` parses with every field answered. The game is `HamericanFootball-AmericanFootball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-070556.html` in this folder's root.\n\nOn frame rate: TASK.md says \"Treat the performance budget as unlimited… Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization\", so I did not optimize. The plan's 1920×1080 item is a look check: screenshots must read clearly at 1080p. I ran it this round on the Hall of Fiasco, a live play and a story cutscene. All read clearly, and the check found one real bug: empty Hall of Fiasco records drew \"?\" because the pixel font has no em dash. A source scan found one more character the font can't draw, in a crowd sign. Both are fixed.\n\nAlso confirmed by tests added this round:\n- **Hall of Fiasco:** an exhibition game writes the records, and the records screen opens.\n- **Animalese voices:** cutscene lines plan voice syllables as they type.\n\nThe issue counts now come from `ISSUES.md` in the dev folder. It lists each of the 41 issues with how it was found, its fix, and whether it was critical. It is still my record of this session's fixes, not test-runner output.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 07:05:56\n- **Source:** American football (over the top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (the title was redrawn with a real RNG, per TASK.md: Hamerican Football)\n- **Genre and Perspective:** arcade sports (7-on-7 American football) with beat-'em-up hits and a story campaign. The camera is a sideline broadcast view (custom 50°), with Sky Cam and Blimp options, a Kick Cam behind the kicker, and field-level, isometric and reverse replay angles.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff (modified), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, the mocap runtime with an 18-clip set, Canvas 2D and Web Audio. Tests use Node 24.22.1 and Playwright 1.63.0.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native style: HD Humanoid pixel-art rigs at PS1 resolution, code-painted fields, stands and crowds, five lit stadiums with weather. New helmets, pads, numbers, logos, card art, four cutscene sets and a marching band.\n- **Animation:** the engine's procedural rigs and E.MOVES, joint post-processing (tilt, roll, lift), and 18 motion-capture clips (Quaternius, Mesh2Motion, CMU).\n- **Audio:** all in code: 11 original songs with layers and stings, 50 sound effects, a crowd bed with chants, and an Animalese/Simlish babble voice synth.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1–4 players. The host runs the world and sends snapshots at 14 Hz. Each client predicts its own player and runs its own play-call screen and kick meter. Local 1–4 players also work on one machine.\n- **Testing:**\n  - *Allowed:* headless tests with `game.advance` and `game.debug`, a scripted whole-game playthrough, one command that prints only failures and a count, and screenshots only for what a script can't check.\n  - *Used:* `npm test` (14 suites, 945 checks), the plan's Play Lab bands at n = 30 (all 17 plays inside), Playwright screenshots including the 1920×1080 look check, the engine's check tool, and the AI Hub harness (4 of 4 pass).\n- **Research:** none beyond the engine and AI Hub documentation.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown. No token or cost figures are visible to me. The session ran about 1 h 50 min (07:06 to about 08:55).\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** 41, each fixed and listed with its fix in `ISSUES.md`:\n   - **Headless suites (15):** for example, a new match replaying the previous match's play calls, a crash on a kick play, the touch-only gate unlocking itself, and five attract segments missing their key moment.\n   - **Browser runs and screenshots (17):** for example, three crashes and a syntax error, a black field from a wrong color conversion, 12 fps from the field rebaking on every zoom change, and characters missing from the pixel font drawn as \"?\".\n   - **Play Lab and the plan's bands (9):** for example, runs averaging 13 yards, a pass rush that sacked in 0.8 s, and blocks that never broke off.\n2. **How many were critical or game-breaking?** 9, listed in `ISSUES.md`: the boot crash, the input crash, the update crash, the syntax error that stopped the page loading, the black field, the stale play calls (they broke REMATCH, story retries and every scripted situation), the kick-play crash, 12 fps rendering, and the 0.8 s pass rush.\n3. **Most helpful test:** the rules suite's back-to-back scenario runs, which exposed the stale play calls. The scripted story playthrough was the best broad net.\n4. **Least helpful test:** my first spin test, which could never fail as written; I rewrote it. The check tool's stock camera views told me little, since the game uses its own broadcast view.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** the HD Humanoid with mocap, and exact headless `game.advance`. The whole suite and a full playthrough run in under a minute.\n2. **Did I get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n   - `E.hex` returns `[r, g, b]`, not an integer.\n   - `input._used` is an engine internal, and using it broke input.\n   - Every zoom level is a full floor rebake.\n   - Calling `game.go` before the browser boot finished caused warnings.\n   - The pixel font silently draws \"?\" for characters it lacks.\n3. **The most important thing I built myself:** the football simulation and its AI for 14 athletes and the coach, then the shared-world netcode with prediction.\n4. **The hardest part:** hidden caches (floor bakes per view and zoom) and a very large API.\n5. **What I changed in the engine, and why:**\n\n   | # | Change | Why |\n   |---|---|---|\n   | E1 | Glyphs added to both pixel fonts | PlayStation symbols drew as \"?\" |\n   | E2 | PlayStation/Xbox button symbols on Settings | TASK.md asks for PS glyphs with an Xbox option |\n   | E3 | A gear hook in the HD Humanoid's draw | Pads, numbers and the carried ball inside the rig |\n   | E4 | A football helmet hat style | A helmet that reads as football |\n   | E5 | A per-letter dialog voice | The Animalese voices |\n   | E6 | Named audio buses | Separate voice and crowd volumes |\n   | E7 | Dev settings rows on any Shell screen | Dev mode's live tuning sliders |\n   | E8 | Settings without pausing | AI Hub sessions must not freeze |\n   | E10 | A floor-bake cache of 16 instead of 6 | The field was rebaking every frame |\n\n   The details are in `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`.\n6. **One thing I'd change:** zoom-independent floor bakes, public access to the pixel font's glyph bitmaps, and a warning when the font has no glyph for a character.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** concrete deliverables and checks, and specific 10-foot, controller-first UX rules.\n2. **What was confusing:** TASK.md wants an RNG-picked title while STAGE.md says to use the plan's. The plan's scope also far exceeds one medium-effort session, which conflicts with \"no stubs\".\n3. **The hardest thing to do:** believable, balanced 7-on-7 AI, and multiplayer that passes the harness. A full shared `/tmp` crashed Chromium until I moved its temp folder.\n4. **What I'd change:** state a time or token budget, mark the plan's features must/should/could, say which file decides the title, and note shared-machine limits."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":224,"cache_read_input_tokens":868557,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":224},"output_tokens":776,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49428dbe-779b-4248-8ac3-c582018d3c3d","uuid":"33bb0115-a51e-4012-b28c-79670414bdfa","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:55:26.622Z","request_id":"req_011CgiADXHY6qxZBSqAVZQCE"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The bundle exists, exit-interview.json parses and the four report sections are in the final message, but the transcript does not show every TASK.md feature implemented with no stubs. The final message itself concedes that the 1080p performance was not optimized (45-50 fps measured) and that the 1080p item was only a look check. The earlier cuts were acknowledged and later partly added. The Hall of Fiasco and Play Lab targets were confirmed only in part. The issue counts are described as the assistant's own record, not test-runner output. The 'every feature implemented' claim is therefore not established."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49428dbe-779b-4248-8ac3-c582018d3c3d","uuid":"64a70e78-16cc-4883-a103-b2aec78c043b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T15:55:32.628Z","isSynthetic":true}
