{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiAjnApWbjjQGF6AFAJz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**HAMERICAN FOOTBALL** is finished: `HamericanFootball-AmericanFootball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-070556.html` in this folder's root. All 982 tests pass, the AI Hub harness passes all four configurations on the final file, and `exit-interview.json` parses with every field answered.\n\nWhat changed this round:\n- **Balance:** I reran the plan's Play Lab bands on the final code at n = 30 (every offensive play against 8 defenses). All 17 plays are inside; the log is `shots/bands-n30-final.txt`.\n- **Hall of Fiasco:** tests now check that the recorded values match the game's own stats and that the attract mode never writes records. That found a real bug: games whose local side was played by the CPU (the Dev \"CPU vs CPU\" cheat) weren't recorded. It's fixed and logged as issue 42 in `ISSUES.md`.\n- **Animalese voices:** tests now check one syllable per typed vowel, one per vowel group with onsets taken from the letters, a rising pitch on questions, and Simlish lines that are gibberish and louder in caps. Headless, this checks the plan the synth would schedule, not the sound itself.\n- **Dev sliders:** a test checks that changing a slider changes play (raising speedBase raises every top speed) and that reset restores the defaults.\n- **Frame rate:** TASK.md says \"Out of scope (handled later): FPS targets, optimization\", so I did not optimize. On an idle machine it measured 45–60 fps at 720p and 45–50 fps at 1080p.\n- **Issue counts:** they come from `ISSUES.md`, my itemized session log, not from test-runner output.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 07:05:56\n- **Source:** American football (over the top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (the title was redrawn with a real RNG, per TASK.md: Hamerican Football)\n- **Genre and Perspective:** arcade sports (7-on-7 American football) with beat-'em-up hits and a story campaign. The camera is a sideline broadcast view (custom 50°), with Sky Cam and Blimp options, a Kick Cam behind the kicker, and field-level, isometric and reverse replay angles.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff (modified), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, the mocap runtime with an 18-clip set, Canvas 2D and Web Audio. Tests use Node 24.22.1 and Playwright 1.63.0.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native style: HD Humanoid pixel-art rigs at PS1 resolution, code-painted fields, stands and crowds, five lit stadiums with weather. New helmets, pads, numbers, logos, card art, four cutscene sets and a marching band.\n- **Animation:** the engine's procedural rigs and E.MOVES, joint post-processing (tilt, roll, lift), and 18 motion-capture clips (Quaternius, Mesh2Motion, CMU).\n- **Audio:** all in code: 11 original songs with layers and stings, 50 sound effects, a crowd bed with chants, and an Animalese/Simlish babble voice synth.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1–4 players. The host runs the world and sends snapshots at 14 Hz. Each client predicts its own player and runs its own play-call screen and kick meter. Local 1–4 players also work on one machine.\n- **Testing:**\n  - *Allowed:* headless tests with `game.advance` and `game.debug`, a scripted whole-game playthrough, one command that prints only failures and a count, and screenshots only for what a script can't check.\n  - *Used:* `npm test` (15 suites, 982 checks, including the TASK.md requirements suite).\n  - *Also used:* the plan's bands at n = 30 (all 17 plays inside), Playwright screenshots including the 1080p look check, the engine's check tool, and the AI Hub harness (4 of 4 pass).\n- **Research:** none beyond the engine and AI Hub documentation.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown. No token or cost figures are visible to me. The session ran about 1 h 55 min (07:06 to about 09:01).\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** 42, each fixed and listed with its fix in `ISSUES.md`:\n   - **Headless suites (15):** for example, a new match replaying the previous match's play calls, a crash on a kick play, and the touch-only gate unlocking itself.\n   - **Browser runs and screenshots (17):** for example, three crashes and a syntax error, a black field, 12 fps from field rebakes, and characters the pixel font lacks drawn as \"?\".\n   - **Play Lab and the plan's bands (9):** for example, runs averaging 13 yards, a 0.8 s pass rush, and blocks that never broke off.\n   - **Behavioural records test (1):** the Hall of Fiasco skipped games whose local side was CPU-driven.\n2. **How many were critical or game-breaking?** 9:\n   - the boot crash, the input crash and the update crash;\n   - the syntax error that stopped the page loading;\n   - the black field;\n   - the stale play calls;\n   - the kick-play crash;\n   - 12 fps rendering;\n   - the 0.8 s pass rush.\n3. **Most helpful test:** the rules suite's back-to-back scenario runs, which exposed the stale play calls. The scripted story playthrough was the best broad net.\n4. **Least helpful test:** my first spin test, which could never fail until I rewrote it, and the check tool's stock camera views.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** the HD Humanoid with mocap, and exact headless `game.advance`. The whole suite and a full playthrough run in under a minute.\n2. **Did I get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes:\n   - `E.hex` returns `[r, g, b]`, not an integer.\n   - `input._used` is an engine internal, and using it broke input.\n   - Every zoom level is a full floor rebake.\n   - Calling `game.go` before the browser boot finished caused warnings.\n   - The pixel font silently draws \"?\" for characters it lacks.\n3. **The most important thing I built myself:** the football simulation and its AI for 14 athletes and the coach, then the shared-world netcode with prediction.\n4. **The hardest part:** hidden caches (floor bakes per view and zoom) and a very large API.\n5. **What I changed in the engine, and why:**\n\n   | # | Change | Why |\n   |---|---|---|\n   | E1 | Glyphs added to both pixel fonts | PlayStation symbols drew as \"?\" |\n   | E2 | PlayStation/Xbox button symbols on Settings | TASK.md asks for PS glyphs with an Xbox option |\n   | E3 | A gear hook in the HD Humanoid's draw | Pads, numbers and the carried ball inside the rig |\n   | E4 | A football helmet hat style | A helmet that reads as football |\n   | E5 | A per-letter dialog voice | The Animalese voices |\n   | E6 | Named audio buses | Separate voice and crowd volumes |\n   | E7 | Dev settings rows on any Shell screen | Dev mode's live tuning sliders |\n   | E8 | Settings without pausing | AI Hub sessions must not freeze |\n   | E10 | A floor-bake cache of 16 instead of 6 | The field was rebaking every frame |\n\n   The details are in `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`.\n6. **One thing I'd change:** zoom-independent floor bakes, public access to the font's glyph bitmaps, and a warning when the font has no glyph for a character.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What I liked most:** concrete deliverables and checks, and specific 10-foot, controller-first UX rules.\n2. **What was confusing:** TASK.md wants an RNG-picked title, while STAGE.md says to use the plan's. The plan's scope also far exceeds one medium-effort session, which conflicts with \"no stubs\".\n3. **The hardest thing to do:** believable, balanced 7-on-7 AI, and multiplayer that passes the harness. A full shared `/tmp` crashed Chromium until I moved its temp folder.\n4. **What I'd change:** state a time or token budget, mark the plan's features must/should/could, say which file decides the title, and note shared-machine limits."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":775,"cache_read_input_tokens":885822,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":775},"output_tokens":763,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49428dbe-779b-4248-8ac3-c582018d3c3d","uuid":"83c58772-ba3e-4bb6-8123-50b18aeb51e4","timestamp":"2026-11-04T16:02:17.537Z","request_id":"req_011CgiAjmPwf29DYw3DCkuWT"}
